hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1201","1281 - And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi at al-Harbiyyah informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Ubayy ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever reaches his parents or one of them, then enters the Fire after that, may Allah cast him far and crush him. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Hajjaj, from Shubah, from Qatadah who said: I heard Zurarah ibn Awfa narrating from Ubayy ibn Malik. And he narrated it from Bahz, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from a man of his people called Ubayy ibn Malik: that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned it."
"1202","1282 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us by reading to him while we listened at Isfahan - it was said to him: Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed you by reading to him while you were present - it was said to him: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed you: Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, Faraj ibn Said ibn Alqamah ibn Said ibn Abyad ibn Hammal al-Muradi al-Sabai narrated to us, he said: My uncle Thabit ibn Said narrated to me, from his father Said ibn Abyad ibn Hammal, from his father Abyad ibn Hammal: that he requested the salt from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which is called the salt of Marib, and he granted it to him. Then al-Aqra ibn Habis al-Tamimi said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to the salt in Jahiliyyah; it is a land with no water; whoever comes to it takes from it, and it is like ever-flowing water. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Abyad ibn Hammal to return his grant of the salt. Abyad said: I return it to you on condition that it is charity from me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is charity from you, and it is like ever-flowing water; whoever comes to it takes from it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him land and pasture at al-Jurf, the Jurf of Murad, when he returned it to him."
"1203","1283 - And Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh informed us by reading to him while we listened at Isfahan; it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed you by reading to her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, Faraj ibn Said ibn Alqamah ibn Said ibn Abyad ibn Hammal narrated to us, that he requested the salt from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which is called Shadha at Marib, and he granted it to him. Then al-Aqra ibn Habis al-Tamimi said: O Prophet of Allah, I have come to the salt in Jahiliyyah and it is in a land; whoever comes to it takes from it, and it is like ever-flowing water. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Abyad ibn Hammal to return his grant. Abyad said: I return it on condition that he make it charity from me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is charity from you and it is like ever-flowing water; whoever comes to it takes from it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him land and herbage at al-Jurf, the Jurf of Murad, in its place when he returned it to him. He asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about reserving the arak trees, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no reservation in arak. He said: An arak tree in my enclosure. He said: There is no reservation in arak. Faraj said: Abyad meant by in my enclosure the land in which crops are, enclosed. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abi Umar similar to it. And Abu Dawud narrated from it: There is no reservation in arak, from Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Qurashi, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr al-Humaydi, from Faraj."
"1204","1284 - With this chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Qays ibn Hafs al-Darimi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Qays al-Maribi narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Thumamah ibn Sharahil, from Shumayr ibn Abd al-Madan, from Abyad ibn Hammal, that he came as a delegate to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he granted him the salt. When he turned away, a man said: O Messenger of Allah, do you know what you granted him? You only granted him ever-flowing water. So he took it back. He asked him about what may be reserved of the arak? He said: What the hooves of camels do not reach. Abu Dawud narrated it from Qutaybah and Muhammad ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Asqalani. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar, all from Muhammad ibn Yahya similar to it. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Khalifah. It has been narrated with an additional man in its chain."
"1205","1285 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Surayj ibn Yunus Abu al-Harith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Qays al-Maribi narrated to us, from his father, from Thumamah ibn Sharahil, from Sumayy ibn Qays, from Shumayr, from Abyad ibn Hammal: that he came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and requested the salt, and he granted it to him. When he turned away, a man said: O Messenger of Allah, do you know what you granted him? You only granted him ever-flowing water. So he called him and took it back from him. Abyad said: I asked him what may be reserved of the arak? He said: What the hooves of camels do not reach."
"1206","1286 - And Asad ibn Said at Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr al-Tannuri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Qays al-Maribi narrated to us, from his father, from Sumayy ibn Qays, from Thumamah ibn Sharahil, from Shumayr, from Abyad ibn Hammal: that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) requesting the salt, and he granted it to him. A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you know what you granted him? Ever-flowing water; take it back from him. And I asked him: What may be reserved of the arak? He said: What the hooves of camels do not reach. So he added in its chain Sumayy ibn Qays."
"1207","1287 - Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Rawh informed us by reading to him while we listened - it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed you by reading to her while they listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Faraj ibn Said narrated to us: my uncle Thabit ibn Said narrated to me, from his father Said, from Abyad ibn Hammal, that he had hazarah on his face - meaning ringworm - and his nose was affected. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and wiped over his face, and he did not reach evening that day with any trace in it."
"1208","1288 - Asad informed us, that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Faraj ibn Said ibn Alqamah ibn Said ibn Abyad ibn Hammal al-Maribi al-Sabai narrated to us: my uncle Thabit ibn Said ibn Abyad ibn Hammal narrated to me, that Said ibn Abyad ibn Hammal narrated to him, from his father Abyad ibn Hammal: that he spoke to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about charity when he came to him at Madinah as a delegate. He said: O brother of Saba, charity is unavoidable. He said: We only planted cotton, O Messenger of Allah; Saba has dispersed and none remains of them but a few at Marib. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a settlement with Abyad ibn Hammal for seventy garments of the finest value of the cloth of al-Maafir every year from those remaining of Saba at Marib. They continued to pay it until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Qurashi and Harun ibn Abd Allah al-Hammal, from Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr al-Humaydi, from Faraj."
"1209","1289 - Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh at Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Sad narrated to us, my uncle narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Labid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Ibrahim ibn Khallad ibn Suwayd al-Khazraji - brother of Balharith ibn al-Khazraj - who said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, be loud in crying out and abundant in shedding blood of sacrifice. Waki narrated it from Sufyan, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Labid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Khallad ibn al-Saib, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Jibril came to me and said to me: O Muhammad, command your companions to raise their voices with talbiyah, for it is of the rites of Hajj. Malik ibn Anas and Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Khallad ibn al-Saib al-Ansari, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Jibril came to me and commanded me to command my companions and those with me to raise their voices with talbiyah... the hadith. As for the hadith of Zayd ibn Khalid, Ibn Majah narrated it in his Sunan. As for the hadith of al-Saib, Abu Dawud narrated it from the hadith of Malik. Al-Tirmidhi, al-Nasai and Ibn Majah narrated it from the hadith of Ibn Uyaynah. Al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan sahih hadith. Muhammad ibn Ishaq cannot rival the precision of Sufyan al-Thawri, and I do not know whether companionship is established for Ibrahim ibn Khallad or not, and Allah knows best."
"1210","1290 - Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harbi informed us by my reading to him on the western side of Baghdad - I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you by reading to him while you listened: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from al-Hasan: Ahmar, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to us, he said: We used to feel pity for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of how he kept his hands away from his sides when he prostrated. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Affan, from Abbad ibn Rashid: al-Hasan narrated to us: Ahmar, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me."
"1211","1291 - And Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us. 1292 - Sulayman said: And Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malti narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us. 1293 - Sulayman said: And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Muhammad al-Sirini narrated to us, they said: Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from al-Hasan: Ahmar ibn Jaz, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to us, he said: We used to feel pity for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of how he kept his hand away from his sides when he prostrated."
"1212","1294 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik the litterateur informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abu Musa narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan saying: Ahmar, the companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to us, he said: We used to feel pity for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of how he kept his elbows away from his sides when he prostrated. Abbad ibn Rashid: al-Nasai said: Not strong. Ibn Hibban said: He is not used as proof. Al-Bukhari narrated for him in his Sahih, and he knows better than those who spoke about him, and Allah knows best. Bakkar ibn Muhammad has been spoken about; reliance in this chain is not upon his narration. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muslim ibn Ibrahim. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Waki, both from Abbad. Al-Daraqutni said: Al-Bukhari narrated from al-Hasan, from Amr ibn Taghlib, and none but al-Hasan narrated from him; he is obliged to bring out the hadith of al-Hasan from Ahmar ibn Jaz - We used to feel pity for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) because of how he kept apart - from the hadith of Abbad ibn Rashid, from al-Hasan, from Ahmar, because he narrated from Abbad ibn Rashid, from al-Hasan, from Maqil: that his sister was divorced."
"1213","1295 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said al-Asbahani narrated to us. 1296 - Sulayman said: And al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us. 1297 - He said: And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. 1298 - He said: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi and Said ibn Mansur and Mualla ibn Mahdi narrated to us. 1299 - He said: And Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhaynah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath and sees something else better than it, let him do what is better and expiate for his oath. Al-Bukhari said in his Tarikh: Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhaynah al-Abdi, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mursal. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim said: Udhaynah al-Abdi is Basran; he narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and from Umar ibn al-Khattab; his son Abd al-Rahman narrated from him. I heard my father saying that."
"1214","1300 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi at al-Harbiyyah informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Isam ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Imran narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn al-Arqam, from his grandfather al-Arqam: that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him. He said: Where do you intend? He said: I intended, O Messenger of Allah, here - and he gestured with his hand toward the direction of Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: What takes you out to it? Trade? He said: I said: No, but I intended prayer. He said: Prayer - and he gestured with his hand toward Makkah - is better than a thousand prayers - and he gestured toward Syria."
"1215","1301 - With the same chain, my father narrated to me: Ali ibn Abbas narrated to us, al-Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Imran and Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn al-Arqam narrated to me, from his grandfather: that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he mentioned the hadith."
"1216","1302 - And Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh at Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Sad ibn Ufayr narrated to us, Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam, from his grandfather al-Arqam - and he was a Badri - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sheltered in his house at al-Safa until they completed forty Muslim men; the last of them to embrace Islam was Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him). When they were forty they went out against the polytheists. He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to bid him farewell, intending to go out to Bayt al-Maqdis. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: I said: I want Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: What takes you out to it? For trade? I said: No, but I pray in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer here is better than a thousand prayers there. Attaf ibn Khalid was criticized by some and deemed trustworthy by some. Yahya ibn Imran: Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Unknown. This hadith Attaf narrated from Yahya and Uthman; then another than Attaf ibn Khalid narrates it from him; he is mentioned in the hadith after it."
"1217","1303 - Sad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Jad al-Washsha narrated to us, Abu Musab narrated to us, Yahya ibn Imran narrated to us, from his grandfather Uthman ibn al-Arqam, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Badr: Lay down what spoils you have with you."
"1218","1304 - Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Asbahani informed us by ijazah, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them by reading to him: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawwazi narrated to us, Abu Musab narrated to us, Yahya ibn Imran narrated to us, from his grandfather Uthman ibn al-Arqam, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Badr: Return what spoils you have with you. Abu Usayd al-Saidi raised the sword of Banu al-Aidh ibn al-Marzuban, and al-Arqam recognized it and said: Give it to me, O Messenger of Allah. So he gave it to him. Al-Tabarani said: This hadith is not narrated from al-Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam except with this chain; Abu Musab is alone in it."
"1219","1305 - Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh at Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. 1306 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, both said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Bashir ibn Maymun, from his uncle Usamah ibn Akhdari: that a man of Banu Shaqirah called Asram was among the group who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He brought him an Abyssinian boy he had bought in those lands and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I bought him and wished to name him and that you supplicate for blessing for him. He said: What is your name? He said: Asram. He said: Rather you are Zura. He said: What do you want him for? He said: I want him as a shepherd. He said: Then he is Asim. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clenched his fist. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad."
"1220","1307 - The Imam Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Naja ibn Ghanim the preacher informed us between Cairo and Egypt, that Abu Sabir Abd al-Sabur ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Fadl ibn Abi Mansur al-Harawi informed them by reading to him: Abu Amir Mahmud ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Azdi informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahbub informed us, Abu Isa Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sawrah al-Tirmidhi informed us, Sufyan ibn Waki and Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, both said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Musa ibn Yaqub al-Zamai narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir: Muslim ibn Abi Sahl al-Nabbal informed me: al-Hasan ibn Usamah ibn Zayd informed me: my father Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, he said: I knocked on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night for some need. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out wrapping something I did not know what it was. When I finished my need I said: What is this you are wrapping? He uncovered it, and behold Hasan and Husayn upon his thighs. He said: These two are my sons and the sons of my daughter. O Allah, I love them, so love them and love whoever loves them. Abu Isa al-Tirmidhi narrated it thus and said: A hasan gharib hadith. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Khalid ibn Makhlad with his chain, except that he said: Musa ibn Abi Sahl al-Nabbal, and I think it is a slip, and Allah knows best."
"1221","1308 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar the preacher at al-Harbiyyah informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ashath, from al-Hasan, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast. Abu Asim narrated it from Ashath."
"1222","1309 - Abu Zura Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Fannaki informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Ashath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast. Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik al-Humrani Abu Hani al-Basri: Yahya ibn Said said: In my view he is trustworthy and reliable, and Yahya ibn Main deemed him trustworthy."
"1223","1310 - The Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi at Isfahan informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zibriqan, from Usamah ibn Zayd: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr at midday heat, and none would be behind him but one or two rows, the people being in their midday rest and their trade. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have intended to burn down the houses of peoples who do not attend the prayer."
"1224","1311 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi at Baghdad informed us, that Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Bistami informed them by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Isa ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zibriqan: that a group of Quraysh passed Zayd ibn Thabit by, so they sent two men to ask him about the middle prayer. Zayd said: It is Zuhr. Two men among them stood and came to Usamah ibn Zayd and asked him about the middle prayer. He said: It is Zuhr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr at midday heat, and none would be behind him but one or two rows, the people being in their midday rest and their trade. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have intended to burn down the houses of peoples who do not attend the prayer. In this hadith is what indicates that al-Zibriqan did not hear it from Usamah, and Allah knows best. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yazid. Ibn Majah narrated it from Uthman ibn Ismail al-Hudhali al-Dimashqi, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, from Ibn Abi Dhib. Al-Zibriqan narrated it from a man from him."
"1225","1312 - Abu Zura Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zibriqan, from Zuhrah who said: We were sitting with Zayd ibn Thabit when he was asked about the middle prayer. He said: It is Zuhr. Usamah ibn Zayd passed by us, so we stood to him and asked him. He said: It is Zuhr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray it at midday heat. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it thus in his Musnad."
"1226","1313 - Umar ibn Ali the preacher informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Sulaym, freedman of Layth - and he was old - who said: Marwan ibn al-Hakam passed by Usamah ibn Zayd while he was praying, and Marwan mimicked him. Abu Mashar said: He had met them both. Usamah said: O Marwan, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not love every foul-mouthed, obscene person. Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah and Muhammad ibn Aflah narrated it from Usamah; it comes later. We mentioned this path only as a supporting witness for others."
"1227","1314 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abu al-Shatha, who said: I went out for Hajj and entered the House. When I was between the two pillars I went on until I clung to the wall. Ibn Umar entered until he stood beside me and prayed four. When he prayed I said to him: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Here Usamah ibn Zayd told me that he prayed. I said: How many did he pray? He said: For this I blame myself, that I stayed with him a lifetime and never asked him how many he prayed. In the next year he said: I went out for Hajj and came until I stood in his station. Ibn al-Zubayr came until he stood beside me and kept crowding me until he pushed me out of it, then prayed four. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Abu Muawiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim."
"1228","1315 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harbi at Baghdad informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah, from Abu al-Shatha who said: I went out for Hajj and came until I entered the House. When I was between the two pillars I went on until I clung to the wall. Ibn Umar came praying beside me and prayed four. When he prayed I said to him: Where in the House did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Usamah ibn Zayd told me that he prayed here. I said: How many did he pray? He said: For this I blame myself; I stayed with him a lifetime and never asked him how many he prayed. Then I performed Hajj the next year and came until I stood in his station. Ibn al-Zubayr came until he stood beside me and kept crowding me until he pushed me out of it, then prayed in it. Abu al-Shatha is Sulaym ibn al-Aswad al-Kufi, father of al-Ashath. Umarah is Ibn Umayr al-Taymi of Taym Allah, Kufan; both are men of the Sahih. Al-Daraqutni said: Abu Muawiyah al-Darir narrated it from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu al-Shatha, from Ibn Umar who said: Usamah ibn Zayd told me. Abu Ubaydah ibn Mamar differed from him and narrated it from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Shatha, from Ibn Umar, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Yazid ibn Zuray, Ashhal ibn Hatim, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi and al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated it from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House with Usamah ibn Zayd, Bilal and Uthman ibn Talhah; I met them and asked them, and they narrated it from Ibn Umar from the three of them. It has been narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Abbas, from Usamah: that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House he supplicated in all its corners and did not pray in it until he came out; when he came out he bowed two rakahs facing the House and said: This is the qiblah."
"1229","1316 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us: my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, who said: I saw Usamah ibn Zayd at the chamber of Aishah supplicating, then Marwan came and let him hear harsh words. Usamah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah hates the foul-mouthed, obscene person."
"1230","1317 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik the litterateur informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Muqri informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, both said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah who said: I saw Usamah ibn Zayd reclining at the door of the chamber of Aishah, raising his voice in song, and I saw him praying at the grave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Marwan passed by him and said: Do you pray at his grave, O son of my brother? He said to him an ugly word, then turned away. Usamah left and said to him: O Marwan, you are foul and obscene. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah hates the foul and the obscene, and you are foul and obscene."
"1231","1318 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubayd Allah who said: I saw Usamah. He said: I saw him praying at the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then Marwan ibn al-Hakam came out and said: Do you pray at his grave? He said: I love him. He said to him an ugly word, then turned away. Usamah left and said to Marwan: You have hurt me. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah hates the foul, obscene person, and you are foul and obscene. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili."
"1232","1319 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah informed us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Thabit ibn Qays Abu al-Ghusn narrated to me, he said: Abu Said al-Maqburi narrated to me, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I see you fasting in Shaban a fast you do not fast in any of the months except Ramadan? He said: That is a month people neglect between Rajab and Ramadan; the deeds of people are raised in it, so I love that my deed not be raised except while I am fasting."
"1233","1320 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr at Isfahan informed us by my reading to him - I said to him: Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed you by reading to him while you were present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Qays Abi al-Ghusn, from Abu Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I see you fasting in Shaban a fast you do not fast in any month? He said: That is a month people neglect; the deeds of people are raised in it, so I love that no deed of mine be raised except while I am fasting. It has been narrated from Abu Said from Usamah. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Rahawi, from Zayd ibn al-Hubab. Some narrated it without mentioning Abu Hurayrah. Thabit ibn Qays: Ahmad ibn Hanbal deemed him trustworthy, Yahya ibn Main said: No harm in him, and in a narration: weak. Ibn Hibban said: His report is not used as proof when none other corroborates him. Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated from him, and the narration of Ibn Mahdi from him suffices."
"1234","1321 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Saydalani at Isfahan informed us, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them by reading to him while present: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Furak al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Husayn ibn Hasan al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, Suayr ibn al-Khums narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a favor done to him and says to its doer: May Allah reward you with good, has excelled in praise."
"1235","1322 - And Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Talhah at Cairo, and Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari and Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Isa al-Qasri at Baghdad informed us, that Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad al-Shaybani informed them by reading to him while they listened: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ghaylan informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafii informed us: al-Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, Suayr ibn al-Khums narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a favor done to him and says to its doer: May Allah reward you with good, has excelled in praise. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Marwazi. He and al-Nasai also narrated it in the Book of the Deeds of Day and Night from Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari. Al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan sahih gharib hadith; we know it from the hadith of Usamah only by this way. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Umar ibn Said ibn Sinan and al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah al-Qattan, from Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari. Abu Hatim al-Razi was asked about this hadith and said: This hadith is munkar with this chain."
"1236","1323 - The Imam Abu al-Futuh Asad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli and others at Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn al-Hajjaj al-Zubaydi at Zabid in Yemen narrated to us, Abu Humah Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri mentioned from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two vicious wolves spending the night in an enclosure with sheep, tearing and eating, do not cause corruption in it faster than the seeking of wealth and honor causes in the religion of a Muslim. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Sufyan from Sulayman al-Taymi but Abu Qurrah."
"1237","1324 - Abu Zura Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Nasr al-Laftuwani at Isfahan informed us, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik the litterateur informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the hand of al-Hasan and al-Husayn and said: O Allah, I love them, so love them."
"1238","1325 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar - he is Ibn Qays al-Qawariri - narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, from al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I love them, so love them. Al-Taymi said: His hadith with me is written among what I heard from Abu Uthman. Yahya ibn Said said: Meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them). In Sahih al-Bukhari from the narration of Abu Uthman from Usamah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take me and al-Hasan and say: O Allah, I love them, so love them."
"1239","1326 - Humayd ibn Masadah narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usamah ibn Zayd and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas and another man of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever claims sonship to other than his father knowingly, Allah forbids Paradise to him."
"1240","1327 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud at Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Malih, from Usamah [ibn Zayd] who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not decree the death of a servant in a land except that He makes for him a need in it. Its chain is hasan, but I fear it is a mistake; the hadith is only known from the hadith of Abu Ishaq, from Matar ibn Ukamis, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1241","1328 - Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them by reading to him: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salim al-Khawlani narrated to us, Abu al-Asbagh Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to visit Abd Allah ibn Ubayy in his illness in which he died, and I was with him. He recognized death in him and said: I used to forbid you from loving the Jews. He said: Asad ibn Zurarah died, so what? When he died, his son Abd Allah came to him and said: Abd Allah has died, so give me your shirt to shroud him in. So he removed his shirt and clothed him in it."
"1242","1329 - Abu Zura Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Abd Allah ibn Ubayy in his illness in which he died. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recognized death in him, he said: By Allah, I used to forbid you from loving the Jews. He said: Sad - and the correct is Asad - ibn Zurarah hated them and died, so what? Abu Yala al-Mawsili narrated it from Abu Kurayb also. Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan from Abu al-Asbagh Abd al-Aziz."
"1243","1330 - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Harbi there informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: I entered with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Abd Allah ibn Ubayy in his illness to visit him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I used to forbid you from loving the Jews. Abd Allah said: Asad ibn Zurarah hated them and died."
"1244","1331 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar the preacher al-Harbi there informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik: Ata narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd: that he and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House, and he ordered Bilal, who closed the door. The House at that time was upon six pillars. He went on until he came to the two columns next to the door - the door of the Kabah - and sat, praised Allah, extolled Him, asked Him and sought His forgiveness. Then he stood until he came to what faced him of the back of the Kabah, and placed his face and body upon the Kabah, praised Allah, extolled Him, asked Him and sought His forgiveness. Then he left until he came to every corner of the House and faced it with takbir, tahlil, tasbih, praise of Allah mighty and exalted, seeking forgiveness and supplication. Then he came out and prayed two rakahs outside the House facing the Kabah, then left and said: This is the qiblah, this is the qiblah. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Hushaym, from Abd al-Malik, similar to it."
"1245","1332 - And Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi at Isfahan informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Yazid narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Ata, from Usamah ibn Zayd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House with Usamah, the House at that time upon six pillars. He prayed two rakahs between the two front columns, then came to what faced him of the House and pressed his belly and chest to it, and asked and sought forgiveness. Then he turned to every corner of the corners of the House with takbir, tahlil, tahmid, praise of Allah, supplication. Then he came out and faced the House and said: This is the qiblah, this is the qiblah, three times. Thus in the narration of Yazid ibn Harun he mentioned prayer in the House."
"1246","1333 - And Abu Zura Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Liftuwani at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik the litterateur informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us: Ata narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that he and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House, and he ordered Bilal, who closed the door. The House at that time was upon six pillars. He went on until he came to the two columns next to the door - the door of the Kabah - and praised Allah, extolled Him and sought His forgiveness. Then he turned to every corner of the corners of the House and faced it with takbir, tahlil and tasbih, and praised Allah and extolled Him with supplication and seeking forgiveness. Then he came out and prayed two rakahs facing the Kabah outside the House, and said: This is the qiblah, this is the qiblah. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated in the Two Sahihs from the narration of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata: Did you hear Ibn Abbas saying: You were only commanded with tawaf and not commanded to enter it? He said: He did not forbid me from entering it, but I heard him saying: Usamah ibn Zayd told me that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House he supplicated in all its corners and did not pray in it until he came out; when he came out he bowed two rakahs facing the House and said: This is the qiblah. I said: What are its corners, its angles? He said: Rather in every direction of the House. This is the wording of Muslim. The hadith we brought out contains other than this; perhaps Ata heard this wording from Ibn Abbas from Usamah, and heard the wordings in the hadith we mentioned from Usamah ibn Zayd, and Allah knows best. Al-Nasai narrated it from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, from Yahya ibn Said, and from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, from Hushaym, from Abd al-Malik, similar to it."
"1247","1334 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar the preacher at al-Harbiyyah informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us: Abd al-Malik informed us: Ata narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafat. He raised his hands supplicating, then his she-camel tilted with him and its bridle fell. He took the bridle with one hand while raising the other."
"1248","1335 - Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Qurashi informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Hushaym narrated to us: Abd al-Malik informed us: Ata informed us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd said: I was riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafat. He raised his hands supplicating, then his she-camel tilted with him and its bridle fell, so he took the bridle with one hand while raising the other. Al-Nasai narrated it from Yaqub, from Hushaym."
"1249","1336 - The Imam, the Hafiz Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Umar al-Madini informed us in his book, that Abu al-Qasim Ghanim ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ubayd Allah al-Burji informed them by reading to him: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us, Abu Bishr Yunus ibn Habib al-Ijli informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mihran who said: Umayr, freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to me from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Kabah, and he saw images. He called for a bucket of water, so I brought it to him, and he began erasing them, saying: May Allah destroy people who depict what they do not create."
"1250","1337 - Asad ibn Said al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, al-Tabarani informed us, al-Asfati narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mihran, from Umayr, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the House and saw images, so he called for water and began erasing them, saying: May Allah destroy people who depict what they do not create. We did not rely in narrating this hadith upon Khalid al-Umari, but upon the narration of Abu Dawud."
"1251","1338 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik the litterateur informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri: Iyad al-Kalbi narrated to me - and he was the cousin of Usamah ibn Zayd, and Usamah had married his daughter to him - from Usamah: that a man came from some of these countryside areas, and when he neared Madinah pain reminded him, so he returned. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I hope its mountain pass will not loom over us - meaning the pass of Madinah."
"1252","1339 - With the same chain, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Numan narrating from al-Zuhri, from Iyad al-Kalbi - and he was the cousin of Usamah - he said: Usamah had married his daughter to him: that Usamah ibn Zayd told him, he said: A man of some of these countryside areas with plague in him was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he neared Madinah, and that frightened people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope its mountain pass will not loom over us."
"1253","1340 - And Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us: my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri: Iyad ibn Subayri, freedman of Usamah, narrated to me from Usamah: that a man came from some countryside areas, pain seized him and he returned. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope its mountain pass will not loom over us - meaning the pass of Madinah."
"1254","1341 - And my maternal uncle the Imam, the scholar Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us by reading to him - it was said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Hilal al-Daqqaq informed you by reading to him: Abu al-Fadl Abd Allah ibn Ali, known as Ibn Zakari al-Daqqaq, informed us, Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us, Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Bakhtari al-Razzaz informed us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from a cousin of Usamah ibn Zayd called Iyad - and the daughter of Usamah was under him - from Usamah who said: A man who left some countryside areas was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he was on part of the road, pestilence struck him, and that frightened people. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope none of its passes will loom over us - meaning Madinah. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Ibrahim ibn Sad. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Kamil al-Muzaffar, from Ibrahim ibn Sad. Al-Haytham ibn Kulayb narrated it from Isa ibn Ahmad, from Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi, from Ibrahim ibn Sad."
"1255","1342 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Qurashi at Isfahan informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Yazid narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim who said: Usamah ibn Zayd came after his father was killed and stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shed tears. He came the next day and stood in that station of his, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Shall I meet from you today what I met from you yesterday? Thus Yazid ibn Harun narrated it, except that Qays did not mention in it what clarifies that he heard it from Usamah, and Allah knows best."
"1256","1343 - Abu Zura Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Muqri informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muhajir informed me, from al-Dahhak al-Maafiri, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Is there none eager for Paradise? For Paradise bears no risk; by the Lord of the Kabah it is a glittering light, a shaking sweet basil, a built palace, a flowing river, abundant ripe fruit, a beautiful handsome wife, many garments, in an eternal station, in joy, radiance and bliss, in a lofty, safe, splendid abode. They said: We are the eager ones for it, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: If Allah wills. He said: Then he mentioned jihad and urged it."
"1257","1344 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that Abu al-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them by ijazah if not by hearing: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Yala informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahm al-Antaki and Abd Allah ibn Awn al-Kharraz and others narrated to us, they said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir al-Ansari narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Usamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there none eager for Paradise? By the Lord of the Kabah it is a glittering light, a shaking sweet basil, a flowing river, a beautiful wife, in bliss, joy and eternal stay."
"1258","1345 - Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh at Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them by reading to him: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muhajir, from Sulayman ibn Musa: Kurayb narrated to me that Usamah ibn Zayd told him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there none eager for Paradise? By the Lord of the Kabah it is a glittering light, a shaking sweet basil, a flowing river, a beautiful handsome wife, in a garden and joy, in eternal stay. Ibn Majah narrated it from al-Abbas ibn Uthman al-Dimashqi, from al-Walid. Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Abbas ibn Uthman al-Dimashqi al-Balkhi."
"1259","1346 - Umar ibn Ali the preacher at al-Harbiyyah informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with gloom upon him. I asked him: What is wrong with him? He said: Jibril has not come to me for three days. Then a puppy was between his houses, so he ordered it killed. Jibril (peace be upon him) appeared to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejoiced at him when he saw him. He said: You did not come to me? He said: We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Husayn, from Ibn Abi Dhib, similar to it."
"1260","1347 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Kurayb, from Usamah who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw gloom upon him. I said: I see gloom upon you. He said: Jibril has not come to me for three days. He went out, and behold a puppy between his houses, so he ordered it killed. Jibril appeared to him and he said: You have not come to me for three days. He said: We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."
"1261","1348 - And Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, my uncle Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to me, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with gloom upon him. I asked him: What is wrong with you? He said: Jibril promised to come to me and has not come to me for three days; when he promises me he never breaks it. He said: I placed my hands upon my head. He said: What is wrong with you, woe to you, Usamah; I have a puppy. So he ordered it killed. Jibril (peace be upon him) appeared to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejoiced at him when he saw him. He said: You promised to come to me and did not come to me, and when you promised me you never broke it. Jibril said: We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images."
"1262","1349 - With the same chain, Muhammad ibn Harun informed us: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Kurayb, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw gloom upon him. I said: Why do I see gloom upon you? He said: Jibril (peace be upon him) has not come to me; and behold a puppy, so he ordered it killed. Jibril (peace be upon him) appeared to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejoiced at him and said: You did not come to me? He said: We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."
"1263","1350 - And Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them by reading to him: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Kurayb, from Usamah who said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with gloom upon him. I said: What is wrong with you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Jibril (peace be upon him) promised to come to me and has not come to me for three days. Then behold a dog. Usamah said: I placed my hands upon my head and cried out. He said: What is wrong with you, Usamah? I said: A dog. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered it killed. Then Jibril came to him and he said: Why did you not come to me? When you promised me you never broke it. He said: We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images. We did not rely in this report upon Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it in his Musnad from Ibn Abi Dhib. Al-Haytham ibn Kulayb narrated it in his Musnad from Ali ibn Sahl ibn al-Mughirah, from Shabbabah ibn Sawwar, from Ibn Abi Dhib."
"1264","1351 - Ubayd Allah al-Laftuwani at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik the litterateur informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Muqri informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, my uncle Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to me, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Kurayb, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Usamah ibn Zayd, that he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Kabah, and he saw images in it. He ordered me to bring him water, so I would bring him water in the bucket, and he would wet the cloth then strike the images with it, saying: May Allah destroy people who depict what they do not create. Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman has been spoken about, though Muslim brought him out in his Sahih. This hadith has preceded in the narration of Umayr, freedman of Ibn Abbas."
"1265","1352 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr - he is Ibn Abi Shaybah - narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Kulthum, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: We visited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while ill, and found him sleeping with his face covered by an Adani cloak. He uncovered his face and said: May Allah curse the Jews; they forbid the fat of sheep yet eat its price. It was said: Al-Baghawi narrated it from this Abu Bakr, from Ubayd Allah, from Shayban - meaning the grammarian - from al-Amash."
"1266","1353 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi at Baghdad informed us, that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Ali ibn Sahl ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from al-Amash, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Kulthum, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visiting him, and he was covered with an Adani cloak. He uncovered the cloth from his face, then said: May Allah curse the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, so they sold them and ate their price."
"1267","1354 - With the same chain, al-Haytham informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Kulthum, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: We visited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while ill, and found him sleeping with his face covered by an Adani cloak. He uncovered his face and said: May Allah curse the Jews; they forbid fats yet eat their price. Al-Haytham also narrated it from Abbas al-Duri, from Ubayd Allah, from Shayban."
"1268","1355 - Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh at Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, al-Tabarani informed us, Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Ghurab informed us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Kulthum al-Khuzai, from Usamah ibn Zayd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in his illness in which he died: May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques. Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it from Qays ibn al-Rabi. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, from Qays. Qays has been criticized by some; Shubah and Sharik used to praise him."
"1269","1356 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Harbi there informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Thabit ibn Qays Abu Ghusn narrated to us: Abu Said al-Maqburi narrated to me: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast days continuously until it was said: He does not break fast; and he would break fast days until he would hardly fast except two days of the week - if they fell in his fasting, otherwise he fasted them. He would not fast any month as he fasted Shaban. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast almost without breaking, and you break fast almost without fasting except two days - if they enter your fasting, otherwise you fast them? He said: Which two days? I said: Monday and Thursday. He said: Those are two days in which deeds are presented to the Lord of the worlds, and I love that my deed be presented while I am fasting. I said: I never saw you fasting any month as you fast Shaban? He said: That is a month people neglect between Rajab and Ramadan; it is a month in which deeds are raised to the Lord of the worlds, so I love that my deed be raised while I am fasting."
"1270","1357 - With the same chain, Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Thabit ibn Qays informed me, from Abu Said al-Maqburi, from Usamah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast Monday and Thursday."
"1271","1358 - And Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari at Baghdad informed us, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Bazzaz informed them by reading to him: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us, Abu al-Qasim Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Musa al-Kharaqi informed us, Abu Bakr Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Firyabi informed us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad and Said ibn Zakariyya al-Madaini narrated to us, both said: Thabit ibn Qays narrated to us: Abu Said al-Maqburi narrated to me from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until he would hardly break fast, and break fast until he would hardly fast. Two days of the week he would hardly leave without fasting them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, two days of the week you hardly leave without fasting them, Monday and Thursday? He said: Those are two days in which deeds are presented, so I love that my deed be presented while I am fasting. Al-Nasai narrated it from Amr ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi. Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii narrated it in his Musnad from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Ibn Mahdi; and from Ibn Bashshar, from Abu Amir, from Abi al-Ghusn. Al-Maqburi heard this hadith from Usamah ibn Zayd and from Abu Hurayrah from Usamah, and Allah knows best."
"1272","1359 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and Umm Habibah Aishah bint Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid at Isfahan informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi al-Khuzai informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim: that Usamah ibn Zayd used to fast the sacred months. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Fast Shawwal. So he left the sacred months and kept fasting Shawwal until he died. Ibn Majah narrated it in his Sunan from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi."
"1273","1360 - Abu Zura Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us by my reading to him at Isfahan - I said to him: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you by reading to him while you listened: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah ibn Fannaki informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Abu Kurayb informed us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Said ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Muhammad ibn Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill, I came down to him and the people came down to Madinah. I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he had lost speech and did not speak. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began placing his hands upon me then raising them, so I knew he was supplicating for me."
"1274","1361 - Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud informed us by reading to him while we listened at Isfahan - it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed you by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Said ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Muhammad ibn Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill, I came down and the people came down to Madinah. I entered upon him and he had lost speech and did not speak. He began raising his hand to the sky and pouring it upon me, so I knew that he was supplicating for me."
"1275","1362 - And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad and Umar ibn Ali al-Harbiyan at al-Harbiyyah informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them by reading to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Said ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father Usamah ibn Zayd who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill, I came down and the people came down with me to Madinah. I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he had lost speech and did not speak. He began raising his hands to the sky then pouring them upon me; I knew he was supplicating for me."
"1276","1363 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr at Isfahan informed us, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them by reading to him while present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah Samuwayh informed us, Abu Jafar Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Nufayl al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Said ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Usamah, from his father Usamah who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill, I came down and the people came down with me to Madinah. I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he had become grave and lost speech and did not speak. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began raising his hands to the sky then pouring them upon me; I knew he was supplicating for me."
"1277","1364 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik the litterateur informed them: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Abu Bishr Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Said ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Muhammad ibn Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill, I came down and the people came down with me to Madinah. I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he had lost speech and did not speak. He began raising his hands to the sky then pouring upon me; I knew he was supplicating for me. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Kurayb and said: A hasan gharib hadith."
"1278","1365 - Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh at Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed him with a Qibti garment from what Dihyah al-Kalbi had gifted him. I clothed my wife with it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why do you not wear the Qibti garment? I said: I clothed my wife with it. He said: Command her to put an undergarment beneath it, for I fear it describes her bones."
"1279","1366 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi at Baghdad informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father."
"1280","1367 - And Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik the litterateur informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Muqri informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed me with a thick Qibti garment which Dihyah al-Kalbi had gifted him. I clothed my wife with it. He said: Why have you not worn it? And in the narration of Ibn Bashshar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why have you not worn the Qibti garment? I said: I clothed my wife with it. He said: Command her to put an undergarment beneath it; I fear it describes her bones. Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated it from Abd Allah."
"1281","1368 - Umar ibn Ali the preacher at al-Harbiyyah informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr - meaning Ibn Muhammad - narrated to us, from Abd Allah - meaning Ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil - from Ibn Usamah ibn Zayd: that his father Usamah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed me with a thick Qibti garment from what Dihyah al-Kalbi had gifted. I clothed my wife with it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Why have you not worn the Qibti garment? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I clothed my wife with it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Command her to put an undergarment beneath it; I fear it describes the size of her bones."
"1282","1369 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi at al-Harbiyyah informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, from Muhammad ibn Usamah, from his father who said: Jafar, Ali and Zayd ibn Harithah gathered. Jafar said: I am the dearest of you to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ali said: I am the dearest of you to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Zayd said: I am the dearest of you to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: Come with us to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to ask him. Usamah said: They came seeking permission. He said: Go out and see who they are. I said: This is Jafar, Ali and Zayd - I did not say my father. He said: Permit them. They entered and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is dearest to you? He said: Fatimah. They said: We ask you about men. He said: As for you, Jafar, your character resembles mine and your creation resembles my creation, and you are of me and my tree. As for you, Ali, you are my in-law and the father of my child, and I am of you and you are of me. As for you, Zayd, you are my freedman, of me and to me, and the dearest of the people to me."
"1283","1370 - And Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh at Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Iqal narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, from Muhammad ibn Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Jafar, your character is as my character, your creation resembles my creation, and you are of me. And you, Ali, are of me and the father of my child."
"1284","1371 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud informed us by reading to him at Isfahan - it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed you by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us. 1372 - Sulayman said: And al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Muhammad ibn Aflah, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not love the foul, obscene person."
"1285","1373 - Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi and Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Usamah ibn Zayd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the House."
"1286","1374 - And Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar and al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali at Baghdad informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ali Abu Jafar narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the House. Al-Masudi is Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah ibn Abd Allah ibn Masud; Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Yahya ibn Main deemed him trustworthy. Ahmad ibn Hanbal said: The hearing of Abu al-Nadr and Asim and these from al-Masudi was after he became confused, yet they bore hearing from him and heard."
"1287","1375 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Abu Said narrated to us, Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Ibn Dharr narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Usamah ibn Zayd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth with tranquility upon him and commanded them with tranquility, and hastened in the valley of Muhassir."
"1288","1376 - And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Usamah ibn Zayd: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him riding behind him from Arafah. He said: People said: Our companion will tell us what he did. Usamah said: When he moved from Arafah and halted, he restrained the head of his mount until its head touched the middle of the saddle or nearly touched it, gesturing to people with his hand: Tranquility, tranquility, tranquility, until he came to Jam. Then he took al-Fadl ibn Abbas riding behind him. People said: Our companion will tell us what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did. Al-Fadl said: He kept moving gently as on the previous day, until he came upon the valley of Muhassir and moved swiftly in it until the ground became level with him. In this hadith is what indicates that the mention of Muhassir is only from the hadith of al-Fadl ibn Abbas."
"1289","1377 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn the litterateur informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Bundar narrated to us, Abd al-Kabir ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from his father, from Usamah ibn Zayd: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade facing the qiblah with stool or urine."
"1290","1378 - With the same chain, Abu Yala informed us: al-Zimmani narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from his father, that Usamah ibn Zayd told him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not face the qiblah with stool or urine."
"1291","1379 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, Mualla ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me, he said: I passed by the mosque and Ali and al-Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) were sitting. They said: O Usamah, seek permission for us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: O Messenger of Allah, Ali and al-Abbas are at the door wishing to enter upon you. He said: Do you know what brought them? I said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not know what brought them. He said: But I know what brought them; permit them. They entered upon him, and Ali said to him: O Messenger of Allah, we came to ask you: Which of your family is dearest to you? He said: Fatimah bint Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ali said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not ask you about your family. He said: Then the dearest of my family to me is he upon whom Allah bestowed favor and I bestowed favor, Usamah. He said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then you. Al-Abbas said: Have you made your uncle the last of them? He said: Ali preceded you in Hijrah."
"1292","1380 - And Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Muqri informed us, Jafar ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyanii informed us, Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah: Usamah ibn Zayd told me, he said: I passed and Ali and al-Abbas were sitting in the mosque. They said: O Usamah, seek permission for us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I entered and said: O Messenger of Allah, Ali and al-Abbas are at the door seeking permission. He said: Do you know what brought them? I said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: But I know what brought them; permit them. They entered and sat. Ali said: O Messenger of Allah, we came to ask you: Which of your family is dearest to you? He said: The dearest of my family to me is Fatimah bint Muhammad. Ali said: No, by Allah, we do not ask you about your family. He said: Then the dearest of my family to me is he upon whom Allah bestowed favor and I bestowed favor, Usamah ibn Zayd. Ali said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then you. Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said: O Messenger of Allah, have you made your uncle the last of them? He said: Ali preceded you in Hijrah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn al-Hasan, from Musa ibn Ismail, from Abu Awanah, and said: A hasan hadith. Shubah used to weaken Umar ibn Abi Salamah. Yahya ibn Main said: No harm in him. Al-Bukhari narrated for him as a witness, saying in the Book of Manners: Umar ibn Abi Salamah said from his father: He heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man carved wood and placed wealth inside it... the hadith of one who borrowed a thousand dinars; this or its meaning."
"1293","1381 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us by reading to him while we listened at Baghdad - it was said to him: Your father Abu Mansur Ali ibn Ali informed you by reading to him while you listened: Abu Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Sarifini informed us, Abu al-Qasim Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Hababah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi informed us, Ali narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Bedouins came from every place and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there sin upon us in such-and-such? He said: O servants of Allah, Allah has laid down hardship except for one who backbites a Muslim wrongfully; that one is ruined, or sinful and ruined. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we treat illness? He said: Yes, O servants of Allah; Allah mighty and exalted did not send down a disease but He sent down a cure for it, except one disease: old age. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing given to man or the Muslim? He said: Good character."
"1294","1382 - And Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us by reading to him while we listened there - it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed you by reading to her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us. 1383 - Al-Tabarani said: And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, both said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafat as if birds were upon the heads of his companions. Bedouins came to him from here and there: O Messenger of Allah, is there sin upon us in such-and-such? Is there sin upon us in such-and-such? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has lifted hardship except for one who backbites a Muslim wrongfully; that is the one who is sinful and ruined. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we treat illness? He said: Treat illness, for Allah mighty and exalted did not send down a disease but He placed a cure for it, except old age. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing given to people? He said: People have not been given anything better than good character."
"1295","1384 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us by my reading to him at Isfahan - I said to him: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed you by reading to him while you listened: Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Khalaf al-Maghribi informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah al-Sulami informed us, my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Bishr ibn Muadh narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik who said: The Bedouins said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we treat illness? He said: Yes, O servants of Allah, treat illness; Allah did not place a disease but He placed a cure for it, except one disease. They said: What is it? He said: Old age."
"1296","1385 - And Asad ibn Said at Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ziyad, from Usamah ibn Sharik who said: I witnessed Bedouins asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is there sin in such-and-such? He said to them: O servants of Allah, Allah has laid down hardship except for one who backbites the honor of his brother; that is the one who is sinful. And he said: Treat illness, O servants of Allah; Allah did not place a disease but He placed a cure with it, except old age. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing given to a servant? He said: Good character. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Muhammad ibn Jafar. Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan from Hafs ibn Umar al-Namari - both - from Shubah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Bishr ibn Muadh similar to it and said: A hasan sahih hadith. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Hisham ibn Ammar, from Ibn Uyaynah. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ismail ibn Masud and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, both from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Shubah abridged. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Amr, from Ali ibn Khashram, from Isa ibn Nawwas, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Ziyad similar to it; and from al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi, from Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi, from Sufyan: Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated to us: He heard Usamah ibn Sharik, similar to the hadith of Abu Bakr from Sufyan. Sufyan ibn Uyaynah said: There is no chain on the face of the earth today better than this. He narrated his saying: Treat illness, for Allah did not send down a disease but He sent down a cure for it except death and old age, from Imran ibn Musa ibn Mujashi, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ibn Idris, from Misar and Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah. Al-Daraqutni said: Mention of hadiths of men of the companions who narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); their hadiths were narrated by sound ways whose transmitters are not impugned, though al-Bukhari and Muslim did not bring them out; bringing them out is binding by their method. Usamah ibn Sharik: Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated from him, and Muslim brought out from Ziyad..."
"1297","1386 - Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us. 1387 - Sulayman said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, both from al-Shaybani, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik who said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Hajj. People would come to him, and one said: O Messenger of Allah, I hastened before I circumambulated? Or I delayed something or advanced something? He would say to them: No sin, except upon a man who backbites the honor of a Muslim wrongfully; that is the one who is sinful and ruined."
"1298","1388 - With the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Aslami narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with people asking him; one saying: I shaved before I sacrificed? Another saying: I did such-and-such before? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying: No sin."
"1299","1389 - With the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, Abu al-Awwam Imran narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj saying: Your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then the nearest, the nearest. A people came and said: O Messenger of Allah, Banu Yarbu killed us? He said: No soul wrongs another. Then a man asked him who forgot to stone the jamarat. He said: Stone, no sin. Then another came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I forgot tawaf. He said: Perform tawaf, no sin. Then another came to him who shaved before sacrificing. He said: Sacrifice, no sin. Whatever they asked him that day he said: No sin. Then he said: Allah mighty and exalted has removed hardship except for a man who backbites a Muslim; that is the one who is sinful and ruined. And he said: Allah mighty and exalted did not send down a disease but He sent down a cure for it, except old age."
"1300","1390 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us by reading to him at Baghdad - it was said to him: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Bazzar informed you by reading to him: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Fath, known as al-Ushari, informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi ibn Masud al-Daraqutni the Hafiz informed us by reading to him: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Wakil narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shubah ibn Jawan narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Bishr: Ziyad ibn Ilaqah narrated to us: Usamah ibn Sharik narrated to us, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with people asking him. A man said: I sacrificed before I shaved? He said: No sin. He kept saying: No sin. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing given to people? He said: Good character. They said: Shall we treat illness? He said: Yes; Allah mighty and exalted did not send down a disease but He sent down a cure for it, except death. Al-Tabarani said: Abu Asim is alone in it from Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Bashir al-Aslami. Abu Dawud brought it out from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. Ibn Majah narrated: No soul wrongs another, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Aqil, from Amr ibn Asim. Abu al-Awwam Imran ibn Dawar al-Qattan: Affan ibn Muslim deemed him trustworthy, while Yahya ibn Main and al-Nasai weakened him. His statement about advancing and delaying in Hajj rites has a witness in the Two Sahihs from the hadith of Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As."
"1301","1391 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi at Isfahan informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them by reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Ata ibn al-Saib, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes out seeking to divide my community while they are united, strike his neck. Al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Qudamah, from Jarir. Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Zayd is not well known. A group narrated it from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah from Arfajah ibn Shurayh. I say: Perhaps he heard it from both, and Allah knows best. Ahmad ibn Mani narrated it from Hushaym, from Mujalid. Abu Yala also narrated it from Surayj ibn Yunus, from Hushaym, from Mujalid, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah. Al-Tabarani narrated it from Ubayd ibn Ghannam, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Muhammad ibn Bishr, from Mujalid, from Ziyad."
"1302","1392 - Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh at Isfahan informed us, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the black seed there is cure for every disease except death. Al-Muttalib: Ahmad and Yahya deemed him trustworthy. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He is not used as proof, without clarifying the criticism, so it is not accepted, and Allah knows best. This hadith has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Aishah and others."
"1303","1393 - Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there, that Tamim ibn Abi Said al-Jurjani informed them by reading to him: Ali ibn Muhammad al-Bahhathi informed us, Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban ibn Ahmad al-Busti informed us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Zuhayr informed us at Tustar: Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever Allah dislikes from you, do not do it in solitude."
"1304","1394 - Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them by reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun and Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Said. 1395 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the skins of predators. Yazid ibn Harun added: to be spread as furnishings."
"1305","1396 - With the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Shubah - and the correct is Said - from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that the skins of predators be spread as furnishings."
"1306","1397 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Isma'il narrated to us, Sa'id informed us, and Ibn Ja'far, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the skins of predatory beasts. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Yahya and Ibn 'Ulayyah, from Sa'id. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, and from Abu Kurayb, from Ibn al-Mubarak and Muhammad ibn Bishr and Abdullah ibn Isma'il, from Sa'id, with the addition (that they be used as furnishings). Al-Tirmidhi said: We do not know anyone who said 'from his father' except Ibn Abi 'Arubah. And from Ibn Bashshar, from Ghundar, from Shu'bah, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Abu al-Malih, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: and this is more authentic. And from Ibn Bashshar, from Mu'adh ibn Hisham, from his father, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih: that he disliked the skins of predatory beasts. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'id, from Yahya, from Ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from his father. Al-Daraqutni said: And the hadiths of Qatadah from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah ibn 'Umayr, from his father, meaning that they are among the hadiths that al-Bukhari and Muslim are obliged to include."
"1307","Another, 1398 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi informed us, with my reading to him there - I said to him: Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn al-Fudayl al-Fudayli informed you, with reading to him: Abu Mudar Muhallim ibn Isma'il al-Dabbi informed us, the judge Abu Sa'id al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi informed us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi al-Sarraj informed us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (Hadith)."
"1308","1399 - Abu al-Hasan al-Mu'ayyad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Tusi informed us, with my reading to him in Nishapur - I said to him: Umm al-Khayr Fatimah bint 'Ali ibn al-Muzaffar ibn Ruz'bil informed you, with reading to her: Abu al-Husayn 'Abd al-Ghafir ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Ghafir al-Farisi informed us, Abu 'Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan al-Hiri informed us, Abu al-'Abbas al-Hasan ibn Sha'ban in Nasa narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id and Sulayman ibn Ayyub, companion of al-Basri, and Abu Kamil al-Fudayl ibn al-Husayn narrated: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (Hadith)."
"1309","1400 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us, with reading to him while we listened there - it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed you, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu 'Umar al-Darir narrated to us. 1401 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us. 1402 - He said: And Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, they said: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prayer is accepted without purification, and no charity from misappropriated spoils; their wording is one."
"1310","1403 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ali ibn 'Ali al-Sufi informed us, with reading to him while we listened in Baghdad - it was said to him: Your father Abu Mansur 'Ali informed you, with reading to him while you listened: Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Sarifini informed us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us, 'Ali narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah: I heard Abu al-Malih narrating from his father: that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No prayer is accepted without purification, and no charity from misappropriation. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id and Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj, all three from Shu'bah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muslim ibn Ibrahim, from Shu'bah. Ibn Majah narrated it from Bundar, from Yahya ibn Sa'id and Ghundar, from Bakr ibn Khalaf, from Yazid ibn Zuray', and from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from 'Ubayd ibn Sa'id and Shabababah ibn Sawwar, all of them from Shu'bah. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, and from al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Dhari', from Yazid ibn Zuray', and from Isma'il ibn Mas'ud, from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, both from Shu'bah. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sami, from 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd, and from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Hibban ibn Musa, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Shu'bah. This hadith has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"1311","Another, 1404 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah, he said: We prayed 'Isha' in Basra and it rained on us, then I came seeking to open the door, and my father Usamah said to me: You saw us with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it rained on us, and the soles of our sandals were not even wetted, and the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out: Pray in your dwellings."
"1312","1405 - And with it, al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Malih, he said: I went out on a rainy night to the mosque; when I returned I sought to open the door, and my father said to me: You certainly saw us with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Hudaybiyah, and rain fell on us that did not wet the soles of our sandals, and then the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced: Pray in your dwellings."
"1313","1406 - And with it, al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abu 'Umar al-Hawdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a rainy day, and he ordered a caller who called out: Prayer is in the dwellings."
"1314","1407 - 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad: that his father Abu Mansur informed them, with reading to him: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini informed us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi informed us, 'Ali narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, he said: Rain befell us at Hunayn, and the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out: Pray in the dwellings. Imam Ahmad narrated it from 'Abd al-Razzaq. And he narrated it from 'Affan and Bahz, Hammam; and from Bahz, from Shu'bah; and from Yunus, from Aban, from Qatadah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Kathir, from Hammam; and from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from 'Abd al-A'la, from Sa'id, from a companion of his, from Abu al-Malih; and from Nasr ibn 'Ali, from Sufyan ibn Habib, from Khalid al-Hadhdha'. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Ghundar, from Shu'bah. Ibn Hibban narrated it from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sami, from 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd; and from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Hibban, from Abdullah, from Shu'bah; and from Shabab ibn Salih in Wasit, from Wahb ibn Baqiyyah, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah. It has been narrated at the time of al-Hudaybiyah and narrated on the day of Hunayn through various chains, and this indicates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted them that at the time of al-Hudaybiyah and on the day of Hunayn, and Allah knows best."
"1315","Another, 1408 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Asbahan: that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to me, from Abu al-Malih, from his father: that a man freed a share of a slave, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed it and said: Allah has no partner."
"1316","1409 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harbi informed us in Baghdad: that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from his father: that a man of his people freed a share he owned of a slave, and that was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he placed his full emancipation upon him from his wealth, and said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has no partner."
"1317","1410 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abu 'Umar al-Hawdi and Hani ibn Yahya narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, that a man freed a portion of a slave, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed his emancipation, and said: Allah has no partner."
"1318","1411 - Abdullah al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, that a man of Hudhayl freed a share he owned of a slave, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is entirely free; Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has no partner. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Bahz, from Hammam, with the hadith of the share in the slave as mursal. Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan from Abu al-Walid Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik and from Muhammad ibn Kathir, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, without saying 'from his father'. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Abu al-Walid; and from Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, from Habban ibn Hilal, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih, from his father; and from Mu'ammal ibn Hisham, from Isma'il, from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah; and from Ibn Muthanna, from Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi, from Hisham, all from Qatadah, from Abu al-Malih: that a man... and he did not mention his father. Al-Nasa'i said: Hisham and Sa'id are more established in Qatadah than Hammam, and their hadith is more deserving of correctness. I say: Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated it from Sa'id as raised to the Prophet."
"1319","Another, 1412 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Abdan ibn Ahmad and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, they said: Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humran narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from Abu al-Malih, from his father Usamah, he said: I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and our camel stumbled, so I said: May Satan perish. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say 'May Satan perish', for he grows until he becomes like a house, and says: By my strength; but say: In the name of Allah, for he becomes like a fly. Abu Tamimah's name is Tarif ibn Mujalid; al-Bukhari transmitted from him."
"1320","1413 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Asbahan: that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, with reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma' narrated to us, Abdullah narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Sulayman al-Ahwal, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from the one riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): the she-camel stumbled with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: So I said: May Satan perish. He said: Do not say 'May Satan perish', for he magnifies himself until he becomes like a mountain and says: By my strength I threw him down; but say: In the name of Allah, for he diminishes until he becomes like a fly."
"1321","1414 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there: that Hibat Allah informed them, with reading to him: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from the one riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or one who narrated to him from the one riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he was riding behind him and his mount stumbled with him, and he said: May Satan perish. He said: Do not do that, for he magnifies when you say that until he becomes like a mountain, and says: By my strength I threw him down; and when you say: In the name of Allah, he diminishes until he becomes like a fly. Imam Ahmad narrated it from 'Affan, from Shu'bah, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Tamimah, from the one riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or from a man from the one riding behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in the book of deeds of day and night, from 'Uthman ibn Abdullah, from Ahmad ibn 'Abdah. And it was said: it was narrated from Khalid, from Abu Tamimah, from Abu al-Malih, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as mursal."
"1322","Another, 1415 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad, grandson of Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Abdullah ibn Mandah, informed us in Asbahan: that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, with reading to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim informed us, Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamimah, from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah al-Hudhali, from his father, and Usamah had accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: That was among us, meaning Hudhayl, he said: A woman threw another woman with a pole and killed her and killed what was in her womb, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged blood-money for the woman, and judged the blood-money of the fetus as a ghurrah for her husband, and judged the 'aql upon the 'asabah of the killer."
"1323","1416 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Miqdam ibn Dawud al-Basri narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, he said: I heard Abu al-Malih, from his father, and he had accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There were among us two women; one of them struck the other with a pole and killed her and killed what was in her womb, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged for the woman the 'aql, and for the fetus a ghurrah: a male or female slave, or a horse, or two camels, or such-and-such of sheep. A man of the killer's clan said: How can blood-money be paid, O Messenger of Allah, for one who neither ate nor drank nor cried out? Such is wasted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you a rhyming speaker? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that the woman's inheritance is for her husband and child, and that the 'aql is upon the 'asabah of the killer. Al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated it from Salamah ibn Tammam, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, and mentioned it, saying in it: a male or female slave, or five hundred, or a horse, or one hundred and twenty sheep. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."
"1324","Another, 1417 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us, there: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ibrahim ibn 'Umar al-Waki'i narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Sawadah ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, Salih ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah al-Hudhali, my father narrated to me, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When a community of communities, forty or more, bear witness, Allah validates their testimony, or he said: affirms their testimony. Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Ma'mari narrated it from Khalaf ibn Salim, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Shu'bah, from Mubashshir ibn Abi al-Malih, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. It is possible that Abu al-Malih heard it from his father and from Ibn 'Umar, and Allah knows best."
"1325","Another, 1418 - As'ad ibn Sa'id informed us that Fatimah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, al-Tabarani informed us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-'Ayshi narrated to us. 1419 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Musa ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Faddalah narrated to us, from Salim ibn 'Ubayd Allah ibn Salim, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast from wadih to wadih. It was said: it is from crescent to crescent. Abu Qutaybah is Salm ibn Qutaybah. This al-Mufaddal is al-Basri; Abu Hatim al-Razi said: his hadith is written. Yahya ibn Ma'in said: he is not strong. Al-Nasa'i said: he is not strong. Al-Tirmidhi said: al-Mufaddal ibn Faddalah al-Misri is more reliable than this one and better known."
"1326","Another, 1420 - 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ali ibn 'Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad: that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them, with reading to him: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Fath, known as al-'Ushari, informed us, Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn 'Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi al-Daraqutni informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Ahmad al-Jawaribi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Isa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Ghassani narrated to me, 'Abbad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mubashshir, from Abu al-Malih, from Usamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Al-Daraqutni said: Mubashshir is alone in it from Abu al-Malih, and none narrated it from him except 'Abbad ibn Sa'id."
"1327","1421 - As'ad ibn Sa'id informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Isa al-Tammar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mubashshir ibn Abi al-Malih, from Abu al-Malih, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He does not thank Allah who does not thank people. Similar has been narrated from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, which comes later."
"1328","Another, 1422 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us, with reading to him in Asbahan - it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed you, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-'Uruqi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Isa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Ghassani narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from Mubashshir ibn Abi al-Malih, from his father, from his grandfather Usamah ibn 'Umayr: that he prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the two rak'ahs of Fajr, praying near him, and he prayed two light rak'ahs, and I heard him say: O Allah, Lord of Jibril and Mika'il and Israfil and Muhammad, I seek refuge in You from the Fire, three times."
"1329","1423 - Abu Ahmad 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad: that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Baqi al-Bazzaz informed them, with reading to him: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Fath, known as al-'Ushari, informed us, Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn 'Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi ibn Mas'ud al-Daraqutni al-Hafiz informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Ahmad al-Jawaribi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Isa narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya narrated to me, 'Abbad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Mubashshir, from Abu al-Malih, from his father Usamah: that he prayed two rak'ahs while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed near him, and he prayed two light rak'ahs, then I heard him while sitting say: O Allah, Lord of Jibril and Mika'il and Israfil and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I seek refuge in You from the Fire, three times. Al-Daraqutni said: Mubashshir ibn Abi al-Malih is alone in it, from his father, from his grandfather. I say: I have not seen any criticism of any of them."
"1330","Musnad of Asad ibn Kurz al-Qasri, may Allah be pleased with him. 1424 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us: that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, with reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali informed us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Awsat, from Khalid ibn Abdullah, from his grandfather Asad ibn Kurz, he said: He heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The sick person, his sins fall away just as the leaves of a tree fall away."
"1331","1425 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhu'i al-Qadi narrated to us, 'Uqbah ibn Mukram al-'Ammi narrated to us. 1426 - Al-Tabarani said: And 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Hafs 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us. 1427 - He said: And Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us, they said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Awsat narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from his grandfather Asad ibn Kurz: he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Illness removes sins just as the leaves of a tree fall away."
"1332","1428 - 'Umar ibn 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Wa'iz al-Harbi informed us in al-Harbiyyah: that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, 'Uqbah ibn Mukram al-'Ammi narrated to me, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Isma'il ibn Awsat, from Khalid ibn Abdullah, from his grandfather Asad ibn Kurz: he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The sick person's sins fall away just as the leaves of a tree fall away. Ibn Abi Hatim said: Asad ibn Kurz had companionship; Khalid ibn Abdullah, Damrah ibn Habib and al-Muhajir ibn Habib narrated from him; I heard my father say that."
"1333","Another, 1429 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us, there: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu 'Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Artah ibn al-Mundhir, from al-Muhajir ibn Habib al-Zubaydi, from Asad ibn Kurz, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Asad ibn Kurz, you will not enter Paradise by deeds, but by the mercy of Allah. I said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, unless Allah overtakes me or envelops me with mercy from Him."
"1334","Musnad of Asla' ibn Sharik al-Ashja'i, may Allah be pleased with him. 1430 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Sahl ibn Musa Shiran al-Ramahurmuzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, al-'Ala' ibn al-Fadl ibn Abi Suwiyyah al-Minqari narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Ruzayq al-Maliki, of Banu Malik ibn Ka'b ibn Sa'd, who lived one hundred and seventeen years, narrated to us, from his father, from al-Asla' ibn Sharik, he said: I used to saddle the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I became junub on a cold night, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to depart, and I disliked saddling his she-camel while junub, and I feared that if I washed with cold water I would die or fall ill, so I ordered a man of the Ansar and he saddled it, and I placed stones and heated water with them and washed, then I caught up with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions, and he said: O Asla', why do I see your saddling changed? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not saddle it; a man of the Ansar saddled it. He said: Why? I said: I became junub and feared the cold for myself, so I ordered him to saddle it, and I placed stones and heated water and washed with it. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: O you who believe, do not approach prayer while intoxicated, up to: Indeed Allah is Pardoning, Forgiving."
"1335","1431 - Al-Hafiz Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Makki al-Asbahani informed us, there: that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, al-Hafiz Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, al-'Ala' ibn Abi Suwiyyah narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Ruzayq al-Maliki, of Banu Malik ibn Ka'b ibn Sa'd, who lived one hundred and seventeen years, narrated to me, from his father, from al-Asla' ibn Sharik, he said: I used to saddle the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I became junub on a cold night, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to depart, and I disliked saddling his she-camel while junub, and I feared that if I washed with cold water I would die or fall ill, so I ordered a man of the Ansar and he saddled it, then I laid stones and heated water with them and washed, then I caught up with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions. He mentioned the rest of the hadith, and in it: I laid stones. Our shaykh Abu al-Faraj ibn al-Jawzi said: al-'Ala' ibn al-Fadl al-Minqari, they mentioned him among the weak, but he did not mention who declared him weak. I looked in more than one book of the names of weak men and did not see him among them, and Allah knows best."
"1336","Musnad of Aslam ibn Bajrah al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. 1432 - The jurist Imam Abu al-Futuh As'ad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-'Ijli and Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Masqalah al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn 'Amr al-Fihri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Aslam al-Ansari, from his father, from his grandfather Aslam al-Ansari."
"1337","1433 - Abu Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn 'Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi and Abu al-'Ala' 'Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja' ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Asbahanis informed us in their books: that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, with reading to him: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Masqalah al-Asbahani informed us, al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn 'Amr al-Fihri narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Ansari, from his father, from his grandfather Aslam al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put me in charge of the captives of Qurayzah, and I would look at the private part of the boy; if I saw that hair had grown I struck his neck, and if I did not see it grown I placed him among the spoils of the Muslims. Al-Tabarani said: This hadith is not narrated from Aslam al-Ansari except by this chain; al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar is alone in it. 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Aslam ibn Bajrah al-Sa'idi narrated from his grandfather, and his grandfather had companionship; I heard my father say that."
"1338","Musnad of Asmar ibn Mudarris, may Allah be pleased with him. 1434 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us, with reading to him while we listened in Asbahan - it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed you, with reading to her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar, Bundar, narrated to us, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn 'Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Umm Janub bint Tumaylah narrated to me, from her mother Suwaydah bint Jabir, from her mother 'Aqilah bint Asmar ibn Mudarris, from her father Asmar ibn Mudarris, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged allegiance to him, and he said: Whoever gets first to what no Muslim got to before him, it is his. So people went out racing, marking lines. Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan from Muhammad ibn Bashshar. Umm Janub bint Numaylah: I saw it ضبط with nun in the Sunan of Abu Dawud, and with tha' with three dots in al-Mu'jam, and with ta' with two dots in al-Bukhari's Tarikh and in Abu Nu'aym's Ma'rifat al-Sahabah, and Allah knows best what is correct."
"1339","Musnad of Asma' ibn Harithah al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him. 1435 - Abu 'Ali 'Umar ibn 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Wa'iz al-Harbi informed us, there: that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, 'Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Hind ibn Harithah, and Hind was of the companions of al-Hudaybiyah, and his brother whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ordering his people to fast 'Ashura' is Asma' ibn Harithah, and Yahya ibn Hind narrated to me from Asma' ibn Harithah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and said: Order your people to fast this day. He said: What if I find them having already eaten? He said: Then let them complete the rest of their day."
"1340","1436 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Saffar narrated to us, 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us. 1437 - Sulayman said: And 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi narrated to us. 1438 - He said: And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hind ibn Harithah narrated to me from Asma' ibn Harithah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on the day of 'Ashura', saying: Go to your people and order them to fast this day. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not see myself reaching them before they eat. He said: Order whoever of them ate to fast the rest of his day. This hadith has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Salamah ibn al-Akwa' al-Aslami. Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Abu Khalifah, from Sahl ibn Bakkar, from Wuhayb, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Asma', thus he mentioned it."
"1341","Musnad of al-Aswad ibn Asram al-Muharibi, may Allah be pleased with him. 1439 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Iqal al-Harrani narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us. 1440 - Sulayman said: And Abu 'Aqil Anas ibn Salim al-Khawlani and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Mu'afir Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Abi Karimah al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahim, from 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht, from Sulayman ibn Habib al-Muharibi, from Aswad ibn Asram al-Muharibi: that he came with fat camels of his to Medina in a time of drought and barrenness of the land, and when the people of Medina saw them they marveled at their fatness, and I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they were brought, and he went out to them and looked at them, and said: Why did you bring these camels of yours? He said: I wanted a servant for them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who has a servant? 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I have, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Bring her. 'Uthman brought her, and when Aswad saw her he said: The like of her is what I want. He said: Take her, she is yours. Aswad took her and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took possession of his camels. Aswad said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Do you control your tongue? He said: What do I control if I do not control it? He said: Do you control your hand? He said: What do I control if I do not control my hand? He said: Do not say with your tongue except what is good, and do not extend your hand except to good. Abu 'Abd al-Rahim's name is Khalid ibn Abi Yazid, maternal uncle of Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani; Muslim transmitted from him. Musa ibn A'yan also narrated it from Khalid."
"1342","1441 - Al-Hafiz Imam Abu Musa Muhammad ibn 'Umar al-Madini informed us, by ijazah: that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, with reading to him: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Qadi narrated to us, Khalaf ibn 'Amr al-'Ukbari narrated to us, Mu'afa ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi Yazid, from 'Abd al-Wahhab, meaning Ibn Bukht, from Habib ibn Sulayman, from Aswad ibn Asram, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Do you control your tongue? He said: I said: What do I control if I do not control my tongue? He said: Do you control your hand? He said: I said: What do I control if I do not control my hand? He said: Do not say with your tongue except what is good, and do not extend your hand except to good."
"1343","Musnad of al-Aswad ibn Khalaf al-Khuza'i, may Allah be pleased with him. 1442 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu 'Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, 'Abdullah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed me: that Muhammad ibn al-Aswad ibn Khalaf informed him that his father al-Aswad attended the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledging allegiance to the people at Qarn Masqalah. He said: Qarn Masqalah is toward the houses of Abu Thumamah, that which faces the house of Ibn 'Amir from it, and that which turns away from it toward the house of Ibn Samurah and around it. Al-Aswad said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledging allegiance to the people; men, women, young and old came and pledged to him upon Islam and the shahadah. I said: What is the shahadah? Muhammad ibn al-Aswad informed me: upon testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah."
"1344","1443 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us, with my reading to him in Baghdad - I said to him: Hibat Allah informed you, with reading to him: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abdullah ibn 'Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed me that Muhammad ibn al-Aswad ibn Khalaf informed him: that his father al-Aswad saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pledging allegiance to the people on the day of the Conquest. He said: He sat at Qarn Masqalah and pledged the people upon Islam and the shahadah. He said: I said: What is the shahadah? He said: Muhammad ibn al-Aswad ibn Khalaf informed me: that he pledged them upon belief in Allah and testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."
"1345","Musnad of al-Aswad ibn Sari' al-Minqari, may Allah be pleased with him. 1444 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, with reading to him while we listened in Herat - it was said to him: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed you, with reading to him while you listened: Abu 'Amr al-Musayyab ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyab al-Arghiyani informed us, Abu 'Umar 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi informed us, the judge Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, al-Aswad ibn Sari' narrated to us, he said: We were in a campaign and gained victory and killed among the polytheists, until killing reached the point that they killed offspring, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is with people that killing reaches them to killing offspring? Behold, do not kill offspring; behold, do not kill offspring. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, are they not the children of the polytheists? He said: Are not your best ones the children of the polytheists?"
"1346","1445 - Abu 'Ali 'Umar ibn 'Ali al-Wa'iz al-Harbi informed us, there: that Hibat Allah informed them, with reading to him: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yunus narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari': that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment on the day of Khaybar, and its correct form is Hunayn, and they fought the polytheists, and killing led them to the offspring, and when they went beyond, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What made you kill the offspring? They said: O Messenger of Allah, they were only the children of the polytheists. He said: Are your best ones but the children of the polytheists? By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, no soul is born except upon the fitrah until its tongue expresses from it."
"1347","1446 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani informed us, there: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab and Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, they said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Yahya Abu al-Haytham, and he was intelligent, al-Hasan narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', and he was a poet and the first to narrate stories in this mosque, he said: Killing led among them until they killed offspring, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Are not your best ones the children of the polytheists? No child is born except upon the fitrah of Islam until he speaks; then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian or a Magian. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Isma'il and Hushaym, from Yunus, similarly; and from Muhammad ibn Ja'far, from al-Sari ibn Yahya. This hadith was narrated from al-Hasan by Mubarak ibn Fadalah, Abu Hamzah al-'Attar Ishaq ibn al-Rabi', Ash'ath ibn 'Abd al-Malik, 'Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah, Hisham, al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad and 'Anbasah al-Ghanawi; some narrated it in full and some abridged it. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ziyad ibn Ayyub. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Fadl ibn Hubab."
"1348","Another, 1447 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there: that Hibat Allah informed them, with reading to him: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh narrated to us, 'Awf narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not recite to you praises with which I praised my Lord, Mighty and Majestic? He said: Your Lord loves praise."
"1349","1448 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, 'Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, 'Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, and another whom he named, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari': that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I praised you with praises. He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves to be praised, and he did not ask him to recite."
"1350","1449 - And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, 'Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, 'Asim ibn 'Ali narrated to us. 1450 - Sulayman said: And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sawwar al-'Anbari narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Muzani narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: al-Aswad ibn Sari' said: Shall I not recite to you praises with which I praised my Lord? He said: Your Lord loves praise, and he did not ask him for more than that."
"1351","1451 - And with it, Sulayman informed us, Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb al-'Askari narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: al-Aswad ibn Sari' was a poet, and he said: O Prophet of Allah, shall I not let you hear praises with which I praised my Lord? He said: Your Lord loves praise, or: nothing is more beloved to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, than praise."
"1352","1452 - And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn 'Ubayd ibn 'Aqil narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one loves praise more than Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and no one has more excuses than Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from 'Ali ibn Hujr, from Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah, from Yunus, similarly."
"1353","Another, 1453 - As'ad ibn Sa'id al-Asbahani informed us, there: that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ma'mar ibn Bakkar al-Sa'di narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from al-Aswad ibn Sari' al-Tamimi, he said: I came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I have composed poetry in which I praised Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and praised you. He said: As for what you praised Allah with, bring it; and what you praised me with, leave it. I began reciting to him, then a tall, thin-nosed man entered, and he said to me: Stop. When he left he said: Bring it. I began reciting, and before long he returned, and said to me: Stop. When he left he said: Bring it. I said: Who is this, O Prophet of Allah, whom when he enters you say Stop, and when he leaves you say Bring it? He said: This is 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, and there is nothing of falsehood in him. Imam Ahmad narrated it from 'Affan and Hasan ibn Musa, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah."
"1354","Another, 1454 - 'Umar ibn 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Zahid informed us in al-Harbiyyah: that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, 'Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Aswad ibn Sari': that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four on the Day of Resurrection: a deaf man who hears nothing, a foolish man, an aged man, and a man who died in the fatrah. As for the deaf, he says: Lord, Islam came and I heard nothing. As for the foolish, he says: Lord, Islam came and children pelted me with dung. As for the aged, he says: Lord, Islam came and I understood nothing. As for the one who died in the fatrah, he says: Lord, no messenger of Yours came to me. He takes their covenants that they will obey Him, and sends to them: Enter the Fire. He said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if they entered it, it would be coolness and safety upon them."
"1355","1455 - And with it, 'Ali narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: And my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah, with the like of this hadith, except that he said at its end: Whoever enters it, it is coolness upon him, and whoever does not enter it is dragged to it."
"1356","1456 - As'ad ibn Sa'id informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Four on the Day of Resurrection argue with a plea: a deaf man who hears nothing, a foolish man, an aged man, and one who died in the fatrah. As for the deaf, he says: Lord, Islam came and I heard nothing. As for the foolish, he says: Islam came and children pelted me with dung. As for the aged, he says: Islam came and I understood nothing. As for the one who died in the fatrah, he says: Lord, Your messenger did not come to me. He takes their covenants that they will obey Him, and sends to them a messenger: Enter the Fire. He said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, if they entered it, it would be coolness and safety upon them. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim."
"1357","Another, 1457 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, 'Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid al-'Attar narrated to us, Ma'mar ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', he said: When 'Uthman ibn Maz'un died, the Muslims grieved for him; then when Ibrahim, son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, he said: Join our righteous predecessor 'Uthman ibn Maz'un."
"1358","Another, 1458 - As'ad ibn Sa'id informed us, with reading to him, in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. Sulayman said: And Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Abd al-Mu'min narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Mus'ab al-Qirqisani narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin and Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari', he said: A captive was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I repent to Allah and I do not repent to Muhammad. He said: He recognized the right for its people."
"1359","1459 - And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Sallam ibn Miskin, from al-Hasan, from al-Aswad ibn Sari': that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a captive, and he said: O Allah, I repent to You and I do not repent to Muhammad. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He recognized the right for its people. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Muhammad ibn Mus'ab, from Sallam. Muhammad ibn Mus'ab was criticized by Yahya ibn Ma'in and others; Imam Ahmad said: There is no harm in him."
"1360","Musnad of Usayd ibn Hudayr al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. Usayd ibn Hudayr ibn Simak ibn 'Atik al-Ashhali Abu Yahya al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. 1460 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us, there: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, 'Ikrimah ibn Khalid narrated to me: that Usayd ibn Hudayr ibn Simak narrated to him, he said: Mu'awiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to Marwan ibn al-Hakam: When a man is stolen from and finds his stolen property, he is most entitled to it when he finds it. Marwan wrote to me of that, and I was his governor over al-Yamamah, so I wrote to Marwan: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that when it is found with a man not accused, its master may take it for the price if he wishes, or follow his thief if he wishes. Then Abu Bakr, 'Umar and 'Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, judged likewise. Marwan sent my letter to Mu'awiyah, and Mu'awiyah sent to Marwan: Neither you nor Usayd judge over me in what I have been put in charge of; rather I judge over you both, so carry out what I ordered you. Marwan sent Mu'awiyah's letter to me, and I said: By Allah, I will never judge by it. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Hawdhah ibn Khalifah. Abu Dawud narrated it in al-Marasil from Harun ibn Abdullah, from Hammad ibn Mas'adah, from Ibn Jurayj. Harun said: And Ahmad, meaning Ibn Hanbal, said: It is in his book, meaning Ibn Jurayj: Usayd ibn Zuhayr; but thus he narrated to them in Basra. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Harun without mentioning the story."
"1361","1461 - As'ad ibn Sa'id informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Ibn Ridhah informed us, al-Tabarani informed us, Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Usayd ibn Hudayr, kunyah Abu Yahya, died in the year twenty, and 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, carried him between the two posts of the bier until he placed him in al-Baqi' and prayed over him. And one who died in the time of 'Umar, how could the days of Mu'awiyah reach him? Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from 'Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from 'Ikrimah ibn Khalid: that Usayd ibn Zuhayr informed him. Abu Mas'ud al-Razi narrated it from Hammad ibn Mas'adah without attributing Usayd. Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, saying: Usayd ibn Zuhayr."
"1362","Another, 1462 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us, there: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn al-Harish al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Bahrani narrated to us, Harami ibn 'Umarah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from Usayd ibn Hudayr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Ansar are my inner garment and my repository; people will increase while they decrease, so accept from their good-doers and overlook their wrongdoers. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ma'mar. Ghundar narrated it from Shu'bah, from the hadith of Anas, without mentioning Usayd. Thus al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it from Bundar, from Ghundar."
"1363","Another, 1463 - Abu Muhammad 'Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Sa'adat ibn Tirad informed us, with my reading to him in Baghdad - I said to him: al-Hafiz Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Nasir ibn 'Ali al-Salami informed you, with reading to him while you listened: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Saqr al-Anbari informed us, he said: Abu 'Ali al-Husayn ibn Maymun ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Ghaffar al-Sadafi informed you, with your reading to him - I said to him: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh al-Naysaburi informed you, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn 'Ali ibn Bahr al-Nasa'i narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us, from Shu'ayb, he said: al-Layth informed us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha' informed us, from Ibn Abi Hilal, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah, from Abdullah ibn Khabbab, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from Usayd ibn Hudayr, and he was of the people with the finest voice with the Qur'an, he said: I recited Surah al-Baqarah tonight while a horse of his was tied and my son Yahya lay near me as a boy, and it moved about, and I said: I have no concern but my son, and it calmed; then I recited and the horse moved, and I stood having no concern but my son; then I recited and the horse moved, and I raised my head and there was something like a canopy with what looked like lamps coming from the sky, and it frightened me so I stopped. In the morning I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: Recite, O Abu Yahya. I said: I did recite, O Messenger of Allah, and the horse moved, and I stood having no concern but my son. He said: Recite, O Abu Yahya. I said: I did recite, O Messenger of Allah, and the horse moved, having no concern but my son. He said: Recite, O Ibn Hudayr. He said: I did recite, and I raised my head and there was as it were a canopy with lamps in it, and it frightened me. He said: Those are the angels drawn near by your voice; had you recited until morning, people would have woken looking at them. Thus al-Nasa'i transmitted it in Fada'il al-Qur'an. Al-Bukhari narrated it by ta'liq from the musnad of Usayd, saying: And al-Layth said: Ibn al-Had narrated to me from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Usayd, and said at its end: Ibn al-Had said: And this hadith was narrated to me by Abdullah ibn Khabbab, from Abu Sa'id, from Usayd. I say: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim only heard it from Mahmud ibn Labid. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Hasan al-Hulwani and Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir, from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Yazid ibn al-Had, that Abdullah ibn Khabbab narrated to him that Abu Sa'id narrated to him: that Usayd ibn Hudayr, while one night reciting in his enclosure. He made it of the musnad of Abu Sa'id. I say, and Allah knows best: it more resembles the musnad of Usayd, for in the hadith he said: I went in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, while I last night... and mentioned it. Al-Nasa'i also narrated it from Ahmad ibn Sa'id, from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Abdullah ibn Khabbab, from Abu Sa'id, that Usayd. Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from 'Imran ibn Musa, from Hudbah ibn Khalid, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Usayd ibn Hudayr. I say: I do not know whether Ibn Abi Layla's hearing from Usayd is sound, for 'Abd al-Rahman was born in the caliphate of 'Umar while Usayd died in the lifetime of 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them."
"1364","Another, 1464 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Asbahan: that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, with reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Ali informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zahmawayh, who is Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Subayh al-Wasiti, narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Ibn Shafi', and he was a physician, he said: Usayd ibn Hudayr called me and I cut for him the sciatic vein. He said: He narrated to me two hadiths. He said: People of two houses of my people came to me, a house of Banu Zafar and a house of Banu Mu'awiyah, and said: Speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to apportion for us, or give us, or something like this. So I spoke to him, and he said: Yes, I apportion to each household among them half; and if Allah returns to us we return to them. He said: I said: May Allah reward you with good, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And you, may Allah reward you with good, for I know you only as chaste and patient."
"1365","1465 - He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You will meet favoritism after me. When 'Umar ibn al-Khattab distributed cloaks among the people, he sent me a cloak and I deemed it small and gave it to my son. While I was praying, a youth of Quraysh passed wearing a cloak of those cloaks trailing it, and I remembered the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You will meet favoritism after me. I said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. A man went to 'Umar and informed him, and he came while I was praying and said: Pray, O Usayd. When I finished my prayer he said: What did you say? I informed him. He said: That is a cloak I sent to so-and-so son of so-and-so, a Badri, Uhudi, 'Aqabi man; this youth came to him and bought it from him and wore it. Did you think that would be in my time? I said: By Allah, O Commander of the Believers, I thought that would not be in your time."
"1366","1466 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Fadl ibn al-'Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Bashshar ibn Musa al-Khaffaf narrated to us. 1467 - Al-Tabarani said: And al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Ma'mari narrated to us, Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr ibn Sa'd ibn Mu'adh, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Ibn Shafi', and he was a physician, he said: I cut the sciatic vein of Usayd ibn Hudayr, and he narrated to me two hadiths. He said: People of two houses of my people came to me and said: Speak for us to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to apportion for us of these dates. I came to him and spoke to him, and he said: Yes, we apportion to them, to each household half; and if Allah returns to us we return to them. I said: May Allah reward you from us with good. He said: And you, may Allah reward you from me, O company of Ansar, with good, for you, as I know you, are chaste and patient. You will meet favoritism after me, so be patient until you meet me. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili. Its end has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn 'Asim al-Mazini, and in al-Bukhari from the hadith of Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik."
"1367","Another, 1468 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us in Asbahan: that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, with reading to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abdullah informed us, Abdullah ibn Maslamah informed us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, from his father, from his grandfather 'Alqamah ibn Waqqas, from 'A'ishah, from Usayd ibn Hudayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Throne shook for the death of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh. 'A'ishah said: I heard this from Usayd ibn Hudayr while I was walking between him and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Isma'il also narrated it from Sa'id ibn Sulayman, from 'Abbad, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, similarly."
"1368","1469 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from 'A'ishah, from Usayd ibn Hudayr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Throne shook for the death of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh. Al-Tabarani also narrated it from 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, and from Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, from 'Umar al-Darir, all from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr, similarly. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Jabir ibn Abdullah and Anas ibn Malik. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from 'Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Sinan, from Muhammad ibn Qudamah, from 'Abdah ibn Sulayman, from Muhammad ibn 'Amr."
"1369","Another, 1470 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-'Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub and Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, they said: 'Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Uthman, from his mother Fatimah bint Husayn, from 'A'ishah, that she said: Usayd ibn Hudayr was of the most excellent people, and he would say: If I were as I am in one of three states, I would be of the people of Paradise and I would not doubt that: when I recite the Qur'an or when I hear it recited, and when I hear the sermon of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when I attend a funeral; and I never attended a funeral but I spoke to myself of naught but what is done with it and what it will come to. We did not rely in it upon Ibn Lahi'ah."
"1370","Another, 1471 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Usayd ibn Hudayr, he said: While he was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he had humor, entertaining the people to make them laugh, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poked him in the side, and he said: Let me retaliate. He said: Take retaliation. He said: You have a shirt on and I have no shirt on. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his shirt, and he embraced him and began kissing his side, saying: I only wanted this, O Messenger of Allah. Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan from 'Amr ibn 'Ali. I do not know whether the hearing of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Usayd ibn Hudayr is sound or not."
"1371","Musnad of Usayd ibn Zuhayr al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. Usayd ibn Zuhayr ibn Rafi' ibn 'Adi ibn Zayd ibn Jusham ibn Harithah ibn al-Harith al-Harithi Abu Thabit al-Harithi al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. 1472 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Asbahan: that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, with reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Harun ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far al-Ansari narrated to me, Abu al-Abrad, freedman of Banu Khatmah, narrated to us that he heard Usayd ibn Zuhayr al-Ansari: that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A prayer in the mosque of Quba' is like an 'umrah."
"1372","1473 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud ibn Rawh informed us, with reading to him while we listened in Asbahan - it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed you, with reading to her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. 1474 - Sulayman said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, Abu al-Abrad, freedman of Banu Khatmah, narrated to us that he heard Usayd ibn Zuhayr al-Ansari narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A prayer in the mosque of Quba' is like an 'umrah. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Kurayb and Sufyan ibn Waki', from Abu Usamah, and said: A hasan sahih hadith; we do not know for Usayd ibn Zuhayr anything sound except this hadith, and we know it only from the hadith of Abu Usamah; Abu al-Abrad's name is Ziyad, a Madinan. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah."
"1373","Another, 1475 - Abu al-Fath Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Kharaqi informed us, by ijazah: that Abu Muhammad 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them, with reading to him: Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar al-Dinawari informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni informed us, Abu 'Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn 'Ali al-Nasa'i informed us, 'Amr ibn Mansur informed us, Sa'id ibn Dhu'ayb narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: 'Ikrimah ibn Khalid informed me: that Usayd ibn Zuhayr al-Ansari, then one of Banu Harithah, informed him that he was over al-Yamamah, and that Marwan wrote: that Mu'awiyah wrote to him, that whichever man has a theft stolen from him, he is most entitled to it wherever he finds it. Then Marwan wrote of that to me, so I wrote to Marwan: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that when the one who bought it from the one who stole it is not accused, its master is given choice: if he wishes he takes what was stolen from him for its price, and if he wishes he follows his thief. Then Abu Bakr, 'Umar and 'Uthman judged likewise. Marwan sent my letter to Mu'awiyah, and Mu'awiyah wrote to Marwan: Neither you nor Usayd judge over me, but I judge over you in what I have charge of, so carry out what I ordered you. Marwan sent Mu'awiyah's letter, and I said: I will not judge while in charge by what Mu'awiyah said. Thus Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from 'Abd al-Razzaq. This hadith has preceded in the musnad of Usayd ibn Hudayr, and it is more properly by the narration of Usayd ibn Zuhayr; the discussion on it has preceded there."
"1374","Another, 1476 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us, there: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Na'ilah al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Rafi' ibn Usayd, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade leasing land. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn al-Harith. It was said: 'Umayr ibn 'Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated it from 'Abd al-Hamid, similarly. Mujahid narrated it from Usayd ibn Zuhayr, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, in the musnad of Rafi' ibn Khadij. Abu Dawud, Ibn Majah and al-Nasa'i narrated it from the narration of Mujahid."
"1375","Another, 1477 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-'Adawi al-Qirmiti al-Baghdadi, of the descendants of 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah, narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Ya'qub al-'Uthmani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated to us, Bashir ibn Thabit ibn Usayd ibn Zuhayr narrated to us; and in a narration: Husayn ibn Thabit, and he also narrated to me from his sister Su'da bint Thabit, from their father Thabit, from their grandfather Usayd ibn Zuhayr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) deemed Rafi' ibn Khadij too young on the day of Uhud, and his uncle Zuhayr, may Allah have mercy on him, said to him: O Messenger of Allah, he is a man who shoots. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him, and an arrow struck him in his throat area, and his uncle brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My nephew was struck by an arrow. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish that we remove it, we remove it; and if you wish to leave it, then if he dies with it in him he dies a martyr. Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated it from Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Husayn, from his father, from his grandfather, from Rafi' ibn Khadij: that he went out on the day of Uhud, and mentioned it."
"1376","Musnad of Usayr ibn 'Amr al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. Usayr ibn 'Amr ibn Qays al-Ansari, Abu Salit, a Badri, may Allah be pleased with him. 1478 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Bazzaz al-Tustari narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Uruzzi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Harun ibn Abi 'Isa narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, 'Abdullah ibn Damrah al-Fazari narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salit, from his father Abu Salit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the flesh of domestic donkeys while the pots boiled, so we overturned them on their faces."
"1377","1479 - And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, 'Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn Damrah al-Fazari, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salit, from his father Abu Salit, from his father Abu Salit, and he was a Badri, he said: The prohibition of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against eating the flesh of donkeys reached us while the pots boiled with them, so we overturned them on their faces."
"1378","1480 - Abu 'Ali 'Umar ibn 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Wa'iz al-Harbi informed us, there: that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn Damrah al-Fazari narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salit, from his father Abu Salit, he said: The prohibition of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against eating the flesh of domestic donkeys reached us while the pots boiled with them, so we overturned them on their faces."
"1379","1481 - And with it, my father narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah said: And I heard it, I from Ibn Abi Shaybah, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn Damrah al-Fazari, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salit, from his father Abu Salit, and he was a Badri, he said: The prohibition of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against the flesh of donkeys reached us while we were at Khaybar, so we overturned them though hungry."
"1380","1482 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us in Asbahan: that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, with reading to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim informed us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn Damrah al-Fazari, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salit, from his father Abu Salit, and he was a Badri, he said: The prohibition of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against the flesh of donkeys reached us while we were at Khaybar, and our pots boiled, so we overturned them on their faces. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1381","Musnad of Usayr, not attributed, may Allah be pleased with him. 1483 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Asbahan: that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, with reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Saminah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Dawud, from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, he said: I and a companion of mine entered upon a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Usayr, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty brings naught but good. Al-Hasan ibn Sufyan al-Basawi narrated it from Ibn Abi Saminah, from Yahya, from Abu 'Awanah, from Dawud ibn Abdullah."
"1382","Musnad of al-Ash'ath ibn Qays al-Kindi, may Allah be pleased with him. Al-Ash'ath ibn Qays ibn Ma'dikarib ibn Mu'awiyah ibn Jabalah al-Kindi Abu Muhammad. 1484 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us, there: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Sulaym al-Kindi narrated to us, Kurdus al-Tha'labi narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays al-Kindi: that a man of Kindah and a man of Hadramawt disputed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over land in Yemen. The Hadrami said: O Messenger of Allah, my land, his father usurped it. He said to the Kindi: What do you say? He said: I say my land is in my hand, I inherited it from my father. He said to the Hadrami: Have you proof? He said: No; but let him swear, O Messenger of Allah, by the One there is no god but He, that he does not know it is my land his father usurped. The Kindi prepared for the oath, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man cuts off wealth but he meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection leprous. So the Kindi returned it."
"1383","1485 - 'Umar ibn 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Wa'iz al-Harbi informed us, there: that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Kurdus narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays: that a man of Kindah and a man of Hadramawt disputed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over land in Yemen. The Hadrami said: O Messenger of Allah, my land, this man and his father usurped it. The Kindi said: O Messenger of Allah, my land, I inherited it from my father. The Hadrami said: O Messenger of Allah, make him swear that he does not know it is my land and my father's land his father usurped. The Kindi prepared for the oath, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant or man cuts off wealth by his oath but he meets Allah on the Day of Resurrection leprous. The Kindi said: It is his land and his father's land."
"1384","1486 - And with it, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Kurdus, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever swears a binding oath to cut off thereby the wealth of a Muslim man, while lying in it, meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, leprous. Abu Dawud narrated it from Mahmud ibn Khalid, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, from al-Harith ibn Sulayman. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from 'Imran ibn Musa ibn Mujashi', from 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Waki', similarly."
"1385","Another, 1487 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there: that Hibat Allah informed them, with reading to him: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Bahz and 'Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, 'Uqayl ibn Talhah narrated to me; 'Affan said in his hadith: 'Uqayl ibn Talhah al-Sulami informed us, from Muslim ibn Haytham, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, that he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a delegation of Kindah; 'Affan said: they did not deem me the best of them. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we claim you are of us? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are the sons of al-Nadr ibn Kinanah; we do not cast aspersion on our mother nor disown our father. Al-Ash'ath said: By Allah, I will not hear anyone deny Quraysh from al-Nadr ibn Kinanah but I flog him the hadd. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Hammad ibn Salamah."
"1386","1488 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Asbahan: that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, with reading to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abdullah informed us, Muslim, he is Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Uqayl ibn Talhah, from Muslim ibn Haytham, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of my people who did not deem me the best of them, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, we claim you are of us. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No; we are the sons of al-Nadr ibn Kinanah; we do not disown our father nor cast aspersion on our mother. Al-Ash'ath said: I will not hear anyone deny Quraysh from al-Nadr ibn Kinanah but I flog him."
"1387","1489 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim and 'Arim narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, 'Uqayl ibn Talhah al-Sulami narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Haytham, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, he said: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of Kindah who did not deem me the best of them, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, we claim you are of us? He said: No; we are the sons of al-Nadr ibn Kinanah; we do not cast aspersion on our mother nor disown our father. Al-Ash'ath ibn Qays said: O Prophet of Allah, I will not hear anyone deny Quraysh from Kinanah but I flog him. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Yazid ibn Harun; and from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Sulayman ibn Harb; and from Harun ibn Hayyan, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mughirah, all from Hammad ibn Salamah, similarly."
"1388","Another, 1490 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi informed us in Asbahan: that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them, with reading to him: 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yazid ibn Harun informed us, Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sharik, from 'Abd al-Rahman, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The most thankful of people to Allah are the most thankful of them to people."
"1389","1491 - As'ad ibn Sa'id informed us that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us. 1492 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sharik, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Adi al-Kindi, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most thankful of you to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, are the most thankful of you to people."
"1390","1493 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad: that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salm ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Ziyad ibn Kulayb, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He does not thank Allah who does not thank people. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Bahz, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Musarrif; and from Muhammad ibn Fudayl, from Ibn Shubrumah, from Abu Ma'shar, from al-Ash'ath. Abdullah ibn Sharik and Salm ibn 'Abd al-Rahman were criticized by some hadith scholars and declared trustworthy by others, and Allah knows best. Muslim transmitted from Salm in his Sahih."
"1391","Musnad of Asram, may Allah be pleased with him. 1494 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Hafs ibn 'Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Bashir ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Akhdari, from Asram, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I bought a slave, so supplicate to Allah for me for blessing and name him. He said: What is your name? I said: Asram. He said: Rather you are Zur'ah. He said: What do you want him for? He said: A cultivator. He said: Then he is 'Asim. It has preceded in the musnad of Usamah ibn Akhdari. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Bishr, in the musnad of Usamah; it has preceded, and in it 'a shepherd' instead of 'a cultivator'."
"1392","Musnad of Agharr ibn Yasar al-Muzani, may Allah be pleased with him. 1495 - As'ad ibn Sa'id informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibn Abi 'Atiq, from Nafi': that Ibn 'Umar informed him that al-Agharr, a man of Muzaynah who had companionship with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was owed wasqs of dates by a man of Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf, and he went to him repeatedly. He said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he sent Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, with me. He said: Everyone we met greeted us, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Do I not see people beginning you with greeting so they have the reward? Begin them with greeting so you have the reward. It was narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from al-Agharr, similarly."
"1393","Another, 1496 - Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr and As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Shabib Abu Rawh, from al-Agharr, of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he recited Surah al-Rum."
"1394","1497 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali ibn al-Ma'tush informed us in Baghdad: that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from Shabib ibn Abi Rawh, from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr and recited al-Rum in them, and the recitation became confused upon him; when he prayed he said: What is with men who attend prayer with us without purification? Those are the ones who confuse our prayer upon us. Whoever attends prayer with us, let him perfect purification."
"1395","1498 - And with it, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, he said: I heard Shabib Abu Rawh narrating from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he prayed Subh and recited al-Rum in it and made a mistake in it. He said: And what prevents me? Shu'bah said: He mentioned impurity, and the meaning of his saying is: you are not clean."
"1396","Another, 1499 - As'ad ibn Sa'id and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abi Karimah narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah narrated to us, from al-Agharr al-Muzani: that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, morning came upon me and I had not prayed witr. He said: Witr is but by night. He said: O Prophet of Allah, morning came upon me and I had not prayed witr. He said: Then pray witr."
"1397","Musnad of al-Aqra' ibn Habis al-Tamimi, may Allah be pleased with him. 1500 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud informed us in Asbahan, and Fatimah bint Sa'd al-Khayr in Cairo: that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jurdhaniyyah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas al-Mu'addib narrated to us, 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from al-Aqra' ibn Habis: that he called the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from behind the chambers, saying: O Muhammad, my praise is adornment and my blame is disgrace. He said: That is Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"1398","1501 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Khabbaz informed us in Asbahan: that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus and 'Uthman ibn Nasr ibn 'Abd al-Wahid ibn 'Ali al-Hulali al-Darir, it was read to them while they listened: Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Abdullah ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ja'far al-Sa'igh narrated to us. 1502 - Abu Bakr said: And Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ishaq al-Harbi narrated to us. 1503 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Musa ibn al-Walid narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, they said: 'Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from al-Aqra' ibn Habis: that he called the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from behind the chambers: O Muhammad, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not answer him. He said: O Muhammad, by Allah, my praise is adornment and my blame is disgrace. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah, that is Allah. Imam Ahmad narrated it from 'Affan ibn Muslim. 'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated it from Wuhayb, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Abu Salamah, from al-Aqra', once saying: al-Aqra', and mentioned the like."
"1399","Musnad of Aqram al-Khuza'i, may Allah be pleased with him. Aqram al-Khuza'i Abu Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him. 1504 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Asbahan: that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, with reading to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Dawud ibn Qays, he said: I heard 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Aqram narrating from his father, he said: My father narrated to me: that he was with his father at al-Qa' of Namirah, or he said: of Samurah, and a caravan passed and dismounted by the side of the road, and my father said to me: Son, stay with me until I draw near these people. He said: He drew near them and I drew near with him, and prayer was established, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among them. He said: I would look at the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whenever he prostrated."
"1400","1505 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Asbahan: that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, with reading to him: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Aqram al-Khuza'i, from his father, he said: I performed Hajj with my father until when we were at al-Qa' of Namirah, he said: A caravan passed us and dismounted by the side of the road. He said: My father said to me: Son, stay with your young sheep until these people come, then ask them. He said: He went out and I went out after him, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Prayer came and I was with him, looking at the whiteness of the two armpits of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whenever he prostrated. In the first hadith it is as if from the hadith of Aqram, and in this hadith Abdullah ibn Aqram; the well-known is this, and Allah knows best."
"1401","The sixteenth part of al-Ahadith al-Mukhtarah of al-Diya' al-Maqdisi. Musnad of Aktham ibn Abi al-Jawn al-Khuza'i, may Allah be pleased with him. Aktham ibn Abi al-Jawn, and it is said: Ibn al-Jawn, Abu Ma'bad al-Khuza'i, may Allah be pleased with him. 1506 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud al-Asbahani informed us, with reading to him while we listened in Asbahan - it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed you, with reading to her while you listened: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, 'Ali ibn Sa'id al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn 'Ali al-Ansari narrated to us, Damrah ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shawdhab, from Abu Nuhayk, from Shibl ibn Khulayd al-Muzani, from Aktham ibn Abi al-Jawn, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so suffices in fighting. He said: He is in the Fire. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, if so-and-so, with his worship, striving and gentleness, is in the Fire, where are we? He said: That is but the submission of hypocrisy, and he is in the Fire. He said: We watched him in fighting; no horseman or man passed him but he leapt upon him, and his wounds became many. We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so was martyred. He said: He is in the Fire. When the pain of wounds intensified upon him, he took his sword and placed it between his breasts, then leaned upon it until it came out of his back. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may act with the deeds of the people of Paradise though he is of the people of the Fire, and a man may act with the deeds of the people of the Fire though he is of the people of Paradise; wretchedness or felicity overtakes him at the departure of his soul, and he is sealed with it. This hadith has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Sahl ibn Sa'd and Abu Hurayrah."
"1402","Musnad of Umayyah ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Usayd al-Umawi. Umayyah ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Abi al-'Is ibn Usayd, may Allah be pleased with him. 1507 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from Umayyah ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Usayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would seek opening victory through the poor Muhajirun."
"1403","1508 - And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Umayyah ibn Khalid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would seek opening victory through the poor Muhajirun. Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah, from Umayyah ibn Khalid. It was said: Waki' narrated it from Sufyan, as the narration of Yahya ibn Sa'id; Sufyan did not mention al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah."
"1404","Musnad of Umayyah ibn Makhshi al-Khuza'i, may Allah be pleased with him. Umayyah ibn Makhshi al-Khuza'i Abu Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him. 1509 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad: that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Jabir ibn Subh narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Khuza'i narrated to me, and I accompanied him to Wasit, and he would name Allah at the first of his food, and at the last morsel say: In the name of Allah in its first and its last. I said to him: You name at the first of what you eat; what about your saying at the last of what you eat: In the name of Allah, its first and its last? He said: I inform you of that: my grandfather Umayyah ibn Makhshi, and he was of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), says: A man would eat while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked on, and he did not name until there remained of his food a morsel, and he said: In the name of Allah, its first and its last. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan kept eating with him until he named, and nothing remained in his stomach but he vomited it."
"1405","1510 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us in Asbahan: that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, with reading to him while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim informed us, Abu Sufyan 'Abd al-Rahim ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ibn Subh, from al-Muthanna ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Khuza'i, from his uncle Umayyah ibn Makhshi, and he had accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man would eat while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat, and he did not name, and Satan began eating with him; when naught remained of his food but a morsel he said: In the name of Allah in its first and its last. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: He, Satan kept eating with him; when he mentioned Allah, Satan vomited what was in his stomach."
"1406","1511 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, with reading to her: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Jabir ibn Subh narrated to me, al-Muthanna ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Khuza'i narrated to me, and I accompanied him to Wasit, and when he ate he would name, and when it came to the last morsel he said: In the name of Allah, its first and its last. I said to him concerning that, and he said: My grandfather Umayyah ibn Makhshi, and he was of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man would eat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not name; when it came to the last morsel he said: In the name of Allah, its first and its last. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan kept eating with him until he said: its first and its last, and Satan vomited all he ate."
"1407","1512 - And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Raja' ibn Subh narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from his uncle Umayyah ibn Makhshi, and he was of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat while a man ate, and he did not name until naught remained of his food but a morsel, and he said: In the name of Allah, its first and its last. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, then said: Satan kept eating with you; when you mentioned the name of Allah he vomited what was in his stomach. Abu Dawud narrated it from Mu'ammal ibn al-Fadl al-Harrani, from 'Isa ibn Yunus. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from 'Amr ibn 'Ali, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, similarly."
"1408","Musnad of Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him. In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful; praise be to Allah, good blessed praise as our Lord loves and is pleased, and as befits the nobility of His Face and the might of His majesty; and may Allah bless the seal of His prophets and the noblest of His chosen, Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet and the luminous lamp, and his family, and grant abundant peace. These are hadiths I selected from the hadith of Anas ibn Malik ibn al-Nadr ibn Damdam ibn Zayd ibn Haram ibn Jundub ibn 'Amir ibn Ghunm ibn 'Adi ibn al-Najjar, Abu Hamzah al-Bukhari al-Ansari, servant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet, of what neither al-Bukhari nor Muslim transmitted, may Allah be pleased with them. Ibrahim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Rabi'ah, from Anas, and he is the son of the daughter of Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr; al-Zuhri and others narrated from him. 1513 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us, there: that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Shaybani informed them, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Hamdan informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Rabi'ah, from his father, he said: We entered upon Anas ibn Malik while he prayed in a single garment wrapped, with his cloak placed aside. He said: I said to him: Do you pray in a single garment? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray thus. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Jabir ibn Abdullah and 'Umar ibn Abi Salamah."
"1409","Ibrahim ibn 'Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah ibn Rafi' al-Ansari, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him. 1514 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Mufti informed us in Asbahan: that Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah Abu Abdullah al-Katib narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'd al-Zuhri narrated to us, my uncle Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muslim, freedman of the family of Rifa'ah ibn Rafi' al-Ansari, narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn 'Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah ibn Rafi' narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Abu 'Ayyash Zayd ibn al-Samit, one of Banu Zurayq, having sat and said: O Allah, I ask You by that all praise is Yours; there is no god but You, O Bestower, O Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of majesty and honor. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a group of his companions with him: Do you know with what the man supplicated? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: He supplicated Allah by His greatest name, which when He is called by it He answers, and when asked by it He gives. It has been narrated from Anas by other paths. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi, from Salamah ibn al-Fadl, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muslim, from 'Asim, from Ibrahim ibn 'Ubayd, similarly, with the addition of 'Asim."
"1410","Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from his uncle Anas. 1515 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Asbahani informed us, there: that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abdullah Sammuyah informed us, Muhammad ibn Muqatil informed us, Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar informed us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to me, from Anas: that Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Teach me something I may supplicate with in my prayer. He said: Glorify Allah ten times, magnify Allah ten times, praise Him ten times, then ask Him what you wish; He says: Yes, yes."
"1411","1516 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn Abi 'Asim informed us, al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik: that Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Umm Sulaym said: Teach me words I may supplicate with in my prayer. He said: Magnify Allah ten times, glorify Allah ten times, praise Allah ten times, then ask what you wish; He says: Yes, yes. Waki' narrated it from 'Ikrimah, from Ishaq."
"1412","1517 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed us, Abu al-Muzaffar Sa'id ibn Mansur ibn Mis'ar al-Qushayri informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, my grandfather Imam Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Muhammad ibn Aban ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Waki' narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me words I may supplicate with in my prayer. He said: Glorify Allah ten times, praise Him ten times, magnify ten times, then ask Him your need; He says: Yes, yes."
"1413","1518 - Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn al-Saffar informed us in Nishapur: that Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Azhari informed us, Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Makhladi informed us, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hamid ibn Mansur al-Tusi informed us, Abdullah ibn Hashim narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas, he said: Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me words I say when I pray. He said: Glorify Allah ten times, praise Him ten times, magnify Him ten times, then ask Him your need; He says: Yes, yes. Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal transmitted it in his Musnad from Waki', 'Ikrimah narrated to me. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it in his book from Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi, from Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak. Al-Nasa'i transmitted it from 'Ubayd ibn Waki' ibn al-Jarrah, from his father, both from 'Ikrimah. Al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan gharib hadith. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban transmitted it in his book from Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah, from Muhammad ibn Aban, from Waki'."
"1414","Another hadith, 1519 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Asbahan: that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-Khallal al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Ali ibn 'Asim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Yunus al-Hanafi narrated to us, 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Friday would lean his back against a trunk set up in the mosque and address the people, and a Byzantine came to him and said: Shall I not make for you something you sit upon as though standing? He made for him a minbar with two steps, sitting upon the third. When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon the minbar, it bellowed like the bellowing of a bull until it shook with its bellowing, grieving for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended to it from the minbar and embraced it while it bellowed; when he embraced it, it fell silent. Then he said: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, had I not embraced it, it would have remained thus until the Resurrection, grieving for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered it buried."
"1415","1520 - Abu Rawh 'Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi al-Sufi informed us: that Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, my grandfather, meaning Muhammad ibn Ishaq, informed us, Bundar narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand on Friday leaning his back against a trunk set up in the mosque, and a Byzantine came and said: Shall we not make for you something you sit upon, meaning on it, as though standing? He made for him a minbar with two steps, sitting upon the third. When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon the minbar, the trunk bellowed like a bull until the mosque shook with its bellowing, grieving for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended to it from the minbar and embraced it while it bellowed; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) embraced it, it fell silent. Then he said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, had I not embraced it, it would have remained thus until the Hour, grieving for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered it buried. Imam Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Darimi al-Hafiz transmitted it from Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khalaf. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it in al-Manaqib from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, both from 'Umar ibn Yunus, saying: A sahih gharib hadith from this وجه. It has been narrated in the Sahih, the hadith of the trunk, from the narration of Ibn 'Umar and Jabir ibn Abdullah."
"1416","Another hadith, 1521 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Saydalani informed us in Asbahan: that Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, from Anas, he said: Hawazin came on the day of Hunayn, outnumbering the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with women, children, camels and sheep, and the Muslims were routed that day. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began saying: O company of Muhajirun, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger; O company of Muslims, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. Allah routed the polytheists without a spear thrust or an arrow shot. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that day: Whoever kills a polytheist, his spoils are his. Abu Talhah killed twenty men that day and took their spoils. Abu Qatadah said: I charged a man and struck him on the shoulder joint, and was turned aside from him, and upon him was armor; I looked to see who took it. A man said: I took it, O Messenger of Allah, so give it to me and compensate him from it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not be asked anything but he gave it or remained silent. 'Umar said: By Allah, Allah will not return it upon a lion of His lions then give it to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Umar spoke the truth."
"1417","1522 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us. 1523 - And Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Haddad Abu al-Qasim informed us in Asbahan: that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Simsar informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshid informed us by his word, Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated to us, Ya'qub, meaning al-Dawraqi, narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Hunayn: Whoever kills a man, his spoils are his. Abu Talhah killed twenty men that day and took their spoils. The wording is one, except that Ya'qub said: Abu Talhah killed that day. The story of the day of Hunayn has been transmitted in the Sahih from the hadith of Anas, without mentioning 'whoever kills a man', nor the story of Abu Qatadah from the narration of Anas, and Allah knows best. Al-Darimi transmitted the mention of 'whoever kills a man, his spoils are his' from Hajjaj ibn Minhal. Abu Dawud transmitted it in his Sunan from Musa ibn Isma'il, from Hammad. Imam Ahmad transmitted the hadith in full from 'Affan ibn Muslim, from Hammad ibn Salamah. Ibn Hibban al-Busti transmitted it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Hibban ibn Musa, from Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, from Hammad ibn Salamah; and from Abu Ya'la, from 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath, from Hammad ibn Salamah."
"1418","Another hadith, 1524 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Darir informed us, may Allah have mercy on him: that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Ali informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Hammam ibn Yahya, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought dates and began picking out things from them."
"1419","1525 - Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Baghdadi informed us in Fustat of Egypt: that Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn 'Umar al-Urmawi informed them, Abu al-Qasim 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Tustari informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-'Abbas al-Mukhallis informed us, Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought dates and began eating of them and picking out things from them."
"1420","1526 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us: that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought dates and began inspecting them."
"1421","1527 - 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-'Umari informed us in Baghdad: that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, Muhammad ibn Ghaylan informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shafi'i informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Sufi al-Madini narrated to us, Bistam ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, Hammam said: I heard him narrating from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought old dates and began inspecting them with his finger. Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated it from Salm ibn Qutaybah."
"1422","1528 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us in Asbahan: that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Ibrahim ibn 'Azrah al-Sami narrated to us, Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas, he said: I brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) old dates and he began inspecting them. Abu Dawud transmitted it from Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Jabalah, from Salim ibn Qutaybah, from Hammam, from Ishaq, from Anas; and from Muhammad ibn Kathir, from Hammam, from Ishaq as mursal. Ibn Majah narrated it from Bakr ibn Khalaf, from Salim. I say: This hadith was mentioned to Yahya ibn Ma'in, and he said: Waki' narrated it to us only as mursal. In sum: some narrated it connected and some mursal, and many hadiths come thus, and Allah knows best."
"1423","Another, 1529 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad entirely, and Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed them, they said: Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Ishaq al-Ansari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Harb narrated to us, Musa ibn Mas'ud Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas, he said: A man of the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we were in a house where our number was many and our wealth abundant, then we moved to another house where our number dwindled and our wealth lessened. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it, for it is blameworthy. Abu Dawud transmitted it in his Sunan from al-Hasan ibn Yahya, from Bishr ibn 'Umar, from 'Ikrimah."
"1424","Another, 1530 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Asbahan: that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Harun ibn Isma'il al-Khazzaz narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Ishaq ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Anas narrated to us, he said: A Bedouin came to the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He pressed his eye to the door's crevice, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him. He said: He took an arrow or a sharpened stick. He said: He aimed at the Bedouin's eye to gouge it, and the Bedouin ducked. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Had you remained still, I would have gouged your eye. Muslim transmitted something of its meaning from the hadith of 'Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Anas ibn Malik. In this is the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and not in that, and Allah knows best."
"1425","1531 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Asbahan: that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abdullah informed us, Muslim, he is Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, from Anas ibn Malik: that a Bedouin came to the door of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pressed his eye to the door's crevice, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him and aimed at him with an iron to gouge his eye; when he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he withdrew. He said: Had you remained still, I would have gouged your eye. Al-Nasa'i transmitted it from 'Amr ibn Mansur. Al-Tabarani narrated it from 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, both from Muslim ibn Ibrahim."
"1426","Another, 1532 - Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn 'Umar al-Naysaburi informed us, there: that Abu Bakr Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, by ijazah if not hearing: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Azhari informed us, Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Makhladi informed us, Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Isfarayini informed us, Musa ibn Sahl, he is Abu 'Imran al-Ramli, narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Hashim, meaning al-Bayruti, narrated to us, al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to me, from al-Awza'i, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A woman prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by night; when he prayed and sensed her, he prayed two rak'ahs and said to her: Lie down if you wish. She said: I feel energy. He said: You are not like me; the coolness of my eye has been placed in prayer."
"1427","1533 - 'Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim informed us in Asbahan: that Ja'far ibn 'Abd al-Wahid informed them, Abu Bakr ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, al-Fadl ibn al-'Abbas al-Qirtimi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn 'Uthman al-Harbi narrated to us, al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The coolness of my eye has been placed in prayer. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from al-Awza'i except Hiql; Yahya is alone in it. I say: Yahya is not alone in it, for 'Amr narrated it from him as we presented. Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Harun al-Bardiji, mentioning this hadith, said: The defect is from the narrator below al-Awza'i; he mentioned other than this from the narration of Ishaq from Anas, saying they are munkar though transmitted in the two Sahihs or one of them. Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated it from al-Awza'i, from Ishaq, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1428","Another, 1534 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us in Asbahan: that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them, Abu al-'Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man al-Jassas informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi 'Umar al-'Adani narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik: that Umm Sulaym said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry women of the Ansar? He said: They have jealousy. Some narrated it from Hammad, from Ishaq: that Umm Sulaym, making it mursal. I say: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated it like the narration of Bishr ibn al-Sari."
"1429","1535 - It was read to Shaykh Abu Talib al-Khadir ibn Hibat Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Tawus, in Ramadan of the year five hundred seventy-seven, while we listened in Damascus - Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami informed you, and he acknowledged it: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, he said: It was read to Qadi Abu Bakr Yusuf ibn al-Qasim ibn Yusuf ibn Faris al-Mayyanji, while I was present listening - it was said to him: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed you, with reading to him: Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry among the women of the Ansar? He said: They have jealousy. Al-Nasa'i transmitted it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl."
"1430","Another, 1536 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Mu'ammal narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would meet a man and say: O so-and-so, how are you? He would say: Well, I praise Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say to him: May Allah make you well. One day the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him and said: How are you, O so-and-so? He said: Well, if I am thankful. He fell silent toward him. He said: O Prophet of Allah, you used to ask me and say: May Allah make you well, and today you fell silent toward me. He said to him: I used to ask you and you said: Well, I praise Allah, so I said: May Allah make you well; and today you said: Well, if I am thankful, so I fell silent toward you. Al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ishaq, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as mursal."
"1431","Another, 1537 - Abu Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn 'Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us in his book: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us, with reading to him: Abu Nu'aym informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Ja'far al-Ramli narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by the structure of a dome of a man of the Ansar and said: What is this? They said: A dome. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every building, and he gestured with his hand thus over his head, more than this is a calamity upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection. Al-Tabarani said: al-Walid is alone in it."
"1432","Another, 1538 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us in Asbahan: that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us, Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani informed us, Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Musa narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. Al-Qasim ibn Musa: Abu Hatim ibn Hibban mentioned him in the Book of Trustworthy, saying: He narrated from al-Awza'i; Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Tabba' narrated from him."
"1433","Another hadith, 1539 - Abu al-Fadl Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us in Baghdad: that Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn Yusuf al-Azhari informed them, Jabir ibn Yasin ibn Mahmawayh al-'Attar informed us, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad, he is Ibn Ziyad al-Naysaburi, narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Sa'id ibn Muslim narrated to me, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man leaves his house and says: In the name of Allah, I place trust in Allah; there is no power nor strength except by Allah. He said: It is said: It suffices you; you are guided and protected, and Satan turns aside from him; and another devil says: How can you with a man guided, sufficed and protected? Abu Dawud transmitted it from Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Khath'ami. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in deeds of day and night from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Tamim, both from Hajjaj."
"1434","1540 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Ya'la Ishaq ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sabuni informed us, Abu Muhammad 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shurayh al-Ansari al-Zahid informed us, Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Hashimi informed us, Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: In the name of Allah, I place trust in Allah; there is no power nor strength except by Allah, it is said then: You are sufficed and protected, and Satan turns aside from him. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Sa'id ibn Yahya, saying: A hasan gharib hadith; we know it only from this وجه."
"1435","1541 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us, al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed us, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: In the name of Allah, I place trust in Allah; there is no power nor strength except by Allah, it is said then: You are sufficed and protected, and Satan turns aside from him. Al-Bukhari said: I do not know for Ibn Jurayj from Ishaq except this hadith, nor do I know his hearing from him. Al-Daraqutni said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi and Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, saying: I was narrated from Ishaq; the sound view is that Ibn Jurayj did not hear it from Ishaq. I say: Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, from Ishaq; it occurred in our hearing from the narration of Yahya ibn Sa'id: Ishaq informed me, and Allah knows best."
"1436","Isma'il ibn 'Ubayd Allah, from Anas. 1542 - Abu al-Mu'ammar Naqa' ibn 'Umar ibn Hunnadh informed us, with reading to him in Baghdad: that Abu Ghalib Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them, Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hassnun al-Narsi informed us, Abu al-Qasim Musa ibn 'Isa ibn Abdullah al-Sarraj informed us, Abdullah, he is Ibn Abi Dawud, narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Isma'il ibn 'Ubayd Allah, he said: Anas ibn Malik came to al-Walid ibn 'Abd al-Malik, and al-Walid said to him: What did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning the Hour? He narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am not of the world nor is it of me; I was sent while the Hour and I race."
"1437","1543 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there: that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to me, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, Isma'il ibn 'Ubayd Allah narrated to me, he said: Anas ibn Malik came to al-Walid ibn 'Abd al-Malik and he asked him: What did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning the Hour? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You and the Hour are like two. It has been narrated in the Sahih: I was sent, I and the Hour like these two, from the hadith of Anas."
"1438","Akhshan al-Sadusi from Anas. 1544 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad: that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Abu 'Ubaydah, meaning 'Abd al-Mu'min ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Sadusi, narrated to us, Akhshan al-Sadusi narrated to me, he said: I entered upon Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, or: By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you erred until your sins filled what is between heaven and earth, then sought Allah's forgiveness, He would forgive you. By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, or: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, if you did not err, Allah would bring a people who err, then seek Allah's forgiveness and He forgives them."
"1439","1545 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, 'Abd al-Mu'min ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Akhshan al-Sadusi narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, if you erred until your sins filled what is between earth and heaven, then sought Allah's forgiveness, He would forgive you. By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, if you did not err, Allah would bring a people who err, then seek forgiveness and He forgives them."
"1440","Azhar ibn Rashid from Anas. 1546 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi al-Asbahani informed us, there: that al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, al-'Awwam narrated to us, from al-Azhar ibn Rashid, he said: They would come to Anas, and when he narrated to them a hadith whose meaning they did not know, they came to al-Hasan and he explained it to them. He said: One day he narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Do not seek light by the fire of the polytheist, nor engrave Arabic upon your rings. They did not know what it was, so they came to al-Hasan and said to him: Anas narrated to us a hadith we do not know. He said: What did Anas narrate to you? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not seek light by the fire of the polytheist, nor engrave Arabic upon your rings. Al-Hasan said: As for his saying 'Do not engrave Arabic upon your rings': Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and as for his saying 'Do not seek light by the fire of the polytheist', he says: Do not consult the polytheists in your affairs. Then al-Hasan, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Its attestation in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: O you who believe, do not take intimates besides yourselves. Al-Nasa'i transmitted it from Mujahid ibn Musa, from Hushaym, similarly."
"1441","Ash'ath ibn Abdullah al-Huddani from Anas. 1547 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ash'ath ibn Abdullah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while people were with him, and a man among those with him said: I love this man. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you inform him? He said: No. He said: Stand and inform him. He stood to him and informed him, and he said: May the One for whom you loved me love you. Then he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of what he said. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are with whom you love, and for you is what you intended."
"1442","1548 - 'Abd al-Rahim ibn 'Abd al-Karim al-Sam'ani informed us, 'Abd al-Khaliq ibn Zahir al-Shahhami informed us, 'Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Mahmi informed us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Sharqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Abdullah, from Anas ibn Malik, with the like, and in it: Did you not inform him; and in it he said: Then he returned and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him and he informed him, and the rest is like it."
"1443","Another hadith, 1549 - 'Uthman ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Bakr, known as Habbubah al-Asbahani, informed us, there: that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them, Abu 'Amr 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Abdullah ibn Mandah informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshid informed us by his word, Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated to us, brother of Karkhawayh, he is Muhammad ibn Yazid, informed us, Sulayman ibn Harb informed us, from Bistam ibn Hurayth, from Ash'ath al-Huddani, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my ummah. Abu Dawud narrated it from Sulayman ibn Harb. It has been narrated from Humayd, from Anas."
"1444","Anas ibn Sirin from Anas. 1550 - Mu'awiyah ibn 'Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us, by ijazah: that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nu'aym informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking and eating in vessels of gold and silver."
"1445","1551 - Abu al-Ma'ali Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Sabir al-Sulami informed us, by permission, and my brother Imam Scholar Abu al-'Abbas Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us from him: that Sharif Abu al-Qasim 'Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn al-'Abbas al-Husayni informed them, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Ahmad al-Kinani informed us, Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn 'Awf ibn Ahmad ibn 'Awf informed us, Abu al-Qasim al-Fadl ibn Ja'far al-Mu'adhdhin informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abdous al-Naysaburi informed us in al-Ramlah, Ahmad ibn Hafs ibn Abdullah ibn Rashid al-Naysaburi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to me, from al-Hajjaj, he is Ibn al-Hajjaj, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating and drinking in vessels of gold and silver. Al-Nasa'i transmitted it from Ahmad ibn Hafs. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Hudhayfah."
"1446","Another, 1552 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Asbahan: that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Aban Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Kufi narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Abu Khuzaymah. 1553 - And al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad: that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Abu Khuzaymah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: O Allah, I ask You by that all praise is Yours; there is no god but You alone without partner; the Bestower, Originator of the heavens and earth, Possessor of majesty and honor. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have asked Allah, Blessed and Exalted, by His greatest name, which when He is called by it He answers, and when asked by it He gives. The wording is Ahmad's, and Abdullah ibn 'Umar said: He asked by His greatest name, and the rest is like it. Ibn Majah narrated it from 'Ali ibn Muhammad, from Waki'. I say: Abu Khuzaymah's name is Yusuf ibn Maymun al-Sabbagh; he was criticized, but this is a witness to the narration of others."
"1447","Another, 1554 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad informed us in al-Harbiyyah: that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would describe for sciatica the fat of the tail of an Arab black ram, neither large nor small, divided into three parts, melted, drinking each day a part."
"1448","1555 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Abu Abdullah al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Hisham, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered one with sciatica to take the tail fat of an Arab ram, neither small nor large, cut it small, then divide it into three parts, drinking each day a part."
"1449","1556 - Abu Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn 'Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us, by ijazah: that Abu 'Ali al-Haddad informed them, Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn Yazid al-Bahrani narrated to us, 'Abd al-Khaliq ibn Abi al-Mukhariq narrated to us, Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning sciatica: The tail fat of an Arab ram is taken, neither small nor large, melted, drinking it three days on an empty stomach. Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Anas ibn Sirin, from his brother Ma'bad ibn Sirin, from a man of the Ansar, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1450","Burayd ibn Abi Maryam Malik ibn Rabi'ah al-Saluli, from Anas. 1557 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us: that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abdullah informed us, Abu Nu'aym informed us, Yunus, he is Ibn Abi Ishaq, narrated to us, Burayd ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim ever asks Allah for Paradise three times but Paradise says: O Allah, admit him to Paradise; and none seeks refuge from the Fire three times but the Fire says: O Allah, save him."
"1451","1558 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Karam ibn Abi Yasir informed us, on the western side of Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn informed them, it being read to him: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafii informed us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks Allah, mighty and majestic, for Paradise three times, Paradise says: O Allah, admit him into Paradise; and whoever seeks refuge from the Fire three times, the Fire says: O Allah, grant him refuge from the Fire."
"1452","1559 - Abu al-Fadl Ismail ibn Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Janzawi informed us, it being read to him while we were listening in Damascus; it was said to him: Yaqub ibn Abd Allah the merchant informed you: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Said narrated to us, Luwayn narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks Allah for Paradise three times, Paradise says: O Allah, admit him into Paradise; and whoever seeks refuge with Allah from the Fire, the Fire says: O Allah, grant him refuge from the Fire. Imam Yahya ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated it from Abu al-Ahwas."
"1453","1560 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Darir informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abd al-Ala, that is Ibn Hammad, narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks Allah for Paradise three times, Paradise says: O Allah, admit him into Paradise; and whoever seeks refuge with Allah from the Fire three times, the Fire says: O Allah, grant him refuge from me. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Aswad ibn Amir and Qurran ibn Tammam, from Yunus. Al-Tirmidhi, al-Nasai, and Ibn Majah all transmitted it from Hannad ibn al-Sari, from Abu al-Ahwas; except that al-Nasai narrated it in the Book of Day and Night Deeds, and he narrated it in the Book of Seeking Refuge from Qutaybah ibn Said, from Abu al-Ahwas. Al-Tirmidhi said: Some narrated it as the statement of Anas. Abu Hatim al-Busti transmitted it from Ibn al-Junayd, from Qutaybah; and from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khalil, from Abu Kurayb: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Yunus."
"1454","Another hadith 1561 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us, in Isfahan, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Supplication is not rejected between the adhan and the iqamah, so supplicate."
"1455","1562 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us, in Baghdad, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Hasan al-Qazzaz informed them: the noble Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Muhtadi Billah informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Dust al-Allaf narrated to us from dictation: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Supplication is not rejected between the adhan and the iqamah, so supplicate."
"1456","1563 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi informed them, he being present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is not rejected. Al-Nasai narrated it in the Book of Day and Night Deeds from Ismail ibn Masud. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban transmitted it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili, from Muhammad ibn al-Minhal al-Darir, both from Yazid ibn Zuray, from Israil. Yunus narrated it from Burayd. Talq ibn Ghannam narrated from al-Masudi, from Yazid al-Faqir, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar to this."
"1457","Another hadith 1564 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us: that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Yunus ibn Amr, meaning Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik (hawalah)."
"1458","1565 - Ahmad said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, Burayd ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (hawalah)."
"1459","1566 - The hafiz Abu Ubayd Allah Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ghanim informed us, in Isfahan, he said: Abu Rashid Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Amr informed us: al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us: Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Fakihi informed us, in Makkah: Abu Yahya Abd Allah ibn Abi Masarrah narrated to us, Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam al-Saluli who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs one prayer, Allah sends ten prayers upon him and removes ten sins from him. The wording is one, and in the narration of Khallad: and they shall be removed. Abu Ishaq narrated it from Burayd."
"1460","1567 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: al-Azraq ibn Ali Abu al-Jahm narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever mentions me, let him send blessings upon me; and whoever sends one blessing upon me, I send ten blessings upon him. Al-Nasai transmitted it in the Book of Day and Night Deeds through routes to Yunus, from Burayd, from Anas. He narrated it from Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad, from Makhlad ibn Yazid, from Yunus, from Burayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas. I say: the narration of those who narrated it from Burayd, from Anas, is preferable, because he mentioned hearing from him, and Allah knows best. We have written it in the narration of al-Hasan from Anas. Muhammad ibn Yusuf and Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated it from Yunus, from Burayd, from Anas."
"1461","1568 - It was read to Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi, while we were listening in Damascus: Abu al-Majd Maali ibn Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Thalabi informed you, it being read to him: Abu al-Faraj Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini informed us: Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Munir al-Khallal informed us, it being read to him: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh al-Naysaburi informed us, it being read to him, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb ibn Ali ibn Sinan ibn Bahr al-Nasai informed us: Ishaq ibn Mansur informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed us: Yunus narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam who said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten prayers upon him, ten sins are removed from him, and ten ranks are raised for him."
"1462","1569 - And with the same chain, Abu Abd al-Rahman informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Tamim informed us: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Yunus, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of it exactly. Muslim narrated in his Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten blessings upon him."
"1463","Another 1570 - It was read to the judge Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari, while we were listening in Baghdad: The judge Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Bazzaz informed you, you listening, and he acknowledged it: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us: Abu al-Qasim Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Musa al-Kharaqi informed us: Abu Bakr Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Mustafad al-Firyabi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani Abu Muhammad narrated to us, in Tarsus: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Raqabah, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he broke his fast would begin with dates. Al-Daraqutni said: Raqabah ibn Masqalah narrates it from Burayd, from Anas; and Shubah differed from him, narrating it from Burayd, that he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)... as mursal; and it is likely that Raqabah preserved it."
"1464","Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani from Anas 1571 - Abu al-Maali Muhammad ibn Safi ibn Abd Allah al-Naqqash informed us, in Baghdad, may Allah have mercy on him, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Muqri, known as al-Mazrafi, informed them: the noble Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Samad ibn al-Muhtadi Billah narrated to us from his wording: Abu al-Qasim Idris ibn Ali ibn Ishaq ibn Yaqub al-Muaddib narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Harun al-Hadrami narrated to us: Yahya ibn Hakim Abu Said narrated to us: Abu Qutaybah Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Said ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah the Exalted said: My servant, as long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I shall forgive you for whatever you have done; and if you were to meet Me with sins filling the earth, I would meet you with its fill of forgiveness; and if you were to err until your sins reached the clouds of the sky, then sought My forgiveness, I would forgive you and I would not care."
"1465","1572 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, in Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him, that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, he being present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us: Abu Qutaybah narrated to us: Said ibn Ubayd al-Hunai narrated to us: Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord said: My servant, as long as you call upon Me and hope in Me, I forgive you for whatever is in you. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it in full from Abd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Jawhari, from Abu Asim, from Kathir ibn Fayid, from Said ibn Ubayd who said: I heard Bakr ibn Abd Allah say: Anas narrated to us; and he said: a hasan gharib hadith, we know it only from this route. Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated it from Said ibn Ubayd."
"1466","Another 1573 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, in Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Abu Nuaym informed us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Said ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to me: that Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani narrated to him, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey with his Companions, and fasting became hard for them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a vessel containing water and drank while he was upon his mount, with the people looking at him."
"1467","Another 1574 - The jurist Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Saffar informed us, in Naysabur, that his grandfather Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur informed them, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Khalaf informed us: al-Hakim Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih informed us: Ahmad ibn Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us: Khalaf ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says when he goes to his bed: Praise be to Allah who sufficed me and sheltered me; praise be to Allah who fed me and gave me drink; praise be to Allah who bestowed favor upon me and gave abundantly; O Allah, I ask You by Your might to save me from the Fire, then he has praised Allah with all the praises of all creation."
"1468","1575 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Tahir ibn Makki al-Harawani informed us, that Said al-Khayr ibn Muhammad al-Ansari informed them: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad al-Duni informed us: Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sunni informed us: Jafar ibn Isa al-Hulwani informed me: Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir ibn Jabalah narrated to us: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us: Khalaf ibn al-Mundhir Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us: Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says when he goes to his bed: Praise be to Allah who sufficed me and sheltered me, and praise be to Allah who fed me and gave me drink, and praise be to Allah who bestowed favor upon me, and I ask You by Your might to save me from the Fire, except that he has praised Allah, mighty and majestic, with the praises of all creation. Khalaf ibn al-Mundhir: Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him and did not mention any criticism of him. Muslim narrated in his Sahih from the narration of Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he went to his bed he would say: Praise be to Allah who fed us and gave us drink and sheltered us; how many are there who have none to suffice them nor shelter them. And in the hadith we narrated there is an addition over what is in Muslim."
"1469","Bukayr ibn Wahb al-Jazari from Anas 1576 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us, in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Waki narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, from Sahl Abu Asad, from Bukayr al-Jazari, from Anas who said: We were in the house of a man of the Ansar when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and stood, and took hold of the two doorposts, and said: The leaders are from Quraysh; they have a right over you, and you have the like of that over them, as long as when mercy is sought from them they show mercy, and when they judge they are just, and when they covenant they fulfill; so whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Sahl was declared trustworthy by Yahya ibn Main. I say: Shubah narrated it from him, and he used to call him Ali, and I think he used to err in his name, and Allah knows best."
"1470","Bayan al-Raqashi Abu Said or Sinan from Anas 1577 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Tawil narrated to us: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: A man called Bayan narrated to me, he said: I said to Anas: Narrate to me the timing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for prayer. He said: He used to pray Zhuhr at the decline of the sun, and pray Asr between your first prayer and Asr, and pray Maghrib at the setting of the sun, and pray Isha at the setting of the twilight, and pray Fajr at dawn when sight becomes clear; all between these two is time, or he said: is prayer."
"1471","1578 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, in Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abd Allah ibn Sammuwayh narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi narrated to us: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Bayan al-Raqashi say: I said to Anas ibn Malik: Narrate to me about the timing of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for prayer. He said: He used to pray Zhuhr when the sun declined, and pray Asr between your prayers, and pray Maghrib at sunset, and pray Isha at the disappearance of the twilight, and pray Fajr at dawn until sight becomes clear; all of that is time, or: all between that is time."
"1472","1579 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Bayan Abu Sinan, our neighbor, narrated to us, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik, I said: O Abu Hamzah, inform me of the timing of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for prayer, and he mentioned the like of it. Umayyah ibn Bistam also narrated it from Mutamir."
"1473","Bilal ibn Mirdas, also said Ibn Abi Musa al-Fazari, from Anas 1580 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Husayn, that is Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us: Israil narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala who said: I heard Bilal say: I heard Anas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever seeks judgeship and seeks help for it is entrusted to it; and whoever does not seek it nor seek help for it, Allah sends down to him an angel to guide him aright. Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr narrated it, from Yahya ibn Hammad, from Abu Awanah, from Abd al-Ala, from Bilal ibn Mirdas, from Khaythamah, from Anas."
"1474","1581 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, he being present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Waki narrated to us, from Israil, from Abd al-Ala, from Bilal ibn Abi Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks for judgeship is entrusted to himself; and whoever is compelled to it, an angel descends upon him to guide him aright. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Waki. Abu Dawud transmitted it from Muhammad ibn Kathir. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Hannad, from Waki. Ibn Majah transmitted it from Muhammad ibn Ismail and Ali ibn Muhammad, both from Waki, all of them from Israil. In the narration of Ibn Kathir, Bilal is not given a lineage. In the narration of Waki and al-Aswad ibn Amir: Ibn Abi Musa."
"1475","Tawbah ibn Kaysan al-Anbari al-Basri from Anas 1582 - Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Maali ibn Ghanimah ibn al-Hasan, known as Ibn Munina at Bab al-Basrah, informed us, that Abu al-Badr Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit informed us: Abu Umar al-Qasim ibn Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Hashimi informed us: Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Amr al-Lului informed us: Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashath narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn al-Hubab, from Muti ibn Rashid, from Tawbah al-Anbari that he heard Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank milk and did not rinse his mouth nor perform ablution, and prayed. Zayd said: Shubah directed me to this shaykh. Ali ibn al-Madini narrated it from Zayd ibn al-Hubab, from Muti ibn Rashid al-Basri who said: Tawbah al-Anbari narrated to us: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us."
"1476","Thabit ibn Aslam al-Bunani from Anas; Thawwab ibn Hujayl from Thabit 1583 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi informed us in his book: Abu Abd Allah ibn Mandah informed us: Abu Amr Ahmad ibn Muhammad, that is Ibn Ibrahim ibn Hakim al-Madini, narrated to us: Uthman, that is Ibn Khurrazadh, narrated to us: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us: Thawwab ibn Hujayl narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit narrate from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing you will lose of your religion is trustworthiness, then prayer."
"1477","Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai from Thabit 1584 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us, that Yahya ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Tarrah informed them: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn al-Fadl al-Makhbazi informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Hababah informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Nayruz informed us: Abu Yaqub Ishaq ibn al-Dayf narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman informed us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked, when he broke his fast, to break it with milk; if he did not find it, then dates; if he did not find it, he sipped sips of water."
"1478","1585 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Thabit narrated to me, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to break his fast with fresh dates before praying; if there were no fresh dates, then dry dates; if there were no dates, he sipped sips of water."
"1479","1586 - Abu al-Futuh Masud ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Karim al-Daqqaq informed us, at Bab al-Basrah in Baghdad, that Abu al-Qasim Ismail ibn Umar al-Samarqandi informed them: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Naqqur informed us: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn ibn Harun al-Daqqaq informed us: Yahya, that is Ibn Muhammad ibn Said, narrated to us: Muhanna ibn Yahya al-Shami Abu Abd Allah narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammam narrated to us, and I met him in the year 198, from Jafar ibn Sulayman, from Thabit, from Anas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast, he broke it with dates or fresh dates; and if there were none, he sipped sips of water. Abu Dawud transmitted it from Ahmad ibn Hanbal. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rafi, from Abd al-Razzaq, and said: a hasan gharib hadith. Al-Daraqutni transmitted it in his book from Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Said, from Muhanna."
"1480","Another 1587 - Abu Hamid Abd Allah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit informed us, in Baghdad, that Yahya ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Tarrah informed them: Abu al-Ghanaim Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mamun informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Ishaq ibn Hababah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us: Harun ibn Abd Allah narrated to me: Sayyar narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a youth who was dying, and said to him: How do you find yourself? He said: I hope in Allah, O Messenger of Allah, and I fear my sins. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These two do not gather in the heart of a servant in such a situation except that Allah gives him what he hopes for and secures him from what he fears."
"1481","1588 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abi Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Fath al-Nahrawani informed us, in Baghdad, that Sad al-Khayr ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Ansari informed them: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad al-Duni informed us: Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Kassar informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sunni informed us: Abu Yala informed us: al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Shaqiq narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, I think from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a man visiting him while he was dying, and greeted him. He said: How do you find yourself? And he mentioned it. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it in his book, and al-Nasai in the Book of Day and Night Deeds, both from Harun ibn Abd Allah. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sayyar. Al-Tirmidhi said: a gharib hadith. He said: Some narrated this from Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as mursal. Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Fahm narrated it from Sulayman ibn Ayyub, the companion of al-Basri, from Jafar ibn Sulayman, as marfu."
"1482","1589 - Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Urmawi informed us of it by ijazah: that Muhammad ibn Umar informed them: the judge Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn al-Muhtadi Billah narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Khadir ibn Masrur al-Muaddil informed us: Ismail, that is Ibn Ali al-Khatabi, narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Fahm narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ayyub, the companion of al-Basri, narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, and he mentioned it."
"1483","Another 1590 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh, that is Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik, narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman informed us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah in the Umrat al-Qada while Ibn Rawahah was before him saying: Clear the way for his beloved. Umar said: O Ibn Rawahah, in the sanctuary of Allah and before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do you speak this poetry? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him alone, O Umar; by Him in whose hand is my soul, his words are harsher upon them than the striking of arrows."
"1484","1591 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there, that Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu al-Muzaffar Said ibn Mansur al-Qushayri informed us: Abu Tahir ibn Khuzaymah, that is Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq, informed us: my grandfather, meaning Muhammad ibn Ishaq, informed us: Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman informed us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah entered Makkah performing Umrah before conquering it, while Ibn Rawahah walked before him saying: Clear the way for his beloved. Umar said: O Ibn Rawahah, in the sanctuary of Allah and before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do you speak this poetry? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him alone, O Umar; by Him in whose hand is my soul, his words are harsher upon them than the striking of arrows. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq similarly. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it in the Book of Seeking Permission from Ishaq ibn Mansur. Al-Nasai transmitted it in Hajj from Khushaysh ibn Asram al-Nasai and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh, all three from Abd al-Razzaq. Al-Tirmidhi said: a hasan sahih gharib hadith from this route. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami, from Jafar."
"1485","Another 1592 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Bishr, meaning Ibn Hilal, and Ubayd Allah, that is al-Qawariri, narrated to us, they said: Jafar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: When the day came on which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Madinah, everything in it lit up; and when the day came on which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, everything in it darkened; and we had not yet removed our hands from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while we were burying him, before we found our hearts changed. The wording is that of Bashir, and in the narration of Ubayd Allah: Thabit narrated to us. Al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah transmitted it from Bishr ibn Hilal al-Sawwaf. Al-Tirmidhi said: a sahih gharib hadith."
"1486","1593 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, in Isfahan, that Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi informed them, he being present: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan al-Araj informed us: Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Abu Kamil narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: When the day came on which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Madinah, everything in it lit up; and when the day came in which he was taken, everything in it darkened."
"1487","1594 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Sayyar narrated to us: Jafar narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: When the day came in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Madinah, everything in Madinah lit up; and when the day came in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, everything in Madinah darkened; and we had not finished his burial before we found our hearts changed. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Affan, from Jafar. Abd ibn Humayd transmitted it from Abu al-Walid, from Jafar. It was also narrated from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit."
"1488","Another 1595 - The imam Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Naja ibn Ghannam al-Waiz informed us, with my reading to him between Cairo and Egypt; I said to him: Abu Sabir Abd al-Sabur ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Fudayl al-Harawi informed you, it being read to him while you were listening, and he acknowledged it: Abu Amir Mahmud ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Azdi informed us: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Jarrahi informed us: al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahbub narrated to us: Abu Isa Muhammad ibn Sawrah al-Tirmidhi informed us: Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us: Sayyar narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit and Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a disheveled, dusty one with two worn garments, to whom no attention is paid, if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill it; among them is al-Bara ibn Malik. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, and said: a hasan gharib hadith. Hammad narrated it from Thabit without saying: among them is al-Bara."
"1489","1596 - Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sabbagh informed us, in Isfahan, that Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Umar al-Muadhdhin informed them, it being read to him: Abu Amr Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Abd Allah ibn Mandah informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yuwh informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Umar informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Dunya narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us: Sayyar ibn Hatim narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Sulayman, from Thabit and Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a disheveled, dusty one with two worn garments, to whom no attention is paid, if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill it; among them: al-Bara ibn Malik."
"1490","Another 1597 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abi Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Fath al-Nahrawani informed us, in Baghdad, that Abu al-Hasan Sad al-Khayr ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Ansari informed them, it being read to him: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad al-Duni informed us: Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Sunni informed us: Ibn Mani informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ismail al-Wasiti narrated to us: Sayyar ibn Hatim narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Sulayman, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I intend a journey, so provide me. He said: May Allah provide you with piety. He said: Give me more. He said: And may He forgive your sin. He said: Give me more. He said: And may He direct you to good wherever you are."
"1491","1598 - Abu Hamid Abd Allah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit ibn Zayd ibn al-Wakil informed us, in Baghdad, that Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Naqqur informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Dibaji informed us: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Buhturi narrated to us from dictation: Isa ibn Abd Allah al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Yazid ibn Umar ibn Janzah al-Madaini narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I intend a journey, so provide me. He said: May Allah provide you with piety. He said: Give me more. He said: And may He forgive you. He said: Give me more. He said: And may He direct you to good wherever you turn. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it in the Book of Supplications from Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sayyar, from Jafar similarly."
"1492","Another 1599 - Abu al-Fath Umar ibn Ali ibn Mahmud ibn Hammuyah al-Sufi informed us, in Damascus in the year 577: that Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed them: Abu Said al-Khashshab Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Muhammad al-Makhladi informed us: Abu al-Abbas al-Thaqafi al-Sarraj informed us (hawalah). 1600 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us, in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn informed them: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ghaylan informed us, he said: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Muzakki al-Naysaburi informed us, he said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sarraj informed us (hawalah). 1601 - Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ahmad al-Muadhdhin informed us, in Isfahan, that Ismail ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Sufi informed them: Abu Mansur Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Hid, who came to us, informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khaffaf informed us, he said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit. And al-Muzakki said: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not store anything for tomorrow. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Qutaybah, and said: a gharib hadith. Ibn Hibban transmitted it from al-Sarraj, from Qutaybah. It was narrated from Jafar, from Thabit, as mursal."
"1493","Another 1602 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there, that Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn al-Fudayl al-Fudayli informed them: Muhallim ibn Ismail al-Dabbi informed us: al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi al-Sarraj informed us: Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit the Ansar, greet their children, wipe their heads, and supplicate for them."
"1494","1603 - Abu Ismail Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mashadhah informed us, in Isfahan, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Said ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Sufi, among others, informed us, they said: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Makhladi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Said informed us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit the Ansar, greet their children, and wipe their heads. Al-Nasai transmitted it from Qutaybah."
"1495","1604 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us of it, in Isfahan, that Abu al-Wafa Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Sulaym informed them: Abu Uthman Said ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nuaym narrated to us: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Makhladi narrated to us: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj narrated to us, as I read to him: Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us (hawalah). 1605 - Zaynab bint Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed us, in Naysabur, that Wajih ibn Tahir informed them: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Makhladi informed us, he said: Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj informed us: Qutaybah ibn Said informed us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit the Ansar, greet their children, and wipe their heads."
"1496","Another 1606 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, in Isfahan, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Harith informed them, he being present: Abu Ahmad, that is Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-Attar al-Muqri, informed us: Abu Hafs, meaning Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Shahin, informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us (hawalah). 1607 - Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Isa al-Qasri informed us, at his house at Nahr Isa, that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Nasr ibn al-Zaghuni informed them: Abu al-Ghanaim Abd al-Samad ibn al-Mamun informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Hababah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi informed us: Abu al-Rabi narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: Abu Talhah proposed to Umm Sulaym, and she said: One like you is not rejected; but it is not lawful for me to marry you, I am a Muslim and you are a disbeliever; if you accept Islam, that shall be my dowry, I ask you for nothing else; so he accepted Islam and married her. Thabit said: We never heard of a dowry more noble than the dowry of Umm Sulaym: Islam. The wording is one, except that in the narration of Ibn Shahin: Thabit said: I never heard of a dowry. Al-Nasai transmitted it in the Book of Marriage from Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawir, from Jafar similarly. Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah narrated the like of it from Anas; it comes in his biography from Anas."
"1497","Another 1608 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn Yanal al-Sufi informed us by ijazah: that Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them: Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni informed us: Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb ibn Ali al-Nasai informed us: Ali ibn Muslim al-Tusi narrated to us: Sayyar narrated to us: Jafar narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women and perfume have been made beloved to me, and the coolness of my eyes has been placed in prayer. Thus al-Nasai transmitted it."
"1498","Another 1609 - Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani and Afifah bint Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Farfaniyyah informed us, in Isfahan, that Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Haytham al-Sabbagh informed them, Abd al-Wahid being present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, I being present and listening: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sawwaf informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Sayyar ibn Hatim narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah grants the illiterate on the Day of Resurrection a well-being He does not grant the scholars. My father said: This hadith is munkar, and he narrated it to me only once."
"1499","Another 1610 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hamid ibn Usayyah al-Harbi informed us, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Bazzaz informed them: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ushari informed us: Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Shahin narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to us: Qatan ibn Nusayr narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let each one of you ask his Lord for his need, even asking Him for the strap of his sandal when it breaks."
"1500","1611 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala and Abu al-Qasim Ibn Bint Mani, they said: Qatan ibn Nusayr narrated to us: Jafar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let each one of you ask his Lord for his need, even asking Him for the strap of his sandal when it breaks. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban transmitted it from Abu Yala al-Mawsili."
"1501","1612 - My maternal uncle, the learned imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us, that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: al-Hasan ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Darastawayh informed us: Yaqub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Qatan al-Dhari narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let each one of you ask his Lord for his need, even asking Him for the strap of his sandal when it breaks. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Dawud al-Sijistani, from Qatan. He transmitted it from Salih ibn Abd Allah, from Jafar, from Thabit as mursal. I say: Ali ibn al-Madini mentioned it among the objectionable reports of Jafar ibn Sulayman. I say: I do not know of anyone who raised it except Qatan ibn Nusayr, and Allah knows best."
"1502","Another 1613 - My maternal uncle, the imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us, that Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Hilal al-Daqqaq informed them: Abu al-Fadl Abd Allah ibn Ali, known as Ibn Zakari al-Daqqaq, informed us: Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran informed us: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Bakhtari al-Razzaz informed us: al-Hasan ibn Thawwab Abu Ali narrated to us, he said: I was with Ahmad ibn Hanbal, and he asked me about al-Halabi, and he used to declare him trustworthy and regret that nothing had been written from him, and said: What did you write from him? I said: From Hammad ibn Zayd, Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai, and Qazaah ibn Suwayd. He said: I regret him, I wrote nothing from him; he was a trustworthy shaykh. So I narrated to him from him, I said: Ammar ibn Uthman al-Halabi narrated to me, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai narrated to me, from Thabit, from Anas who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me good. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took him by the hand and said: Say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest. The Bedouin counted on his hand, then went and reflected, then returned. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: The poor man reflected. He came and said: O Messenger of Allah, Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest; these are for Allah, so what is for me? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Bedouin, when you say Glory be to Allah, Allah says: You spoke the truth; and when you say Praise be to Allah, Allah says: You spoke the truth; and when you say There is no god but Allah, Allah says: You spoke the truth; and when you say Allah is greatest, Allah says: You spoke the truth; then when you say O Allah forgive me, Allah says: I have done so; then when you say O Allah have mercy on me, Allah says: I have done so; and when you say O Allah provide for me, Allah says: I have done so. He said: The Bedouin counted seven on his hand, then turned away."
"1503","Another 1614 - al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Sayyar narrated to us: Jafar narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The birds of Paradise are like Bactrian camels grazing among the trees of Paradise. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, these are indeed fine birds. He said: Their eaters are finer than them, three times; and I hope that you shall be among those who eat from them, O Abu Bakr. Thus Imam Ahmad narrated it. Abd Allah ibn Muslim al-Zuhri narrated it from Anas. End."
"1504","1615 - Abu al-Fadl Shuja ibn Salim ibn Ali ibn Salamah al-Baytar informed us, at Dar al-Raqiq in Baghdad, that Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Umar al-Azdi informed them: Abu al-Ghanaim Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mamun informed us: al-Daraqutni informed us: Abu al-Abbas Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Maristani narrated to us: Mahmud ibn Masud al-Tarsusi narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammam narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman informed us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you and you narrate to us, it is as if we see Paradise and the Fire with our own eyes; but when we leave you and mix with wives, children, and wealth, our hearts change. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you were to remain upon what you are with me, the angels would shake hands with you openly, time after time. Al-Daraqutni said: Gharib from the hadith of Thabit al-Bunani from Anas; Jafar ibn Sulayman is alone in it, and I have not seen it except from the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Hanzalah the scribe."
"1505","Another 1616 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Muslim ibn Sulayman al-Irbili informed us, having come to us, with my reading to him, I said to him: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Asakir ibn al-Murahhab al-Muqri informed you, it being read to him: Abu Talib Abd al-Qadir ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Yusuf informed us: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Warraq, known as Ibn al-Askari, informed us: Muhammad ibn Khalaf Waki the judge narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sayrafi narrated to us: Abu Zafar Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the people of Paradise? He said: One who does not die until his ears are filled with what he loves. It was said: Who are the people of the Fire? He said: One who does not die until his ears are filled with what he hates. Hammad ibn Salamah and Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated it from Thabit. And Allah knows best."
"1506","Another 1617 - It was read to Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi, while we were listening in Damascus: Maali ibn Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Thalabi informed you, it being read to him: Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini informed us: Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad al-Khallal informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh al-Naysaburi informed us, it being read to him: Ahmad ibn Shuayb ibn Ali al-Nasai informed us: Ahmad ibn Fadalah ibn Ibrahim informed me, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Jafar ibn Sulayman informed us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Khadijah was with him, and said to him: Allah conveys greetings of peace to Khadijah. She said: Allah is Peace, and upon Jibril be peace, and upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Thus al-Nasai transmitted it in the Book of Virtues and in the Book of Day and Night Deeds. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1507","al-Husayn ibn Waqid from Thabit 1618 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi informed us, there, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Mulqabadhi informed us: Makki ibn Abdan informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man passed, and a man of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, I love this man. He said: Have you informed him? He said: No. He said: Stand and inform him. He stood to him and said: O you, by Allah I love you. He said: May He who you love me for love you. Al-Nasai transmitted it from Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Khuwaylid al-Naysaburi, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, and with him: Anas narrated to me."
"1508","1619 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Zayd, that is Ibn al-Hubab, narrated to us: Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to me: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man passed, and a man of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, I love this man. He said: Have you informed him of that? He said: No. He said: Stand and inform him. He said: He stood to him and said: O you, by Allah I love you for the sake of Allah the Exalted. He said: May He who you love me for love you. Thus Imam Ahmad transmitted it in his Musnad. Al-Daraqutni said: Husayn ibn Waqid and Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr al-Bahili narrated it thus. Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Thabit, from Habib ibn Subayah, from al-Harith, from a man of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and the statement is that of Hammad. I say: Muammal and Hammad narrated it from Thabit, from Anas. Muslim narrated in his Sahih from the narration of Hashim ibn al-Qasim, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Thabit, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall come on the Day of Resurrection to the gate of Paradise... the hadith. Ibn al-Mubarak narrated it from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Thabit as mursal."
"1509","Another 1620 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us: Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to me: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me (hawalah)."
"1510","1621 - Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Haddad informed us, in Isfahan, that Masud ibn al-Hasan informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid informed us in his statement: al-Hasan ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mansur Zaj narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Thabit narrated to me, he said: Anas narrated to me, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted a man to a person and said: Guard him. He said: He was heedless of him and the man left. He said: What did the man do? He said: I was heedless of him, O Messenger of Allah, and he left. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah cut off your hands, meaning he raised his hands thus. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the matter with you? He said: O Messenger of Allah, you said such and such. He said: Put down your hand, for I asked Allah, mighty and majestic, that any person of my ummah against whom I supplicate, He make it forgiveness for him. The wording is that of Ali ibn al-Hasan. In the narration of Zayd ibn al-Hubab: he entrusted a man to Hafsah bint Umar... and he mentioned the like of it."
"1511","al-Hakam ibn al-Khazraj al-Saadi from Thabit; Yahya ibn Main declared him trustworthy 1622 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi informed us, in Herat, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Sad Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Musa informed us: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Mukhalladi informed us: Zanjawayh ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan informed us: Muhammad ibn Rafi narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Khazraj: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my ummah. It comes in the narration of Mamar from Thabit, and it preceded in the narration of Ashath al-Huddani from Anas."
"1512","1623 - Abu al-Fakhir Uthman ibn Mahmud, known as Habbuwayh, in Isfahan informed us, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid informed us in his statement: al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us: Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: al-Hakam ibn al-Khazraj narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my ummah."
"1513","Hammad ibn Zayd from Thabit 1624 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad informed them, he being present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, from Hammad, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The believer is disheveled, dusty, humbled, with two worn garments, to whom no attention is paid; if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill it. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of al-Ala from his father, from Abu Hurayrah."
"1514","Another 1625 - Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Isfahani informed us in his book, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Ahmad ibn Zuhayr, that is al-Tustari, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is prohibited by breastfeeding is what is prohibited by lineage. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Aishah exactly the same."
"1515","Hammad ibn Salamah from Thabit al-Bunani 1626 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail informed us: al-Hajjaj informed us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You are our master and the son of our master, our best and the son of our best. He said: O people, say your saying and let not the devils draw you on; I am Muhammad ibn Abd Allah."
"1516","1627 - Abu Tahir ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us, in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik (hawalah). 1628 - Imam Ahmad said: Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man said: O Muhammad, our master and son of our master, our best and son of our best. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep to your saying and let not Satan lure you; I am Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, the servant of Allah and His Messenger; by Allah, I do not like that you raise me above the station in which Allah, mighty and majestic, placed me. The wording is that of al-Hasan ibn Musa, and the hadith of Affan is similar."
"1517","1629 - Abu al-Fadl Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Mawsili informed us, in Baghdad, that Yahya ibn Ali ibn al-Tarrah informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Hababah informed us: Abd Allah al-Baghawi informed us: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that a man said to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O our best and son of our best, our master and son of our master. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, say what I say to you, and let not the devils lure you; place me where Allah, mighty and majestic, placed me: I am the servant of Allah and the Messenger of Allah. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from Hajjaj ibn Minhal and al-Hasan ibn Musa, from Hammad. Al-Nasai narrated it in the Book of Day and Night Deeds from Abu Bakr ibn Nafi, from Bahz; and from Ibrahim ibn Yaqub, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Jabbar, both from Hammad ibn Salamah. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it in his book through Hudbah ibn Khalid. It was narrated from Humayd, from Anas."
"1518","Another 1630 - The learned imam Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Jawzi informed us, it being read to him while we were listening in Baghdad; it was said to him: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Dinawari informed you, and he acknowledged it, he said: The ascetic shaykh Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Qazwini dictated to us in his mosque in al-Harbiyyah: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Zayyat al-Sayrafi informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi informed us, it being read to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Prices rose in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). People said: O Messenger of Allah, fix prices for us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is the Withholder, the Extender, the Provider, the Fixer of prices; and I hope to meet Allah, mighty and majestic, with none demanding of me an injustice regarding a soul or wealth. It is in the narration of Qatadah from Anas. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Surayj and Yunus ibn Muhammad, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Qatadah and Thabit."
"1519","1631 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Thabit, Qatadah, and Humayd informed us. 1632 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, in Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Ahmad ibn Bundar informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Thabit, Qatadah, and Humayd narrated to us, from Anas who said: Prices rose in Madinah in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). People said: O Messenger of Allah, prices have risen, so fix prices for us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is the Fixer of prices, the Withholder, the Extender, the Provider; I hope to meet Allah the Exalted with none of you seeking from me an injustice regarding blood or wealth. The wording is that of Ahmad ibn Hanbal; in the narration of Ibn Abi Shaybah there is no mention of in Madinah, nor his saying fix prices for us; and with him: Allah is the Fixer of prices, the Withholder, the Extender, the Provider, and I hope. Abu Dawud transmitted it in the Book of Sales from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Affan, from Hammad. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it therein from Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar, from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, from Hammad, from Qatadah and Humayd, and said: a hasan sahih hadith. Ibn Majah transmitted it in the Book of Trade from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Hajjaj, from Hammad, from them. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban transmitted it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Hudbah ibn Khalid, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, Qatadah, and Humayd, from Anas."
"1520","Another 1633 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us, in Baghdad, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Ayshi narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was frightened for the sake of Allah and none is frightened; I was harmed for the sake of Allah and none is harmed; and there came upon me thirty days and nights when we had no food to eat except something concealed by the armpit of Bilal."
"1521","1634 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn al-Majd al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Waki narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was harmed for the sake of Allah, blessed and exalted, and none is harmed; I was frightened for the sake of Allah and none is frightened; and there came upon me three days and nights when neither I nor Bilal had food that a living being could eat except what the armpit of Bilal concealed. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Samad. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Abu al-Walid. Abd ibn Humayd transmitted it from Muhammad ibn al-Fadl, all from Hammad, and in it thirty. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Darimi, from Rawh ibn Aslam al-Basri. Ibn Majah transmitted it from Ali ibn Muhammad, from Waki ibn al-Jarrah, both from Hammad ibn Salamah similarly. Al-Tirmidhi said: a hasan sahih hadith. Ismail ibn Ishaq the judge narrated it from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, from Hammad."
"1522","Another 1635 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Yazid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he supplicated would place the backs of his hands toward his face."
"1523","1636 - Uthman ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Bakr, known as Habbuwayh, informed us, in Isfahan, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid informed us in his statement: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jawaribi narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, informed us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, Amr ibn Dinar, Tawus, and Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he supplicated would place the backs of his hands toward his face and their palms toward the earth. Hammad leveled his hands and spread his fingers. Muslim mentioned in the Sahih from the hadith of Hammad, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought rain and pointed with the backs of his hands toward the sky. And Allah knows best."
"1524","Another 1637 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Ibrahim, that is Ibn al-Hajjaj, informed us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then shoot arrows, and one of us could see the landing place of his arrow."
"1525","1638 - The hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud ibn al-Akhdar informed us, in Baghdad, that Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar ibn al-Samarqandi informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Hababah informed us: Abd Allah al-Baghawi informed us: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik who said: We used to pray Maghrib then shoot, and one of us could see the spot of his arrow. Humayd narrated it from Anas. Abu Dawud transmitted it from Dawud ibn Shabib, from Hammad ibn Salamah similarly. Something like this was narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Rafi ibn Khadij."
"1526","Another 1639 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit informed us (hawalah). 1640 - al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us (hawalah). 1641 - Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us, in Isfahan, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to me: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man of the Ansar and said: O uncle, say: There is no god but Allah. He said: An uncle or a paternal uncle? He said: Rather an uncle. He said: Is it better for me to say: There is no god but Allah? He said: Yes. The wording is that of Abd al-Malik. In the narration of Affan and Abd al-Samad: He said: No, rather an uncle. Affan said: He said: And is it better for me to say it? He said: Yes. The hadith of Abd al-Samad is close to it."
"1527","Another 1642 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Darir informed us, may Allah have mercy on him, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Strive against the polytheists with your hands and your tongues. Humayd narrated it from Anas."
"1528","Another 1643 - Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Akhdar al-Hafiz informed us, in Baghdad, that Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi and Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Tarrah informed them, they said: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Naqqur informed us: Abu al-Qasim Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Hababah informed us: Abu al-Qasim Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi informed us: Hudbah narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to preach leaning on a palm trunk; when the minbar was made he moved to it, and the trunk yearned, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and embraced it, and it calmed. He said: Had I not embraced it, it would have yearned until the Day of Resurrection."
"1529","1644 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: al-Qawariri narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach leaning on a palm trunk; when the minbar was built he preached upon the minbar, and the trunk yearned, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and embraced it. He said: Had I not embraced it, it would have yearned until the Day of Resurrection."
"1530","1645 - Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Qurashi informed us, in Isfahan, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Abu Nasr narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas; and Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach leaning on a palm trunk; when the minbar was made he moved to the minbar, and the trunk yearned until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and embraced it, and it calmed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I not embraced it, it would have yearned until the Day of Resurrection. Al-Darimi transmitted it from Hajjaj ibn Minhal, from Hammad. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Musa, from Hammad. Ibn Majah transmitted it from Abu Bakr ibn Khallad, from Bahz, from Hammad. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh transmitted it from Affan, from Hammad; Hammad said: And Habib, meaning Ibn al-Shahid, informed me from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"1531","Another 1646 - The just Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Sadaqah ibn Nasr ibn Zuhayr ibn al-Muqallid al-Harrani informed us, in Baghdad, that the noble Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Makki informed them: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Shafii al-Makki informed us: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani narrated to us, in Makkah: Muhammad ibn Khalaf narrated to us: Adam narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani (hawalah). 1647 - al-Abbas said: Ubayd ibn Adam narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the people of Paradise? He said: One who does not die until his ears are filled with what he loves. They said: Who are the people of the Fire, O Messenger of Allah? He said: One who does not die until his ears are filled with what he hates. Sulayman narrated it from Thabit."
"1532","Another 1648 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi al-Raja informed us, in Isfahan, that Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa al-Hafiz informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us (hawalah). 1649 - Abu Tahir Muawiyah ibn Ali ibn Muawiyah al-Sufi informed us by ijazah: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us: Abu Nuaym informed us: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, they said: Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When al-Najashi died, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek forgiveness for your brother. Some people said: Do you command us to seek forgiveness for him though he died in the land of Abyssinia? Then was revealed: And indeed among the People of the Book are those who believe in Allah and what was sent down to you. The wording is that of al-Tabarani, and the other is with its meaning. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Hammad except Muammal. Humayd narrated it from Anas."
"1533","Another 1650 - Uthman ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Bakr, known as Habbuwayh, in Isfahan informed us, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid informed us in his statement: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yazid, the brother of Karkhawayh, narrated to us: Yazid informed us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, would recite one night, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked to listen; when morning came he was told of it. He said: Had I known, I would have beautified it for you and moved you with longing."
"1534","1651 - Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Saydalani informed us, in Isfahan, that Abu al-Fath Ismail ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Ikhshid al-Sarraj informed them: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us: Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saigh informed us: Abu Bakr Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Firyabi narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Abu Musa stood one night reciting, and the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood to listen to his recitation; when morning came he was informed of that and said: Had I perceived, I would have moved you with longing and beautified it for you. Ahmad ibn Mani narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun."
"1535","1652 - al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah al-Baghdadi informed us, in Isfahan, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Nafi informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us: Bishr, that is Ibn al-Sari, narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Abu Musa al-Ashari would recite one night, and the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to listen; when morning came he was informed of that, and said: Had I known, I would have beautified it for you and moved you with longing."
"1536","Another 1653 - Abu Ali Diya ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Ali al-Nasri informed us, in Baghdad, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them: Abu al-Qasim Umar ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Khaffaf informed us, he said: Abu al-Fadl Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Sad ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf al-Zuhri informed us, it being read to him: Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every good land has been made for me a mosque and a purification."
"1537","1654 - The imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Saffar informed us, in Naysabur, that Wajih ibn Zahir al-Shahhami informed them: Yaqub ibn Ahmad al-Sayrafi and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Ismaili informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Khaffaf informed us: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj al-Thaqafi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khirash, who was awe-inspiring, narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us. 1655 - al-Sarraj said: Abu Yahya informed me: Hajjaj ibn Minhal informed us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was given four not given to those before me: I was sent to every red and black; I was aided with terror cast before me for a month; my ummah was given the spoils of war, which none before me was given; and every good land was made for me good, a mosque, and a purification."
"1538","Another 1656 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us, it being read to him while we were listening there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us (hawalah). 1657 - The imam Abu Bakr Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Qadir al-Jili informed us, that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us: Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym informed us: Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The voice of Abu Talhah is harsher upon the polytheists than a troop. Their wording is one."
"1539","Another 1658 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us, in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When we are with you and you narrate to us, our hearts soften; and when we leave you, we dally with women and children, and do and do. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If they were to remain upon that hour, the angels would shake hands with them. Mamar narrated it from Qatadah, from Anas. It preceded in the narration of Jafar from Thabit."
"1540","1659 - Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid, the Isfahani, by ijazah informed us, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nuaym informed us: Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani informed us: Ibrahim ibn Ahmad, that is Ibn Umar, narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you and you narrate to us, our hearts soften... and he mentioned the like of it."
"1541","Another 1660 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim dies and four of the people of the nearest neighboring houses testify for him that they know only good, except that Allah, mighty and majestic, says: I have accepted your knowledge and forgiven him what you do not know. Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal transmitted it from Muammal. Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban transmitted it in his book from Abu Yala al-Mawsili. It was narrated with other than this wording."
"1542","1661 - Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Khattab al-Harbi informed us, there: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Muslimah informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya, that is Ibn Said, narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bazzah narrated to us: Muammal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man dies and a community of people reaching a hundred pray over him and intercede for him except that they are granted intercession. It is mentioned in the Sahih from Aishah."
"1543","Another 1662 - Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there, that Tamim ibn Abi Said ibn al-Abbas al-Jurjani informed them: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Nasawi al-Qawmasi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Arubah al-Husayn ibn Abi Mashar al-Harrani informed us: Muhammad ibn Mamar and al-Husayn ibn Mudrik narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Muhajirun said: O Messenger of Allah, the Ansar have taken the reward; we have not seen people better in giving generously from plenty nor better in sharing in little than them; they sufficed us the burden and shared with us the comfort. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not praise them and supplicate for them? He said: Yes indeed. He said: Then that is for that. It was narrated from the hadith of Humayd from Anas."
"1544","Another 1663 - Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us, in Isfahan, that Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Sahl narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rafi al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked, when he went out for a need, to hear: O Najih, O Rashid. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it in the Book of Biographies from Muhammad ibn Rafi with his chain, except that he placed Humayd in place of Thabit, and said: a hasan sahih gharib hadith. I wrote it in the hadith of Humayd."
"1545","Another 1664 - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, in Isfahan, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, I think from Anas, that a man brought his brother to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This brother of mine does not help me. He said: Perhaps you are provided for because of him."
"1546","1665 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us, that Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Sabir al-Naqid informed us: al-Abbas, that is Ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isa al-Birti, narrated to us: Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that two brothers lived in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): one of them would attend the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his gathering, and the other was occupied with his craft. He said: O Messenger of Allah, he does not help me with anything. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps you are provided for because of him. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Bundar, from Abu Dawud."
"1547","Another 1666 - Abu Tahir Muawiyah ibn Ali ibn Muawiyah al-Sufi informed us in his book, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nuaym al-Isfahani informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us: Uthman ibn Yahya al-Firsani narrated to us: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution, then with it, and excellent is it; and whoever bathes, bathing is better. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Hammad except Muammal; Uthman ibn Yahya is alone in it."
"1548","Another 1667 - Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Akhdar al-Hafiz informed us, in Baghdad, that Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar ibn al-Samarqandi informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Naqqur informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi informed us: Hudbah narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the soul was breathed into Adam, it moved and flew, and reached his head, or rose to his head, and he sneezed and said: Praise be to Allah. Allah, mighty and majestic, said: May Allah have mercy on you."
"1549","Another 1668 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us, in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit informed us, from Anas, that the Jews entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Death be upon you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And upon you. Aishah said: Upon you be death, O brothers of apes and pigs, and the curse of Allah and His anger. He said: O Aishah, gently! Aishah said: Did you not hear what they said? He said: Did you not hear what I returned to them, O Aishah? Gentleness does not enter anything except that it adorns it, and it is not removed from anything except that it disgraces it. It was narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Aishah."
"1550","1669 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Tabarzadh informed us, with my reading to him, I said to him: Abu Ghalib Ibn al-Banna informed you: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Naqid informed us: Abu Habib al-Abbas ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isa al-Birti narrated to us: Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us: Muammal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: They entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning the Jews, and said: Death be upon you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And upon you. Aishah said: Rather upon you be death and His curse and anger, O brothers of apes and pigs. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, O Aishah? She said: Did you not hear what they said, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And did you not hear what I returned to them? O Aishah, gentleness does not enter anything except that it adorns it, and it is not removed from anything except that it disgraces it."
"1551","Another 1670 - My maternal uncle, the learned imam Abu Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us, that Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Yusuf informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Bishran informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad al-Daraqutni al-Hafiz informed us: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Said narrated to us: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man came after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed, and stood praying alone. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will trade with this one and pray with him?"
"1552","1671 - Muawiyah ibn Ali ibn Muawiyah al-Sufi informed us in his book, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nuaym informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas... and he mentioned the like of it exactly. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi."
"1553","Another 1672 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, in Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, he being present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding His saying: When his Lord manifested Himself to the mountain, He made it crumble. He said: He placed his thumb near the tip of his little finger's nail, and the mountain sank. Humayd said to Thabit: Does he say this? He nudged him and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says it, Anas says it, and should I conceal it?"
"1554","1673 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu al-Muthanna Muadh ibn Muadh al-Anbari narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us (hawalah). 1674 - Imam Ahmad said: Rawh narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding His saying: When his Lord manifested Himself to the mountain, he said: He said thus, meaning he brought out the tip of the little finger. He said: Humayd al-Tawil said to him: What do you intend by this, O Abu Muhammad? He said: He struck his chest a severe blow and said: Who are you, O Humayd? What are you, O Humayd? Anas ibn Malik narrates it to me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and you say: What do you intend by it? The wording is that of al-Anbari. In the narration of Rawh: When his Lord manifested Himself to the mountain, he gestured with his little finger, he said: and it sank; he did not mention what follows."
"1555","1675 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us, in Baghdad, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Bazzaz informed them: the judge Abu Yala Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Khalaf ibn al-Farra informed us: Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn Ali ibn Isa the vizier informed us, he said: It was read to Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, I listening: Hudbah ibn Khalid al-Qaysi narrated to us in Basrah: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: When his Lord manifested Himself to the mountain, He made it crumble. He said: He placed his thumb near the tip of the nail of his little finger, and the mountain sank. Humayd said to Thabit: Does he say this? Thabit raised his hand and struck Humayd's chest with it, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says it, Anas says it, and should I conceal it? Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it similarly from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Darimi, from Sulayman ibn Harb; and from Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Hakam, from Muadh ibn Muadh, both from Hammad ibn Salamah. He said: a hasan sahih gharib hadith, we know it only from the hadith of Hammad. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl and from Affan, from Hammad. Abu Zurah al-Razi was asked about it, and it was said to him: Abu Salamah al-Muqri narrated it from Hammad, from Thabit, from Anas as mawquf? And Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith and Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated it from Hammad, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Abu Salamah used to say before us: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when I read to him, he did not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in it; and the correct is marfu. I say: al-Hajjaj ibn Minhal, Sulayman ibn Harb, and Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated it from Hammad as marfu."
"1556","Another 1676 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, he being present: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Fadhshah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us. 1677 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Abu Nasr narrated to us (hawalah). 1678 - Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Hasan narrated to us (hawalah). 1679 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us, in Baghdad, that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us: Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym informed us: Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has a palm tree, and I support my wall with it, so order him to give it to me so that I may support my wall with it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Give it to him for a palm tree in Paradise. He refused. Abu al-Dahdah came to him and said: Sell me your palm tree for my garden. He did so. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have bought the palm tree for my garden. He said: Give it to him, for I have given it to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a heavy-laden cluster for Abu al-Dahdah in Paradise. He said it repeatedly. He said: He came to his wife and said: O Umm al-Dahdah, leave the garden, for I have sold it for a palm tree in Paradise. She said: A profitable sale, or a word like it. The wording is that of Hasan ibn Musa. The hadith of Abu Nasr is similar. He did not say repeatedly in the narration of Ibn Mani, and it is in the narration of Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz. The judge Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Assal al-Isfahani narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr, from Abu Nasr al-Tammar, from Hammad similarly. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it in his book from Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi, from Abu Nasr al-Tammar."
"1557","Another 1680 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Abyssinians would dance before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and move and say: Muhammad is a righteous servant. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What are they saying? They said: They say: Muhammad is a righteous servant."
"1558","1681 - al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, in Isfahan, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu al-Qasim al-Qushayri, that is Abd al-Karim ibn Hawazin, and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Maghribi informed us, they said: Abu al-Husayn al-Khaffaf narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj informed us: Abu Yahya narrated to me: Abu Salamah narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Abyssinians would dance before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and speak in their language. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What are they saying? He said: They say: Muhammad is a righteous servant. Ibn Hibban al-Busti transmitted it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Hudbah ibn Khalid, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from al-Nadr, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Thabit, from Anas."
"1559","Another 1682 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us: Muammal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say in his supplication: O Allah, turn my heart to Your religion, and guard those behind us with Your mercy. Abu Yusuf's name is Yaqub ibn Ishaq."
"1560","Another 1683 - Umar ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib informed us, that Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Sabir al-Naqid informed us: al-Abbas, that is Ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isa al-Birti, narrated to us: Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, there is no ease except what You make easy; and You make sorrow easy when You will."
"1561","1684 - al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would supplicate: O Allah, there is no ease except what You make easy; and You make sorrow easy when You will."
"1562","1685 - Yahya ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us, in Damascus, that his grandfather al-Hafiz Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl informed them: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Khalaf informed us: Hamzah ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us: Abdus ibn al-Husayn informed us: Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us: Ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us: Bishr, that is Ibn al-Sari, narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would supplicate and say: O Allah, there is no ease except what You make easy; and You make sorrow easy when You will."
"1563","1686 - Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there, that Tamim ibn Abi Said al-Jurjani informed them: Ali ibn Muhammad al-Bahhathi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us: Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Tamimi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Musayyab ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us: Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, there is no ease except what You make easy, and You make sorrow easy. Thus Abu Hatim ibn Hibban transmitted it; these three narrated it from Hammad as marfu. Al-Qanabi narrated it from Hammad, from Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as mursal."
"1564","Another 1687 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Yahya al-Muaddib informed us, in Baghdad, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us: Abu Umar Muhammad ibn al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyawayh informed us: Muhammad, that is Ibn Ahmad ibn al-Muammal ibn Aban ibn Tammam al-Sayrafi Abu Ubayd, narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Bishr, that is Ibn Muhammad al-Sukkari, narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Worship your Lord, pray your five, fast your month, perform Hajj to your House, and enter the Paradise of your Lord. Bishr ibn Muhammad ibn Aban ibn Muslim al-Sukkari, a Basran who settled in Baghdad, Abu Ahmad; Abu Hatim al-Razi and others narrated from him, and did not mention any criticism of him."
"1565","Another 1688 - The learned imam Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Maqdisi informed us, may Allah have mercy on him, that Abu al-Izz Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mawahib ibn al-Khurasani informed them: Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Khushaysh informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan informed us: Abu Amr Uthman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Daqqaq informed us: Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Salamah narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a bond of brotherhood between al-Zubayr and Abd Allah ibn Masud. End."
"1566","1689 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Yazid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: I never saw a day more radiant nor more beautiful than the day on which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr entered Madinah; and I witnessed his death, and I never saw a day darker nor uglier than the day on which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died. Affan ibn Muslim narrated it from Hammad."
"1567","1690 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Samad al-Sulami al-Attar informed us, in Damascus, that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi informed us: Isa ibn Imran al-Abbas informed us: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Darimi informed us: Affan informed us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, and he mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I witnessed the day he entered Madinah, and I never saw a day more beautiful nor brighter than the day on which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us; and I witnessed him on the day of his death, and I never saw a day uglier nor darker than the day on which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died. Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated it from Thabit, and it preceded."
"1568","Another 1691 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us, in Baghdad, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them: Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Mamun informed us: Ali ibn Umar al-Harbi informed us: Abu Khubayb, that is al-Abbas ibn Ahmad al-Birti, narrated to us: Ahmad al-Birti narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bazzah narrated to us: Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earnings of slave girls are unlawful. It was narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the earnings of slave girls."
"1569","Another 1692 - Abu Hamid Abd Allah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit informed us, in Baghdad, that Yahya ibn Ali al-Tarrah informed them: the judge Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muhtadi Billah narrated to us from his wording: Umar ibn Shahin narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Zaynabiyy narrated to us in Askar Mukram: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Yahya al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Jibril, from Allah, mighty and majestic, He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, descended upon Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, Allah, mighty and majestic, conveys greetings of peace to you and says to you: There is no servant against whom I decree a decree, whether he is pleased with it or displeased, except that it is good for him. Ibn Shahin said: This hadith is gharib; there is no chain in the world better than it, and none narrated it from Hammad except this man. Abu Bahr Thalabah narrated it from Anas. It has in the Sahih a witness from the hadith of Suhayb."
"1570","Another 1693 - Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh informed us, in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us: Salamah ibn Subayh al-Yuhmadi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a woman bathes from her menstruation, she undoes her hair and washes it with lote-tree leaves and ushnan; and when she bathes from janabah, she pours water on her head and squeezes it."
"1571","Another 1694 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn Yanal al-Sufi informed us by ijazah: that Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni informed us: Ahmad ibn Shuayb ibn Ali al-Nasai informed us: Ibrahim ibn Yunus ibn Muhammad Harami narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a slave girl with whom he had intercourse, and Aishah and Hafsah kept at him until he forbade her to himself; then Allah the Exalted revealed: O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you, seeking... to the end of the verse. Thus al-Nasai transmitted it."
"1572","1695 - Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Muallim informed us, in Isfahan, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Marduwayh al-Hafiz informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Ibrahim ibn Hashim informed us: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a slave girl with whom he had intercourse, and Aishah and Hafsah kept at him until he forbade her; then Allah revealed: O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you, the verse."
"1573","Another 1696 - Abu Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Salamah al-Qurashi informed us, in Damascus, that Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Qubays and Abd al-Karim ibn Hamzah ibn al-Khadir al-Sulami informed them, they said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Hadid narrated to us: my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Uthman al-Sulami informed us: Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Samiri narrated to us: Abu Badr Abbad ibn al-Walid al-Ghubari narrated to us: Hibban narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Thabit al-Bunani informed us, from Anas (hawalah)."
"1574","1697 - Abu al-Daw Shihab ibn Mahmud ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Hatimi informed us, in Herat, that Abd al-Salam ibn Ahmad ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad informed them: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abi Masud al-Farisi informed us: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shurayh informed us: Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Said narrated to us: Abu Badr Abbad ibn al-Walid al-Ghubari narrated to us: Hibban ibn Hilal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Arabs would serve one another on journeys, and with Abu Bakr and Umar was a man who served them; they slept and awoke, and he had not prepared food for them. One of them said to his companion: This one matches the sleep of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They woke him and said: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say to him: Abu Bakr and Umar convey greetings of peace to you and seek condiment from you. He said: Convey greetings of peace to them and inform them that they have already eaten condiment. They were alarmed and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we sent to you seeking condiment, and you said: They have already eaten condiment; with what did we eat condiment? He said: With the flesh of your brother; by Him in whose hand is my soul, I see his flesh between your teeth. They said: Seek forgiveness for us. He said: He should seek forgiveness for you. The wording is that of Ibn Said. In the narration of al-Samiri: some serve others. With him: serving them, then he slept. With him: He said: This matches the sleep of your house. With him, after seeking condiment from you: He came to him and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Inform them. With him: He said: By eating the flesh of your brother; I see his flesh between your molars. Affan ibn Muslim narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, that the Arabs would serve one another on journeys, and he mentioned it. It was said: Muwaamah is agreement, meaning: this sleep resembles the sleep of home, not the sleep of travel; they faulted him for much sleep."
"1575","Another 1698 - Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Isfahani informed us in his book, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Can none of you recite a third of the Quran every night? They said: Who can bear that? He said: Recite: Say: He is Allah, One. It was narrated from Qatadah from Anas similarly. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Qatadah narrated the like of it; it comes in his biography."
"1576","Another 1699 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us: Muammal narrated to us, from Hammad, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said in his sermon: There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant. Thus Muammal narrated it; Hajjaj differed from him, narrating it from Hammad, from Thabit, Humayd, and Yunus, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as mursal. Al-Daraqutni said: The mursal is more correct."
"1577","Another 1700 - Abu Muhammad Yunus ibn Yahya ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Hashimi informed us, in Egypt, that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad Hammuyah informed us: Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym informed us: Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) strove in supplication, he said: May Allah place upon you the prayer of a righteous people, who stand the night and fast the day, neither sinful nor wicked. Ahmad ibn Mani narrated it from Abu Nasr al-Tammar, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: When one of them strove for his brother in supplication, he mentioned it as the statement of Anas. Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated it from Khalid, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas. Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated it from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Thabit, from Anas, both as the statement of Anas. Some muhaddithun mentioned that Muslim narrated it from Abd ibn Humayd with this chain. I did not see it in Sahih Muslim, and Allah knows best."
"1578","Another 1701 - Abu Ali Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Khattab ibn Muhammad al-Harbi informed us, there, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qazzaz informed them: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Muslimah informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya, that is Ibn Said, narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah al-Makki narrated to us: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a gathering of the Ansar while they were joking and laughing, and said: Frequently remember the destroyer of pleasures, meaning death."
"1579","1702 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, in Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bazzah narrated to us: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people of the Ansar laughing, and said: Frequently remember the destroyer of pleasures. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Thabit except Hammad; Muammal is alone in it. Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Aslam al-Tusi, from Muammal ibn Ismail, with his chain similarly. I say: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bazzah is spoken about."
"1580","Another 1703 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while a man sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The man said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I love this one for the sake of Allah. The Messenger of Allah said: Have you informed him of that? He said: No. He said: Stand and inform him, affection will be established between you. He stood to him and informed him, and said: I love you for the sake of Allah, or he said: for Allah. The man said: May He whom you love me for love you. Husayn ibn Waqid narrated it from Thabit, and it preceded."
"1581","Another 1704 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, in Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Abu Nuaym informed us: Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us: Abu Umayr ibn al-Nahhas narrated to us: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, would begin with prayer before the sermon on Eid. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah except Muammal. It was narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Abbas."
"1582","Another 1705 - Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sad al-Thaqafi informed us, in Damascus, that his grandfather al-Hafiz Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Wahidi informed us: Abd Allah ibn Yusuf informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Said ibn Fardakh al-Ikhmimi informed us in Makkah: Ulayl ibn Ahmad al-Anazi narrated to us: my father Ahmad ibn Yazid ibn Ulayl narrated to me: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj upon a mount with a worn saddle and a blanket not worth four dirhams, then said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Allah, this is a Hajj with no showing off in it nor repute. And Allah knows best."
"1583","The eighteenth part of the Mukhtarah hadiths, being the third part of the hadith of Abu Hamzah Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. Note: our reliance in producing this part and what follows of the Mukhtarah parts is upon the copy of the author Diya al-Din al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him. In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Merciful; praise be to Allah alone; may Allah send blessings upon Muhammad and his family and grant peace. Humayd al-Tawil from Thabit al-Bunani 1706 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, that Zahir ibn Tahir informed them: the teacher Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri informed us, in what he dictated: Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ali al-Muadhdhin informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Khanb al-Baghdadi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Tirmidhi narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to me, from Sulayman, from Humayd, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas who said: The last prayer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people, he prayed in a single garment wrapped in it behind Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1584","1707 - The imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Saffar informed us, in Naysabur, that Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them: Abd al-Karim ibn Hawazin, Abu Bakr Yaqub ibn Ahmad al-Sayrafi, and al-Hakim Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Ismaili informed us, they said: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Khaffaf informed us: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj informed us: Abu Ismail al-Tirmidhi, that is Muhammad ibn Ismail, narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed behind Abu Bakr in a single garment. Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it in his book, from [...]. Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated it from Humayd."
"1585","1708 - Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Asadi informed us, in Damascus, that his grandfather al-Husayn ibn Muhammad informed them: Ali ibn Muhammad al-Massisi informed us: Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun ibn Musa informed us: Khaythamah ibn Sulayman informed us: Ishaq ibn Sayyar Abu Yaqub al-Nasibi narrated to us: Amr ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Humayd, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to me, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed behind Abu Bakr in a single garment, crossing its two ends; when he intended to stand, he said: Call Usamah for me. He came, and he leaned his back against his chest. It was the last prayer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed."
"1586","1709 - al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah informed us, that Wajih ibn Tahir informed them: Yaqub ibn Ahmad al-Sayrafi and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Ismaili informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khaffaf informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar narrated to us: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Humayd, from Thabit al-Bunani who narrated to him, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a single garment wrapped in it. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, from Shabbabah, from Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas similarly. He said: a hasan sahih hadith. He said: More than one narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, without mentioning in it: from Thabit; and whoever mentions in it: from Thabit, is more correct. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Umar ibn Abi Salamah and Jabir ibn Abd Allah."
"1587","Daylam ibn Ghazwan from Thabit 1710 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad, that is Ibn Abi Bakr, and others narrated to us: Daylam ibn Ghazwan narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man of his Companions to a chief of the polytheists calling him to Allah, mighty and majestic. He said: This god to whom you call, is he of silver or of copper? His statement weighed heavily in the breast of the messenger of the Messenger of Allah, so he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Return to him and call him to Allah. He returned and he said to him the like of his statement. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Return and call him to Allah. Allah sent a thunderbolt upon him, while the messenger of the Messenger of Allah was on the road unaware. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him that Allah, mighty and majestic, had destroyed his man. And there was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And He sends thunderbolts and strikes with them whom He wills, while they dispute about Allah. Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Umarah and Ali ibn Abi Sarah narrated it from Thabit similarly."
"1588","1711 - Zahir ibn Ahmad [...] informed us: [...] Yahya ibn Ayyub informed them:  [...] Daylam ibn Ghazwan narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man of his Companions to a chief of the polytheists calling him to Allah, mighty and majestic. He said: This god to whom you call me, is he of gold, silver, or copper? His statement weighed heavily in the breast of the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Allah has destroyed your man. He said: Allah sent down to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): And He sends thunderbolts and strikes with them whom He wills, while they dispute. Daylam: Ibn Majah narrated from him. Ibn Hibban mentioned him among the trustworthy. Ibn Main said: Salih. Ibn Abi Hatim said: I asked my father about Daylam ibn Ghazwan, and he said: There is no harm in him, and he is more beloved to me than Ali ibn Abi Sarah. Ibn Adi mentioned him in al-Kamil and cited hadiths for him."
"1589","Salim ibn Dinar, Abu Jumay, from Thabit 1712 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Tabarzadh al-Muaddib informed us, that Abu al-Badr Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit informed us: al-Qasim ibn Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Hashimi informed us: Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Lului informed us: Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashath narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us: Abu Jumay Salim ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought Fatimah a servant he had granted her. He said: Fatimah wore a garment such that when she covered her head with it, it did not reach her feet, and when she covered her feet with it, it did not reach her head. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw what she faced, he said: There is no harm upon you; it is only your father and your boy. Thus Abu Dawud transmitted it."
"1590","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Taifi, the muezzin of the mosque of Thabit, from him 1713 - Abu al-Wafa Mahmud ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Umar, known as Hamata, the grandson of Muhammad ibn Abi Sad al-Baghdadi, by ijazah informed us, that Abu al-Ala Muhammad ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Firsani informed them, in the year 495: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar informed us: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Bashir al-Thaqafi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sahl ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Dawud ibn Sulayman al-Muqri, the muezzin of the mosque of Thabit al-Bunani, narrated to us: my father informed me, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings to those who walk in the darkness of night to the mosques of complete light on the Day of Resurrection."
"1591","1714 - My maternal uncle, the imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us; it was said to him: Tahir ibn Muhammad ibn Tahir informed you, it being read to him: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn al-Haytham informed us: al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Mundhir al-Juayd informed us: Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Salamah al-Qattan informed us: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Majah narrated to us: Majzaah ibn Sufyan ibn Asid, the freedman of Thabit al-Bunani, narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Taifi narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques of complete light on the Day of Resurrection."
"1592","Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah from Thabit 1715 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Darir informed us, may Allah have mercy on him, in Isfahan, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Abu al-Qasim Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Shayban narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, he said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked dreams; sometimes a man would see a dream, and he would ask about him if he did not know him; and if he was praised as known for good, his dream would be more pleasing to him regarding him. A woman came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw as if I was brought and taken out of Madinah, and admitted into Paradise; I heard a crash at which Paradise shook. I looked, and behold so-and-so son of so-and-so, and so-and-so and so-and-so; she named twelve men, the Messenger of Allah having sent an expedition before that. They were brought, wearing garments with their jugular veins gushing. It was said: Take them to the river al-Baydhakh or al-Baydaj. He said: They were dipped in it, and came out with their faces like the moon on the night of full moon. They were brought a platter of gold containing unripe dates; they ate of its unripe dates as they wished; they did not turn it from one side except that they ate of the fruit what they desired; and I ate with them. The bearer of good news came from that expedition and said: Of the dream, such and such occurred; so-and-so and so-and-so were struck, until he counted twelve men. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the woman and said: Narrate your dream. She narrated it, saying: Such-and-such and so-and-so were brought, as he said. Bahz ibn Asad narrated it from Sulayman."
"1593","1716 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us, in Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Bahz narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked good dreams; sometimes he would say: Has any of you seen a dream? He said: When a man saw a dream, he would ask about him; if there was nothing wrong with him, his dream would be more pleasing to him regarding him. He said: A woman came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw as if I entered Paradise, and heard in it a crash at which Paradise shook. I looked, and behold so-and-so son of so-and-so, and so-and-so son of so-and-so had been brought, she counted twelve men, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having sent an expedition before that. He said: They were brought wearing worn garments with their jugular veins gushing. He said: It was said: Take them to the river al-Baydhakh, or he said: to the river al-Baydakh. They were dipped in it and came out with their faces like the moon on the night of full moon. He said: Then they were brought chairs of gold and sat upon them; a platter was brought, or a word like it, containing unripe dates; they ate of them; they did not turn it to a side except that they ate of fruit what they desired; and I ate with them. He said: The bearer of good news came from that expedition and said: O Messenger of Allah, of our affair was such and such; so-and-so and so-and-so were struck, until he counted the twelve whom the woman had counted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me the woman. She came. He said: Narrate your dream to this one. She narrated; he said: It is as she said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Affan, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah. It was narrated from Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim."
"1594","1717 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, the wording being his, that Abu al-Faraj Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baqqal al-Muallim informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar Ahmad ibn Mani informed us: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked good dreams; among what he would say was: Has any of you seen a dream tonight? When a man he did not know saw a dream, he would ask about him; if he was reported as known for good, his dream would be more pleasing. He said: A woman came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw in sleep as if I was taken out and entered Paradise; I heard a crash at which Paradise shook; and behold so-and-so son of so-and-so, and so-and-so son of so-and-so, until she counted twelve men, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having sent an expedition before that. They were brought wearing worn garments with their jugular veins gushing. It was said: Take them to the river al-Baydhakh. They were dipped in it and came out with their faces like the moon on the night of full moon. She said: Chairs of gold were brought and they sat upon them; a platter of gold containing unripe dates was brought; they ate of unripe dates as they wished; they did not turn it to a side except that they ate of fruit what they wished. She said: O Messenger of Allah, and I ate with them. The bearer of good news came from that expedition and said: O Messenger of Allah, it was such, it was such; so-and-so and so-and-so were struck, until he named twelve. He said: Bring me the woman. She came. He said: Narrate your dream to this one. The man said: It is as she said; so-and-so and so-and-so were struck. Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from Hashim similarly. Al-Nasai transmitted it in the Book of Dreams from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Mukharrimi, from Abu Hisham al-Makhzumi, from Sulayman similarly."
"1595","Another 1718 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, may Allah have mercy on him, in Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Faris informed us: Ismail ibn Abd Allah informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us: Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey; a man of his Companions walking beside him dismounted, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him and said: Shall I not inform you of the best of the Quran? And he recited: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"1596","1719 - Al-Mu'ayyad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Tusi informed us in Nishapur that Abu Muhammad Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Khuwari informed them, recited to him: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Bayhaqi informed us, Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Yaqub narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Ma'ni narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, and a man among his Companions dismounted and walked beside him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him and said: Shall I not tell you of the best of the Qur'an? Then he recited to him: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"1597","1720 - The Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hibat Allah ibn Taghlib al-Fazarani al-Nahwi informed us in Baghdad that al-Mubarakah bint Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhiyyah informed them: Asim ibn al-Hasan informed us, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us, Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us, Musa ibn al-Hasan al-Saqali narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Ma'ni narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, then he dismounted and a man among his Companions walked beside him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him and said: Shall I not tell you of the best of the Qur'an? He said: Then he recited to him: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. Al-Nasa'i transmitted it in Fada'il al-Qur'an and in Amal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah, from Abu Zur'ah al-Razi, from Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid. And Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti transmitted it in his book, from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Ahmad Ghundar, from Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid."
"1598","Another, 1721 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abd Allah Sammuyah narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise are those who do not die until they fill their ears with what they love, and the people of Hellfire are those who do not die until they fill their ears with what they hate. And Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Thabit. And Abu al-Zafar narrated it from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah like the narration of Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid. And Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Thabit, from Abu al-Siddiq, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as mursal. Abu Zur'ah al-Razi said: The error is from Abu al-Zafar, meaning in raising it (to the Prophet). I say: but this is the narration of other than Abu al-Zafar, and it has already preceded in the narration of Hammad ibn Salamah from Thabit as musnad. More than one narrated it from Adam ibn Abi Iyas, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Allah knows best."
"1599","1722 - [...] informed us; Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us, with my recitation to him - I said to him: Yahya ibn Ali ibn al-Tarrah informed you [...] recited to him while I was listening - he said: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Umar ibn Burhan al-Ghazzal informed us, Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, Abu Zafar Abd al-Salam ibn Muzhir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the people of Paradise? He said: He does not die until Allah, mighty and majestic, fills his ears with what he loves. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, then who are the people of Hellfire? He said: He does not die until Allah, mighty and majestic, fills his ears with what he hates."
"1600","Another, 1723 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Hudbah narrated to us, Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I do not recognize anything I used to recognize in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except your saying: there is no god but Allah. He said: It was said: The prayer, O Abu Hamzah? He said: You have prayed it at sunset, though that was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - although I have not seen a time better for the doer of good than this time of yours. And Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated it from Sulayman."
"1601","1724 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Asadi informed us in Damascus that his grandfather al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Asadi informed them: Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini informed us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Husayn ibn Umar ibn Burhan informed us at the frontier post of Tyre: Ishaq ibn Sa'd ibn al-Hasan ibn Sufyan al-Nasawi informed us, my grandfather al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us, Hibban ibn Musa narrated to us, Abd Allah - he is Ibn al-Mubarak - informed us, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I do not recognize among you anything I used to know in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except your saying: there is no god but Allah. We said: O Abu Hamzah, the prayer? He said: You have prayed at sunset, though that was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he said: although I have not seen a time better for the doer of good than this time of yours. And Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad, from Affan, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah. Al-Zuhri reported, saying: I entered upon Anas in Damascus while he was weeping, so I said: What makes you weep? He said: I do not recognize anything of what I knew except this prayer, and this prayer has been neglected. And in the narration of Ghaylan ibn Jarir: of what was in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - it was said: The prayer? Anas said: You have done what you have done with it. This is what is in al-Bukhari."
"1602","Another, 1725 - My maternal uncle, the Imam, the learned Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Salman informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Khayrun informed us, al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Darastawayh informed us, Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Azdi, then al-Ma'ni, Abu al-Husayn, narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the mosque in which there were some young men among his Companions, and he said: Whoever among you has the means, let him marry, and otherwise, fasting is upon him, for it is a suppressant (of desire) and a cutter of the vein."
"1603","1726 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Isma'il ibn Muhammad informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Muzhir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you has the means, let him marry, and whoever does not, let him fast, for fasting is a suppressant (of desire) and a cutter of the vein. Ibn Abi Asim said: And I think I heard it from Ibn Muzhir."
"1604","Another, 1727 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid informed us in Isfahan that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Abu Ali al-Asyuti - he is al-Hasan ibn al-Khadir ibn Abd Allah - narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalaf al-Asqalani narrated to us, Adam narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Safiyyah was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and it was her day, but she lagged behind in the march, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met her while she was weeping, saying: You mounted me on a slow camel. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began wiping her eyes with his hands and calming her, but she refused except weeping, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and left her, and she regretted it. So she went to A'ishah and said: This day of mine with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is yours, if you will make him pleased with me. So A'ishah took to her head-cover, which she had dyed with wars (a yellow dye) and saffron, sprinkled it with some water, then came until she sat at the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah said: What is the matter with you? She said: That is the bounty of Allah which He gives to whom He wills. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) understood the matter and became pleased with Safiyyah. Then he went to Zaynab and said to her: Safiyyah's camel has become exhausted, so what is it to you to give her your camel? Zaynab said: Do you deliberately take my camel and give it to the Jewess? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) boycotted her for three months and did not approach her house. Zaynab neglected herself and neglected her house, and took to the bed and propped it against the back of the house, and despaired of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) coming to her. Then one day, she heard the movement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as he entered the house, and he put the bed back in its place. Zaynab said: O Messenger of Allah, my slave-girl so-and-so has become pure from her menstruation today, for you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went in to her and became pleased with her. Thus al-Nasa'i transmitted it. And Abu Umar Hafs ibn Umar al-Darir narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Sumayyah, from A'ishah."
"1605","Another, 1728 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzar narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt something (of pain), and when morning came it was said: O Messenger of Allah, the trace of pain upon you is evident. He said: Despite what you see of me, last night I recited the seven long surahs."
"1606","Another, 1729 - Abu al-Fada'il al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Saydalani informed us by ijazah that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him - (H). 1730 - And Abu Ghalib Sabir ibn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Uswari informed us by permission that Abu Tahir Muhassid ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Muqri' al-Iskaf informed them - both saying: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq informed us, Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zakariyya al-Atrush narrated to us from his wording, Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Harbi narrated to us, Abu Zafar narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jews envy you for the greeting of peace and for the Amin. Abu Zafar's name is Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar ibn Husam ibn Misakk ibn Zal aldahim ibn Shaytan al-Azdi al-Basri; al-Bukhari and Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated from him."
"1607","Another, 1731 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Darir, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Sulayman - he is Ibn Isa al-Jawhari Abu Ayyub - narrated to us, Umar - he is Ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Tall - narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted from a riding companion of his and walked away from him. Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated it from Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Thabit, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... And Abu Hatim al-Razi mentioned that this is more likely, and Allah knows best. And some of them said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan is alone in this hadith from Sulayman. I say: Muhammad has been criticized by Yahya ibn Ma'in and Abu Hatim ibn Hibban. And al-Bukhari narrated from his son Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan from him other than one hadith in the Sahih; and Allah knows best. End."
"1608","1732 - Umm al-Fadl Karimah bint Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali informed us, recited to her, that Imam Abu Abd Allah al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Rustumi informed them by ijazah. 1733 - And Abu [...] ibn al-Mubarak [...] informed us that Abu Sa'd [...] informed them, recited to him - both saying: Abu al-Muzaffar Mahmud ibn Ja'far al-Kawsaj informed us, Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Baghdadi informed us, the judge Ahmad ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Harb narrated to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, who said: Ali said, I think, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to play with Zaynab bint Umm Salamah, saying: O Zuwaynib, O Zuwaynib, repeatedly."
"1609","Sawwar ibn Dawud Abu Hamzah, the perfume-seller: Yahya ibn Ma'in declared him trustworthy; from Thabit. 1734 - My maternal uncle, the Imam, the learned Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Yahya ibn Thabit ibn Bundar informed them: Tarrad ibn Muhammad al-Zaynabi informed us, Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr - meaning Ibn al-Buhturi - informed us, Muhammad - meaning Ibn Ghalib - narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Sawwar Abu Hamzah, the perfume-seller, narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed al-Miqdad over a detachment of cavalry, and when he came back to him, he said: How did you find them? He said: I found them raising me and lowering me until I thought I was not that (man). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: That is it. Then al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad said to him: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never work over anyone ever again. And they used to say to him: Come forward and lead us in prayer, but he would refuse."
"1610","Another, 1735 - The Hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Silafi informed us in his book that Abu [...] and Abu Khadir Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhakkir informed him there, both saying: Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Yankhab al-Tayyibi informed us, Abu al-Abbas Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah al-Harithi narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad informed me, my father narrated to us, Isa narrated to us, Abu Hamzah - he is Muhammad ibn Maymun al-Sukkari - narrated to us, from Sawwar ibn Dawud al-Basri, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, who said: A young virgin girl came, between her parents, to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My parents married me off without seeking my permission, so do I have any say in the matter? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Fear Allah, mighty and majestic, regarding your parents. She said: I may well do that, but do I have any say in the matter? He said: Yes. She said: I have left him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated the two of them."
"1611","Sallam Abu al-Mundhir from Thabit. 1736 - Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur ibn Muhammad [...] informed us that Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them: Abu [...] Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sunni informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ali al-Nasa'i informed us, al-Husayn ibn Isa al-Qumasi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Made beloved to me of this world are women and perfume, and the coolness of my eye has been placed in prayer. Ja'far ibn Sulayman also narrated it from Thabit. Thus al-Nasa'i transmitted it."
"1612","1737 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abd Allah informed us, Musa - he is Ibn Isma'il - narrated to us, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Made beloved to me are women and perfume, and the coolness of my eye has been placed in prayer. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Affan, from Sallam Abu al-Mundhir, from Thabit. Al-Daraqutni said: Sallam Abu al-Mundhir, Salamah ibn Abi al-Sahba', and Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated it from Thabit, from Anas; and Hammad ibn Zayd opposed them, narrating it from Thabit as mursal, and the mursal is more likely correct."
"1613","Sallam ibn Miskin from Thabit. 1738 - Shuhdah bint Ahmad ibn al-Faraj informed us by permission, and the Imam Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Najm ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hanbali informed us from her, that Abu al-Fath Abd al-Wahid ibn Ulwan ibn Aqil ibn Qays al-Shaybani informed them: Ahmad - he is Ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hasnun al-Qurashi, recited to him - informed us, Abd al-Baqi - he is Ibn Qani' al-Hafiz - informed us, Abu Ayyub Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn Yahya, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A surah in the Qur'an, which is but thirty verses, argued on behalf of its companion until it admitted him into Paradise, and it is the surah Tabarak."
"1614","1739 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them: Abu Bakr ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn Yahya al-Tabib al-Basri narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A surah of the Qur'an, which is but thirty verses, argued on behalf of its companion until it admitted him into Paradise, and it is the surah Tabarak. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Thabit except Sallam."
"1615","Another, 1740 - Abu Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us in his book that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn Yahya al-Tabib al-Basri narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of these two foul-smelling greens, eating them and entering our mosques; but if you must eat them, kill them thoroughly with fire. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Sallam ibn Miskin except Shayban."
"1616","Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj from Thabit. 1741 - Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Dahbal ibn Ali ibn Kazah informed us at al-Harim that Abu Ghalib Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Banna informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar ibn Musa Abu al-Husayn al-Hafiz informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Shababah narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating garlic and onions. It is reported in the two Sahihs: Whoever eats of this plant, let him not approach our mosque - meaning garlic."
"1617","Salih ibn Rustum Abu Amir al-Khazzaz from Thabit. 1742 - The Imam Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Lanjani informed us in Isfahan that al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Rustumi informed them: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Tayyan informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid informed us by his word, saying: It was recited to Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Naysaburi while I was listening: Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother has perished and has been buried, so pray over him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went with the Ansari to his brother's grave and prayed over him."
"1618","1743 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a black man used to clean the mosque, then he died and was buried at night, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached and told, so he said: Go to his grave. Then he said: These graves are filled with darkness over their people, and Allah, mighty and majestic, illuminates them by my prayer over them. So he came to the grave and prayed over him. And a man of the Ansar said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother has died and you did not pray over him. He said: Then where is his grave? So he told him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went with the Ansari. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."
"1619","Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr from Thabit. 1744 - Abu Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us in his book that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Hashim - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two men do not love one another for Allah except that the more beloved of them to Allah is the one with stronger love for his companion. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Thabit except Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr. Al-Daraqutni said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Thabit as mursal, and he said: and that is correct. I say: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated from Thabit, from Anas: A man of the desert came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Who created the heaven? He said: Allah - the hadith; Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from the narration of this Sulayman from Thabit, though Hammad ibn Salamah opposed him and narrated it from Anas as mursal, but that did not harm it. Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr al-Bahili: Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He is unknown."
"1620","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Hudhali from Thabit. 1745 - Abu al-Ala' Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja' ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Asbahani informed us by ijazah that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Asbahani informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Hudhali narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to propose to a woman, he would send Umm Sulaym to look at her, so she would smell her sides and look at her ankles. Al-Tabarani said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi is alone in it. Ibn Abi Hatim said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Hudhali, from Thabit - Isma'il ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated from him; I asked my father about him and he said: An unknown shaykh. I say: He mentioned that Isma'il narrated from him, and Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi also narrated from him."
"1621","Abd Allah ibn Shawdhab al-Marwazi from Thabit. 1746 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym al-Hafiz informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abd Allah Sammuyah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Waqi' narrated to us, Damrah narrated to us, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man who had killed a man, so he handed him over to the guardian of the slain, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Pardon him. He said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then take the blood-money. He said: No. He said: Go and kill him, for you are like him. He said: So the man was caught up with and it was said to him: Woe to you, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go and kill him, for you are like him. So he let him go, and he was seen going to his family, dragging his nose-rein (camel strap). Damrah said, from Ibn Shawdhab: I mentioned that to Abd Allah ibn al-Qasim and he said: This is for no one after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1622","1747 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Darir informed us in Isfahan that Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Dharr al-Salihani informed them: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us, Abu Umayr and Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Damrah narrated to us, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man brought the killer of his relative to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Pardon him, but he refused. So he said: Take the blood-money, but he refused. So he said: Go and kill him, for you are like him. So he let him go, and the man was seen dragging his strap, going to his family. Al-Nasa'i transmitted it in al-Qawad, from Isa ibn Yunus al-Fakhuri. And Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Majah transmitted it in al-Diyat, from Abu Umayr Isa ibn Muhammad al-Nahhas, and Isa ibn Yunus, the two Ramlis, and from al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani, from Damrah ibn Rabi'ah, similarly. Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni said: Damrah is alone in it from Ibn Shawdhab. In Sahih Muslim there is the like of it from Wa'il ibn Hujr."
"1623","Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna from Thabit. 1748 - Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad informed us by ijazah, and the Imam, the learned Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi informed us from him, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi al-Daraqutni al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The first time cupping was disliked for the fasting person was when Ja'far ibn Abi Talib was cupped while fasting, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him and said: These two have broken their fast. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) afterwards permitted cupping for the fasting person. And Anas used to be cupped while fasting. Al-Daraqutni said: All of them are trustworthy, and I know of no defect in it."
"1624","Ubayd Allah ibn Umar from Thabit. 1749 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Mus'ab al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man used to keep to reciting Say: He is Allah, the One in prayer with every surah, while leading his companions, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What obliges you to keep to this surah? He said: I love it. He said: Love of it has admitted you into Paradise. Al-Bukhari transmitted it as a suspended (mu'allaq) narration, saying: And Ubayd Allah said, from Thabit, and mentioned it. And al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari, from Isma'il ibn Abi Uways, from Abd al-Aziz, and said: A hasan gharib sahih hadith. And al-Daraqutni said: Abd al-Aziz is alone in it."
"1625","1750 - It was recited to Zaynab bint Abd al-Rahman al-Sha'ri in Nishapur while I was listening - Abu al-Muzaffar - he is Abd al-Mun'im ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Hawazin, recited to him - informed you: Abu Sa'id ibn al-Khashshab - he is Muhammad ibn Ali - informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Adl informed us. And Abu al-Abbas al-Daghuli informed us, Ahmad ibn Sayyar narrated to us, saying: I said to Ibrahim ibn Hamzah, and al-Darawardi narrated to you, from Ubayd Allah, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man used to lead the people in Quba', and when he prayed he would begin their prayer - he would begin with Say: He is Allah, the One, then recite after it another surah he would recite, doing that in all of his prayer. His companions said to him: If only you would use what you recite in prayer (alone), that would be more beloved to us. He said to them: If you love that I lead you, then I will recite nothing but this surah. He said: And they disliked that anyone other than him lead them, and they considered him among the best of them, so they mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he called him and asked about what the people had said, and he acknowledged it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why do you do that? He said: I love it. He said: Your love of it has admitted you into Paradise. I say: It has been narrated from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ubayd Allah."
"1626","1751 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi informed us in Damascus that his grandfather al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi informed them: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ala' informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi al-Nasr informed us, Khaythamah - he is Ibn Sulayman al-Atrabulsi - informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Uways informed us, my brother Abu Bakr narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Why do you keep to reciting Say: He is Allah, the One? He said: I love it indeed. He said: Then love of it has admitted you into Paradise."
"1627","Abd al-Wahid ibn Thabit al-Bahili Abu Thabit from Thabit. 1752 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Take suhur even if with a gulp of water."
"1628","1753 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us, al-Husayn al-Adib informed us, Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Thabit al-Bahili narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take suhur even if with a gulp of water."
"1629","1754 - Ubayd Allah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit informed us in Baghdad that Abu [...] informed them, recited to him, saying: [...] ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us, Salamah ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn [...] informed us, recited to him: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub ibn Isma'il al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Thabit al-Bahili narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take suhur even if with a gulp of water."
"1630","Another, 1755 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Abu Thabit Abd al-Wahid ibn Thabit narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked to break his fast with three dates or something untouched by fire."
"1631","Abbad ibn Rashid al-Basri from Thabit. 1756 - Yusuf ibn al-Mutawakkil ibn Kamil informed us in Baghdad that Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Sa'igh informed them, recited to him: Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Khallal informed us, al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali Abu Yahya informed us, Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Mubashshir narrated to us, Isa - he is Ibn Shadhan - narrated to us - (H). 1757 - And Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad ibn Yusuf informed us by permission, and my maternal uncle, the Imam, the learned Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi, informed us from him, that Abu Tahir Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Yusuf informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us, saying: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi al-Hafiz al-Daraqutni informed us, Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Mubashshir narrated to us at Wasit, Isa ibn Shadhan narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My father has perished and did not perform Hajj? He said: What do you think - if your father had a debt and you settled it for him, would it be accepted? He said: Yes. He said: Then perform Hajj on his behalf. Their wording is one. Thus al-Daraqutni transmitted it in his book. I say: Abbad ibn Rashid was declared trustworthy by Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal, Ibn Hibban spoke about him, and more than one of the Imams praised him. Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and the early ones narrated from him, and the early ones know him better than the later ones; and Allah knows best. And Abu Sa'id, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated it from Abbad ibn Rashid."
"1632","Ubayd ibn Muslim, the Sabori-cloth merchant, from Thabit. 1758 - Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud ibn al-Mubarak al-Hafiz informed us in Baghdad that Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn Umar ibn al-Samarqandi informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Naqur informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi informed us, Hudbah ibn Khalid al-Qaysi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Muslim, the Sabori-cloth merchant, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of ..... (H)."
"1633","1759 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Muslim, the Sabori-cloth merchant, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the believer is like the ear of grain; it inclines at times and stands upright at times. And Abu Ali al-Sawwaf narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sulayman ibn Nafi' al-Darimi, from Hudbah. And Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi narrated it from Busr. And it is reported in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Ka'b ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The example of the believer is like the tender plant of cultivation which the wind sets upright at times ... the hadith. And Muslim narrated from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The example of the believer is like the crop; the wind keeps bending it, and the believer keeps being struck by affliction ... the hadith."
"1634","Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab from Thabit. 1760 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Jurjani informed them: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Bahhathi informed us, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Zuhayr al-Jurjani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hawdah narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad - he is Ibn Zayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab - narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not be incapable in supplication, for no one perishes along with supplication. Thus Abu Hatim transmitted it in his book. And Mu'alla ibn Asad also narrated it from Umar."
"1635","1761 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan al-A'raj informed us, Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not be incapable in supplication, for no one perishes along with supplication."
"1636","Ghassan ibn Burzin al-Tuhawi from Thabit. 1762 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abd al-Wahid - he is Ibn Ghiyath - narrated to us, Ghassan ibn Burzin, meaning al-Tuhawi, narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came early one day and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are ruined, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. He said: What is that? They said: Hypocrisy, hypocrisy. He said: Do you not bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? They said: Yes indeed. He said: That is not hypocrisy. He said: Then they repeated a second time and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are ruined, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. He said: What is that? They said: Hypocrisy, hypocrisy. He said: Do you not bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? They said: Yes indeed. He said: That is not hypocrisy. He said: Then they returned a third time and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are ruined, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. He said: What is that? They said: Hypocrisy. He said: Do you not bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger? They said: Yes indeed. He said: That is not hypocrisy. They said: When we are with you we are in one state, but when we leave you, the worldly life and our families preoccupy us. He said: If when you left me you remained in the state you are in with me, the angels would shake hands with you on the roads of Madinah. Ghassan: Yahya ibn Ma'in declared him trustworthy. And Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated something of it from Thabit. And something of this is reported in Muslim from the hadith of Hanzalah the scribe."
"1637","Kathir ibn Habib al-Laythi Abu Sa'id from Thabit. 1763 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us in Baghdad that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them, recited to him: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn al-Naqur informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Daqqaq informed us, Abd Allah, meaning al-Baghawi, narrated to us, al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Kathir ibn Habib al-Laythi narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gentleness was never in anything except that it adorned it, and harshness was never in anything except that it disgraced it; and Allah, mighty and majestic, is Gentle and loves gentleness. Kathir ibn Habib: Ali ibn al-Madini, al-Salt, and others narrated from him. And Abu Hatim al-Razi was asked about him and said: There is no harm in him. And Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Thabit, from Anas. And it is reported in the Sahih from the hadith of A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness."
"1638","Another, 1764 - Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn al-Wathiq ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khayyat informed us in Marv - I said to him: Abu al-Qasim al-Junayd ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Qayini informed you, recited to him while you were listening, and he acknowledged it - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Umayri informed us, recited to him: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Bashani informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Idris ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari al-Basri narrated to us, Kathir ibn Habib al-Laythi narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Prophet has a pulpit of light on the Day of Resurrection, and I shall be upon the tallest and most luminous of them."
"1639","1765 - Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak informed us in Baghdad that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Naqur informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Daqqaq informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, al-Salt ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, Kathir ibn Habib narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every Prophet on the Day of Resurrection has a pulpit of light, and I shall be upon the tallest and most luminous of them. Then the caller will come and call: Where is the unlettered Prophet? The Prophets will say: We are all prophets of Allah - meaning: to which of us were you sent? - Then he will say: Where is the unlettered Arab Prophet? Then Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will descend until he comes to the gate of Paradise; then he mentioned the hadith of intercession at length. I say: The hadith of intercession is in the Sahih, though they did not mention these wordings; and Allah knows best. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban transmitted it at length from Abu Khalifah, from Ali ibn al-Madini, from Kathir ibn Habib Abu Sa'id."
"1640","Kathir ibn Yasar Abu al-Fadl from Thabit. 1766 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Tasnim narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Abu al-Fadl Kathir ibn Yasar narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought moist, well-watered dates, and he said: Where did you get this? They said: We had rain-watered dates, so we sold two sa's for one sa'. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return it to its owner, sell it for money, then buy the dates. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Thabit except Kathir Abu al-Fadl; Rawh is alone in it. And Muslim narrated something like it in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri."
"1641","Muhammad ibn Salim al-Basri from Thabit. 1767 - Abu al-Futuh As'ad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli, the Imam, the Mufti, informed us in Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Talib ibn Qurrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salim al-Basri narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you complains, let him place his hand upon that pain, then let him say: In the name of Allah and by Allah, I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of this pain of mine."
"1642","1768 - The Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Saffar, the Mufti, informed us in Nishapur that Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us, Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Makhladi informed us, Abu Bakr - he is Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Isfarayini - narrated to us, Musa ibn Sahl - he is Abu Imran al-Ramli - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salim al-Basri narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you complains of an ailment, let him place his hand upon the spot he complains of, then let him say: In the name of Allah and by Allah, I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of this pain of mine. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Salim, similarly, and said: A hasan gharib hadith from this angle. Abu Hatim al-Razi was asked about Muhammad ibn Salim al-Basri and said: There is no harm in him."
"1643","Muhammad ibn Mihran Abu Ja'far al-Razi from Thabit. 1769 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah informed us, Abu al-Qasim al-Lakhmi informed us, al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya al-Mutarriz narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Tamim ibn al-Ju'bad narrated to us, Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women of the worlds are: Maryam bint Imran, Asiyah bint Muzahim, Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, and Fatimah bint Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Qatadah narrated it from Anas."
"1644","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Tamimi al-Ammi al-Basri from Thabit. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Shabbabah and Hashim narrated from him, and he did not mention any criticism of him. 1770 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi al-Dimashqi informed us there that Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn al-Fath informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Samiri informed us, Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ammi narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Are you incapable of being like Abu Damdam? They said: And who is Abu Damdam, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Abu Damdam was a man before you; when he woke in the morning he would say: O Allah, I have given my honor in charity today to whoever wrongs me."
"1645","1771 - Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn al-Fadl al-Haddad informed us, may Allah have mercy on him, in Isfahan, that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Khurshid informed us by his word, al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated to us, Fadl al-A'raj narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ammi narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you incapable of being like Abu Damdam? They said: And who is Abu Damdam? He said: A man among those before us - or before you - who, when he woke in the morning, would say: O Allah, I give my honor in charity to whoever wrongs me."
"1646","1772 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ammi narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Are you incapable of being like Abu Damdam? They said: And who is Abu Damdam? He said: A man among those before you who, when he woke in the morning, would say: O Allah, I give my honor in charity today to whoever wrongs me. Al-Daraqutni said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ajlan as mursal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that is correct."
"1647","Mastur ibn Abbad al-Huna'i Abu Hammam from Thabit. Ibn al-Mubarak, Muslim ibn Ibrahim, and Abu Asim narrated from him. 1773 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Mastur Abu Hammam al-Huna'i narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have left no small nor great need except that I have committed it. He said: Do you not bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? - three times. He said: Yes. He said: Then that wipes away that."
"1648","1774 - It was recited to Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami while we were listening - your grandfather Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Mawazini informed you, recited to him and he acknowledged it - Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, the judge Yusuf ibn al-Qasim ibn Yusuf al-Mayanaji informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Mastur ibn Abbad al-Huna'i narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Anas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... the like of it, except that he did not say: three times."
"1649","1775 - The Imam Abu al-Futuh As'ad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf informed us in Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Hafs ibn Bahmard al-Askari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad Abu Asim narrated to us, Mastur ibn Abbad Abu Hammam al-Huna'i narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have left no small nor great need except that I have committed it. He said: Do you not bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. He said: Then that wipes away all of that. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Thabit except Mastur; Abu Asim is alone in it."
"1650","Ma'mar ibn Rashid al-Basri from Thabit. 1776 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak, known as Ibn al-Ma'tush al-Harimi, informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us - (H). 1777 - And Abu Dharr Sahl ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Mahmud al-Ta'i informed us at Busanj that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dawudi informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym informed us, Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Obscenity was never in anything except that it disgraced it, and modesty was never in anything except that it adorned it. Their wording is one, except that Abd ibn Humayd did not say qattu (ever) in the two places."
"1651","1778 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad that his maternal grandfather Abu al-Barakat Isma'il ibn Ahmad al-Naysaburi informed them: Abu Mansur Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Attar informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us, Ahmad - he is Ibn Ishaq ibn al-Buhlul the judge - narrated to us, al-Mu'ammal ibn Ihab narrated to us in Makkah, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Gentleness was never in anything except that it adorned it, and it was never removed from anything except that it disgraced it."
"1652","1779 - Umm Habibah A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Batirqani narrated to us, Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Mandah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Muqaddami informed us, Muhammad ibn Hammad al-Tihrani narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty was never in anything except that it adorned it, and obscenity was never in anything except that it disgraced it. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la and more than one, from Abd al-Razzaq, and said: A hasan gharib hadith, we know it only from the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq. And Ibn Majah narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal, from Abd al-Razzaq. And Ishaq ibn Rahawayh transmitted it in his Musnad from Abd al-Razzaq. And this hadith has already preceded in the narration of Hammad ibn Salamah from Thabit, and in the narration of Kathir ibn Habib from Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik. And it is in the narration of Ma'mar from Qatadah."
"1653","Another, 1780 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, the Abyssinians played with their spears out of joy at that."
"1654","1781 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, the Abyssinians played with their spears upon his arrival out of joy at that."
"1655","1782 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there that al-Mukhtar ibn Abd al-Hamid informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dawudi informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym informed us, Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah, the Abyssinians played upon his arrival out of joy at that; they played with their spears. Abu Dawud transmitted it in his Sunan from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal, from Abd al-Razzaq."
"1656","Another, 1783 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas - or another - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought permission to enter upon Sa'd ibn Ubadah, saying: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. Sa'd said: And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah, but he did not let the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hear, until he greeted three times, and Sa'd answered him three times without letting him hear. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back, and Sa'd followed him and said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father be ransom for you, there was no greeting you gave except that it reached my ear, but I answered you without letting you hear; I loved to increase in your greeting and in blessing. Then he admitted him into the house and brought raisins near to him, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate. When he finished, he said: The righteous have eaten your food, the angels have prayed upon you, and the fasting have broken fast with you."
"1657","1784 - The Imam Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muzaffar ibn Ibrahim al-Harbi, the preacher, informed us at Mosul that Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Barizi informed them: al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Ni'ali informed us, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran informed us, Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us, Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas - or another - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought permission to enter upon Sa'd ibn Ubadah, saying: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, without letting the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hear, three times, and Sa'd answered him three times without letting him hear. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned back, and Sa'd followed him and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), may my father and mother be ransom for you, there was no greeting you gave except that it reached my ear, and I did answer you without letting you hear; I loved to increase in your greeting and in blessing. Then they entered the house and he brought raisins near to them, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate. When he finished, he said: The righteous have eaten your food, the angels have prayed upon you, and the fasting have broken fast with you. Imam Ishaq ibn Rahawayh transmitted it from Abd al-Razzaq, and in it is also: from Anas or another, and with him is raisins. And Abu Dawud transmitted it in his Sunan in Foods, from Makhlad ibn Khalid, from Abd al-Razzaq, and with him is bread and oil; and Allah knows best."
"1658","The nineteenth part of al-Ahadith al-Mukhtarah, being the fourth part of the hadith of Abu Hamzah Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful; praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family and grant peace. Remainder of the hadith of Ma'mar ibn Rashid from Thabit. 1785 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Husayn informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Hamdan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a pledge from the women when they gave him allegiance, that they not wail. They said: O Messenger of Allah, some women helped us (in wailing) in the Jahiliyyah, so shall we help them in Islam? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no helping (in wailing) in Islam, nor shighar, nor sacrificial slaughter at graves in Islam, nor jalab, nor janab in Islam; and whoever plunders is not of us."
"1659","1786 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Razzaq al-Attar al-Sulami informed us in Damascus that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dawudi informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym informed us, Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took from the women when they gave him allegiance that they not wail ... then he mentioned it, and with him: nor shighar in Islam, nor slaughter at graves in Islam, nor jalab nor janab; and whoever plunders is not of us. And the rest is the like of it."
"1660","1787 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: the judge Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad al-Isma'ili informed us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Harb informed us, Makki ibn Abdan ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abu al-Azhar narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he took allegiance from the women, took upon them that they not wail. They said: O Messenger of Allah, some women helped us in the Jahiliyyah, shall we help them in Islam? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no helping in Islam - meaning wailing - nor shighar in Islam, nor janab, nor jalab, nor slaughter at graves in Islam; and whoever plunders is not of us. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh transmitted it in his Musnad from Abd al-Razzaq, without mentioning shighar. And Abu Dawud transmitted in his Sunan: nor slaughter at graves in Islam, from Yahya ibn Musa al-Balkhi, from Abd al-Razzaq. And al-Tirmidhi transmitted: and whoever plunders is not of us, from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Abd al-Razzaq, and said: A hasan sahih gharib hadith from the hadith of Anas. And Ibn Majah transmitted: no shighar in Islam, from al-Husayn ibn Mahdi, from Abd al-Razzaq. And Abu Hatim al-Razi said: This is a very rejected hadith. And al-Daraqutni said: Ma'mar is alone in it from Thabit. And the Imams who narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq - some of them are more knowledgeable than Abu Hatim al-Razi; and Allah knows best. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it in his book from the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq from Ma'mar."
"1661","1788 - Another. The Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Saffar informed us in Nishapur that Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Azhari informed us, Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Makhladi informed us, al-Mu'ammal - he is Ibn al-Hasan - informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sijzi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah wanted to marry a woman, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go and look at her, for it is more likely to bring harmony between you. He said: So he looked at her and mentioned her suitability. Al-Sijzi: Ibn Adi spoke about him, though others followed him in this hadith."
"1662","1789 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there that As'ad ibn Ziyad informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dawudi informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym informed us, Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah wanted to marry a woman, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go and look at her, for it is more likely to bring harmony between you. He said: So he did so and married her, and mentioned her suitability."
"1663","1790 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Bashir - he is al-Tayalisi Abu Ayyub - narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wants to marry a woman, there is no harm in looking at her. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it in his book from Imran ibn Musa, from Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim, from Abd al-Razzaq. Al-Hafiz al-Daraqutni said: Ma'mar is alone in it, and from him Abd al-Razzaq. And al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Thabit except Ma'mar; Abd al-Razzaq is alone in it. Abu Abd Allah ibn Majah transmitted it from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Khallal, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik - all of them - from Abd al-Razzaq."
"1664","Another, 1791 - Abu al-Najib Isma'il ibn Uthman ibn Isma'il al-Naysaburi informed us there that Abu al-Futuh Abd al-Wahhab ibn Isma'il ibn Umar al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Sarram informed us, the noble Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-Alawi narrated to us, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sharqi informed us, dictating from his memory: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli, Abu al-Azhar al-Sulayti, and Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us - (H). 1792 - And Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Naysaburi informed them: my father informed us, Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammish al-Ziyadi informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan informed us, Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for the people of major sins among my community. Their wording is one. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it in al-Zuhd from Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari, from Abd al-Razzaq, and said: A hasan sahih gharib hadith from this angle. And Humayd and Ash'ath narrated it from Anas."
"1665","Another, 1793 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah said: Daughter of a Jew - so she wept, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to her and said: What is the matter with you? She said: Hafsah said to me: I am the daughter of a Jew. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are indeed the daughter of a Prophet, your uncle is indeed a Prophet, and you are indeed under a Prophet, so in what does she boast over you? Then he said: Fear Allah, O Hafsah."
"1666","1794 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah said to her: Daughter of a Jew, so she came in to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while weeping. He said: What makes you weep? She said: Hafsah said to me: I am the daughter of a Jew. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are indeed the daughter of a Prophet, your uncle is indeed a Prophet, and you are indeed under a Prophet, so in what does she boast over you? Then he said: Fear Allah, O Hafsah."
"1667","1795 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah said: Daughter of a Jew, so she wept. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to her while she was weeping and said: What is the matter with you? She said: Hafsah said to me ...: I am the daughter of a Jew. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are indeed the daughter of a Prophet, your uncle is indeed a Prophet, and you are indeed under a Prophet, so in what does she boast over you? Then he said: Fear Allah, O Hafsah."
"1668","1796 - The noble Sharif Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ali ibn Hamzah al-Musawi informed us at Herat that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dawudi informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym informed us, Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik: It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah said: O daughter of a Jew - so she wept, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to her while she was weeping and said: What makes you weep? She said: Hafsah said: I am the daughter of a Jew. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - meaning -: You are indeed the daughter of a Prophet, your uncle is indeed a Prophet, and you are indeed under a Prophet, so in what does she boast over you? Then he said: Fear Allah, O Hafsah."
"1669","1797 - Abu al-Mafakhir Uthman ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Bakr Habbuwayh informed us in Isfahan that Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghiyan informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid informed us by his word, Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah, may Allah be pleased with her, said to her: Daughter of a Jew, so she wept. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in while she was weeping and said: What makes you weep? She said: Hafsah said to me: Daughter of a Jew. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are indeed the daughter of a Prophet, your uncle is indeed a Prophet, and you are indeed under a Prophet, so in what does she boast over you? Then he said: Fear Allah, O Hafsah. And Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it in al-Manaqib from Ishaq ibn Mansur and Abd ibn Humayd. And al-Nasa'i transmitted it in Ishrat al-Nisa' from Khushaysh ibn Asram - all three - from Abd al-Razzaq. Al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan sahih gharib hadith from this angle. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it in his book from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili, from Ibn Zanjawayh."
"1670","Another, 1798 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us in Isfahan that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us, Isma'il ibn Abd Allah Sammuyah narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Thabit and Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked toward Iraq, Sham, and Yemen - I do not know with which of them he began - and said: O Allah, turn their hearts toward Your obedience, and protect those behind them."
"1671","1799 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr ibn Barri narrated to us, Hisham ibn Yusuf al-San'ani narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, Thabit and Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked toward Iraq, Sham, and Yemen and said: O Allah, turn their hearts to Your obedience and protect those behind them. And al-Husayn ibn Mu'adh narrated it from Ali ibn Bahr. And Tammam ibn Muhammad al-Razi narrated it from Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Nasr the judge, from Ishaq ibn Khalawayh al-Babasiri, from Ali ibn Bahr. Al-Daraqutni said: Ma'mar is alone in it, and none narrated it from Hisham ibn Yusuf from him except Ali ibn Bahr; and Allah knows best."
"1672","Another, 1800 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to a woman of the Ansar on behalf of Julaybib, to her father, who said: Until I consult her mother. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then yes, if so. The man went to his wife and mentioned that to her, and she said: No, by Allah, then - did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) find none but Julaybib? We have already refused her to so-and-so and so-and-so. The girl was in her seclusion listening. The man set out wanting to tell the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of that, so the girl said: Do you want to turn back the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? If he is pleased with him for you, then marry him. It was as if she removed the doubt from her parents, and they said: You are right. So her father went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: If you are pleased with him, then we are pleased with him. He said: I am indeed pleased with him. So he married her to him. Then the people of Madinah were alarmed (for battle), and Julaybib rode out, and they found him killed, with people of the polytheists around him whom he had killed. Anas said: I saw her, and she was among the most spending widows in Madinah."
"1673","1801 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym informed us, Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us with its chain similarly, except that in his narration he said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) find none but Julaybib? And we have already refused her. And with him: it was as if she removed (doubt). And with him: so he married her to him. He said: Then ... And with him: and they found him killed. And Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban transmitted it in his book from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq. Muslim narrated in his Sahih the story of Julaybib in another wording, from Ishaq ibn Umar ibn Salit, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Kinanah ibn Nu'aym, from Abu Burdah al-Aslami. So Thabit al-Bunani retained it from Anas in one wording, and retained it from Kinanah from Abu Barzah in another wording; and Allah knows best."
"1674","Another, 1802 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl informed us at Herat that Abu al-Muhsin As'ad ibn Ziyad informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us, Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym al-Shashi informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd ibn Humayd ibn Nasr narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik - (H)."
"1675","1803 - Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Sam'ani informed us at Marv that Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Furawi informed them: Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Mahmi informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us, Abu Hamid ibn al-Sharqi informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I counted in the head and beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) no more than fourteen white hairs. Their wording is one."
"1676","1804 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak Abu Tahir al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I counted in the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) no more than fourteen white hairs."
"1677","Another, 1805 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a desert man whose name was Zahir used to bring gifts from the desert to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would provide him when he wanted to leave. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zahir is our desert, and we are his town. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved him, and he was an unattractive man. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him while he was selling his goods and embraced him from behind while the man could not see him. He said: Let me go, who is this? Then he recognized the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and began pressing his back against the belly of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he recognized him. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began saying: Who will buy the slave? The man said: O Messenger of Allah, then you will find me, by Allah, unsellable. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: But with Allah you are not unsellable; and he said: With Allah you are precious."
"1678","1806 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that a man ... then he mentioned the hadith, and in it: Zahir is our desert man and we are his townsfolk. And in it: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him one day. And in it: Let me go, who is this? Then he turned and recognized the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And in it: his back against the chest of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And in it: He said: O Messenger of Allah, then by Allah you will find me unsellable. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: But with Allah you are not unsellable - or he said: But you are with Allah precious. And the rest is the like of it. And Ishaq ibn Rahawayh and Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq similarly. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban transmitted it in his book from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, similarly. And Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Abd al-Razzaq."
"1679","Another, 1807 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Hamdan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, saying: I heard Thabit narrating from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth in Makkah and I have family there, and I want to go to them - am I free if I speak against you or say something? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him to say what he wished. He went to his wife when he arrived and said: Gather what you have with you, for I want to buy from the spoils of Muhammad and his Companions, for they have been plundered and their wealth taken. That spread in Makkah, so the Muslims were subdued, and the polytheists displayed joy and delight. The news reached al-Abbas, so he was struck as if hamstrung and could not stand. Uthman al-Jazari informed me, from Miqsam, saying: He took a son of his called Qutham, lay down and placed him on his chest, saying: Qutham, Qutham, the noble-featured. Thabit said, from Anas: Then he sent a slave boy of his to al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat: Woe to you, what have you brought? What are you saying? What Allah, blessed and exalted, has promised is better than what you have brought. Al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat said to his slave boy: Convey greetings to Abu al-Fadl and tell him to be alone for me in one of his houses so I may come to him, for the news is what will please him. His slave boy came, and when he reached the door of the house he said: Glad tidings, O Abu al-Fadl. Al-Abbas leapt up in joy until he kissed him between his eyes, and he told him what al-Hajjaj had said, so he freed him. Then al-Hajjaj came to him and told him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had conquered Khaybar and taken their wealth as spoils, the arrows of Allah had run in their wealth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had chosen Safiyyah bint Huyayy for himself, taking her for himself, giving her the choice to free her and be his wife or to join her family - and she chose that he free her and she be his wife. But I came for wealth of mine here which I wanted to gather and take away, so I sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to say what I wished, so conceal me for three days, then mention what you wish."
"1680","1808 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi al-Darir informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a house in Makkah and I have family there, and I want to go to them - am I free if I speak against you or say something? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him to say what he wished. He went to his wife when he arrived and said: Gather for me what you have with you ... and he recounted the hadith like the hadith of Ahmad, adding regarding Qutham: and he resembled the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, Abd ibn Humayd, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani, and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in abridged form from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban transmitted it in his book from Abu Ya'la, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh at length."
"1681","1809 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh and Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani, both together, informed us in Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth in Makkah and I have family there, and I want to go to them - am I free if I speak against you or say something? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted him to say what he wished. He said: He went to his wife when he arrived and said: Gather for me what you have with you, for I want to buy from the spoils of Muhammad and his Companions, for they have been plundered and their wealth taken. That spread in Makkah, so the Muslims were subdued, and the polytheists displayed joy and delight. The news reached al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, so he was struck as if hamstrung and could not stand. Then he sent a slave boy to al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat: Woe to you, what have you brought? What are you saying? What Allah has promised is better than what you have brought. Al-Hajjaj ibn Ilat said: Convey greetings to Abu al-Fadl and tell him to be alone for me in one of his houses so I may come to him, for the news is what will please him. His slave boy came to him, and when he reached the door he said: Glad tidings, O Abu al-Fadl. Al-Abbas leapt up in joy until he kissed him between his eyes, and he told him what al-Hajjaj had said, so he freed him. Then al-Hajjaj came and told him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had conquered Khaybar and taken their wealth as spoils, the arrows of Allah had run in their wealth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had chosen Safiyyah bint Huyayy and taken her for himself, giving her the choice between freeing her and being his wife, or joining her family. She chose that he free her and she be his wife. But I came for wealth of mine here which I wanted to gather and take away, so I sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he permitted me to say what I wished - so conceal me for three days, then mention what you wish. His wife gathered what jewelry she had with her."
"1682","Maymun Abu Abd Allah from Thabit. 1810 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us, recited to him in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them, recited to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Maymun Abu Abd Allah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: I had a forelock, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stretch it and hold it."
"1683","Nuh ibn Abbad al-Qurashi al-Basri from Thabit. 1811 - As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us in Isfahan that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Nuh ibn Abbad al-Qurashi al-Basri narrated to us. 1812 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym al-Asbahani informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Faris informed us, Isma'il ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad al-Misri - he is al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar - narrated to me, Nuh ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The servant reaches by good character the great ranks of the Hereafter and noble stations, though his worship is weak; and he reaches by bad character the lowest of Hell, though he is a worshipper. The wording is one, except that in the narration of al-Miqdam: the lowest rank in Hell, and he did not say: though he is a worshipper."
"1684","1813 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn al-Muslim al-Lakhmi informed us that Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fath al-Sulami informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Abi al-Hadid informed me, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Samiri informed us, Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Askari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Muradi narrated to us, Nuh ibn Abbad al-Qurashi informed us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik ... the like of it up to his saying: though his worship is weak, and he did not mention what is at its end."
"1685","Warqa' ibn Umar from Thabit. 1814 - Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Dahbal ibn Kazah informed us on the western side of Baghdad that the judge Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them: the Imam Abu Ya'la Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Khalaf informed us, dictating: Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Malik al-Bayyi' informed us, recited to him while I was listening: Abu Nasr al-Layth ibn Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Marwazi narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Nasr al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Warqa' narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is inspired with five is not deprived of five: whoever is inspired with supplication is not deprived of answer, for Allah, exalted, says: And your Lord said: Call upon Me, I will answer you. Whoever is inspired with repentance is not deprived of acceptance, for Allah, exalted, says: And He is the One who accepts repentance from His servants. Whoever is inspired with gratitude is not deprived of increase, for Allah, exalted, says: If you are grateful, I will surely increase you. Whoever is inspired with seeking forgiveness is not deprived of forgiveness, for Allah says: Seek forgiveness from your Lord; indeed He is Most Forgiving. And whoever is inspired with spending is not deprived of replacement, for Allah, exalted, says: Whatever you spend of anything, He will replace it."
"1686","Tha'labah Abu Bahr, the freedman of Anas - and it is said he is Ibn Asim - from Anas ibn Malik. Shu'bah, Mis'ar, Hajjaj, al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah, al-Qasim ibn Shurayh, Raqabah, al-Mas'udi, and others narrated from him. 1815 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, al-Qasim ibn Shurayh narrated to me, from Tha'labah, who said: I heard Anas saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am amazed at the believer - Allah, exalted, decrees no decree for him except that it is good for him. Al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah narrated it from Tha'labah. And Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Waki', from Sufyan."
"1687","1816 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Tha'labah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, then said: I am amazed at the believer - Allah decrees no decree for him except that it is good for him. And Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr, from Abu Khalid al-Ahmar, from al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah. And he narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Waki', from Sufyan, from al-Qasim ibn Shurayh. And Asim al-Ahwal narrated from Tha'labah ibn Asim, from Anas, similarly."
"1688","1817 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Bahhathi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban ibn Ahmad al-Busti informed us, al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah al-Qattan narrated to us, Nuh ibn Habib narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Tha'labah ibn Asim, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am amazed at the believer - Allah decrees nothing except that it is good for him. Thus Abu Hatim transmitted it. And Abu Mu'awiyah narrated it from Hajjaj from him."
"1689","1818 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us, Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, al-Ju'fi - he is al-Husayn ibn Ali - narrated to us, from Za'idah, from al-Husayn ibn Ubayd Allah, who said: Tha'labah narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, what are you laughing at? He said: Wonder at the believer - Allah, mighty and majestic, decrees no decree for him except that it is good for him."
"1690","Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas, from his grandfather. 1819 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Mubarak al-Khayyat narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about coitus interruptus. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even if the fluid from which the child comes were poured upon a rock, Allah would surely bring forth a child from it; and Allah will surely create a soul He is to create."
"1691","1820 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Asim narrated to us, Abu Amr Mubarak al-Khayyat - the grandfather of the children of Abbad ibn Kathir - narrated to us, saying: I asked Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas about coitus interruptus. He said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or asked about coitus interruptus? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even if you poured the fluid from which the child comes upon a rock, Allah, blessed and exalted, would surely bring forth from it - or: there would come forth from it - the doubt is from him - and Allah, blessed and exalted, will surely create a soul He is to create."
"1692","1821 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Saydalani informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Faris narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Isam narrated to us, Abu Asim al-Nabil narrated to us, Abu Amr Mubarak al-Khayyat narrated to us, saying: I asked Thumamah ibn Anas about coitus interruptus, and he said: I heard Anas saying: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about coitus interruptus. He said: The fluid from which the child comes - even if it were poured upon a rock, a child would come from it, or: there would come forth from it a child - the doubt is from them - and Allah will surely create a soul He is to create. And Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili narrated it from Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan, from Abu Asim."
"1693","Another, 1822 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, that he performed Hajj upon a saddlebag and was not miserly, and reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj upon a saddlebag, which was his provision-carrier. Al-Bukhari transmitted it as a suspended narration, saying: And Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr said, from Yazid. And it is said Ali ibn al-Madini denied that it is from the hadith of Yazid ibn Zuray'; and Allah knows best."
"1694","1823 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas, who said: Anas performed Hajj upon a saddlebag and was not miserly, and reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj upon a saddlebag, which was his provision-carrier."
"1695","Another, 1824 - Abu Rashid Habib ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Sufi informed us by ijazah that Ghanim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Burji informed them, recited to him: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sawwaf informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a small boy or girl, saying: If anyone were to be saved from the narrowness or squeeze of the grave, this child would have been saved."
"1696","1825 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Abu al-Tayyib Talhah ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi Dharr informed them while he was present: my grandfather Abu Dharr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Salhaniyy informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Habban informed us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas. Abu Salamah Musa ibn Isma'il narrated it from Hammad, from Thumamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - as mursal. I say: More than one narrated it connected as we transmitted it, among them al-Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il and al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Jabbar; and Allah knows best."
"1697","1826 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Darir informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Ibrahim al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Abd Allah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a little girl or boy and said: If anyone were to be saved from the embrace of the grave, this child would have been saved. Al-Daraqutni said: Harami ibn Umarah and Sa'id ibn Asim al-Lakhmi - a Basran shaykh - narrated it from Hammad, from Thumamah, from Anas; while Waki' and Abu Umar al-Hawdi opposed them, narrating it from Hammad, from Thumamah as mursal, and that is correct."
"1698","Another, 1827 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn As'ad al-Harawi informed us there that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Janzarudhi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Marzuq al-Bahili narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his uncle Thumamah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who sees is not like the one who is told."
"1699","1828 - Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us in writing that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Thumamah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Report is not like eyewitness. Al-Tabarani said: Muhammad ibn Marzuq is alone in it."
"1700","Another, 1829 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Hunayn: Cut them down completely."
"1701","Another, 1830 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Husayn informed them: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Thumamah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a donkey branded on its face and said: May Allah curse whoever did this. Thus Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated it from Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj."
"1702","Another, 1831 - Zahir informed us that al-Husayn informed them: Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not remove his sandals in prayer except once; he removed them and the people removed theirs, so he said: Why did you remove them? They said: You removed yours, so we removed ours. He said: Jibril (peace be upon him) told me there was filth on them. And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated it from Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj like the narration of Abu Ya'la."
"1703","Another, 1832 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Mas'ud - he is al-Maqdisi - narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed an aqiqah for himself after he was sent as a Prophet."
"1704","1833 - Abu al-Haytham Shadhrah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ala' al-Madini al-Khayyat informed us in the city of Isfahan that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baghban informed them, recited to him: Abu Amr Abd al-Wahhab ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah informed us, Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yusuf ibn Yawah informed us, recited to him: Abu Amr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Hakim al-Madini narrated to us, dictating: Abu Hatim - he is Muhammad ibn Idris al-Razi - narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna ibn Anas al-Ansari narrated to us, Thumamah ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed an aqiqah for himself after prophethood came to him. And Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna said [...]."
"1705","Another, 1834 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Azrah ibn Thabit, from Thumamah, from Anas, who said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years; never did he send me on an errand that was not accomplished except that he said: If it had been decreed, it would have been - or: if it had been ordained, it would have been. As for the mention of the hadith, it has been mentioned in the Sahih."
"1706","Another, 1835 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ma'ali ibn Shaddaqiniyya informed us, recited to him while I was listening on the western side of Baghdad - it was said to him: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed you, recited to him while you were listening, and he acknowledged it - Abu al-Qasim Umar ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim al-Khaffaf informed us, Abu al-Fadl Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri informed us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Attab Sahl ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas narrated to me, saying: We were with Anas ibn Malik when a fly fell into a vessel, so Anas pushed it with his finger and dipped it in the water three times, saying: In the name of Allah. And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them to do that, saying: One of its wings carries disease and in the other is cure. Something like it is reported in al-Bukhari from Abu Hurayrah."
"1707","Another, 1836 - Abu al-Ma'ali Muhammad ibn Nasir ibn Sulayman ibn Nasir al-Ansari informed us in Nishapur that Abu Sa'id Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Kirmani informed them, recited to him: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Khalaf al-Shirazi narrated to us, the judge Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Ali al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Hafiz narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar ibn Hammad al-Azdi narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Hammad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna al-Ansari, from his uncle Thumamah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds a man's prayer alone in his house by twenty-seven degrees. When one of you prays in the mosque, let him make a share of his prayer in his house, for Allah, exalted, will place good in his house through his prayer; and Satan does not enter a house in which the Qur'an is recited."
"1708","Juthah ibn Ubayd al-Dayli from Anas. 1837 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim al-Khabbaz informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri' narrated to us, Ayyash ibn Uqbah al-Hadrami narrated to us, saying: I heard Juthah ibn Ubayd al-Dayali narrating from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Men will recite the Qur'an and it will not pass beyond their throats; they will pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game. Something of this is reported in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri regarding the description of the Khawarij; and Allah knows best."
"1709","Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah al-Tamimi from Anas. 1838 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja' al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Ishaq informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us, Yazid narrated to us, Rib'i ibn al-Jarud informed us - (H). 1839 - And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Rib'i ibn al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah informed us, saying: Amr ibn Abi al-Hajjaj narrated to me, from al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to pray voluntarily upon his mount, he would face the qiblah, say the takbir for prayer, then leave his mount free and pray wherever it turned with him. The wording is one. And Ibn Mani' said: from Anas, who said: he was. Musaddad narrated it from Rib'i."
"1710","1840 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Asbahani informed us there that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad ibn Musarhad narrated to us, Rib'i ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Jarud narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled and wanted to pray voluntarily upon the mount, he would face the qiblah with his she-camel, say the takbir, then pray wherever the she-camel turned with him. Abu Dawud al-Sijistani transmitted it in his Sunan from Musaddad. And Yahya ibn Yahya narrated it from Rib'i."
"1711","1841 - Zaynab bint Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Sha'ri informed us in Nishapur that Isma'il ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Bakr al-Qari' informed them: Abd al-Ghafir ibn Muhammad al-Farisi informed us, Bishr ibn Muhammad al-Isfarayini informed us, Dawud ibn al-Husayn al-Bayhaqi informed us, Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Rib'i ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Jarud informed us, from Amr ibn Abi al-Hajjaj, al-Jarud ibn Abi Sabrah narrated to me, saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled and wanted to pray voluntarily, he would face the qiblah with his she-camel, say the takbir, then pray wherever the she-camel turned. And Ali ibn al-Madini narrated it from Rib'i ibn Abd Allah, saying: Amr ibn Abi al-Hajjaj narrated to me, saying: al-Jarud narrated to me, saying: Anas narrated to me, similarly."
"1712","Ja'far ibn Ma'bad al-Himyari from Anas. 1842 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali, known as Ibn al-Ma'tush, informed us, with my recitation to him in Baghdad - I said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you, and he acknowledged it: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Ma'bad - the nephew of Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari - narrated to us, saying: I went with Humayd to Anas, and he said: When the people pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or: when we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he would dictate to us, or say to us: upon what you are able. Affan narrated it from Shu'bah."
"1713","1843 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Ma'bad informed me, saying: I went to Anas ibn Malik, I and Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman. He said: I heard Anas saying: When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would dictate to us: it is upon what you are able. And Bishr ibn Umar narrated it from Shu'bah."
"1714","1844 - Umar ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Yahya ibn Ali ibn al-Tarrah informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Naqur informed us, Abu Tahir al-Mukhallis informed us - it was said to him: Muhammad ibn Harun al-Hadrami narrated to you: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Ma'bad, from Anas, who said: When we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hear and obey, he said: Upon what you are able. And Attab, the freedman of Hurmuz, narrated something like it from Anas. Something like it is reported in the Sahih from Jarir ibn Abd Allah."
"1715","Al-Hajjaj ibn Hassan from Anas ibn Malik. 1845 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Hassan narrated to us, saying: We were with Anas ibn Malik, and he called for a vessel with three iron bands and an iron ring, taken out of a black cover, smaller than a quarter (sa') and larger than half a quarter. Anas ibn Malik ordered, and water was put in it for us; we were brought it and drank, poured upon our heads and faces, and invoked blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1716","Al-Hasan ibn Yasar al-Basri from Anas ibn Malik. 1846 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, then mounted his riding camel, and when he ascended the hill of al-Bayda' he entered ihram. Abu Dawud transmitted it from Ahmad ibn Hanbal. And al-Nasa'i transmitted it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, from Ash'ath. And from Ahmad ibn al-Azhar, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari, from Ash'ath similarly. Something like it is reported from Jabir ibn Abd Allah in Muslim in his long hadith."
"1717","Another, 1847 - Abu al-Majd al-Fadl ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim ibn Sulayman ibn al-Baniyasiyy informed us, recited while we were listening in Damascus - it was said to him: Muhammad and Ali, the two sons of al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Mawazini, informed you: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yahya ibn Sulwan al-Mazini informed us, Abu al-Qasim al-Fadl ibn Ja'far al-Tamimi the muezzin informed us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us at Hims, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Isa al-Khazzaz narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord and wards off an evil death. Al-Tirmidhi transmitted it from Uqbah ibn Mukram and said: A hasan gharib hadith from this angle. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it in his book from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn al-Fadl al-Kala'i al-Himsi and al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Qattan al-Raqqi, saying: two precise, trustworthy shaykhs, from Uqbah ibn Mukram. So we have a coincidence with the shaykh of al-Tirmidhi and the shaykh of Ibn Hibban, except that in the book of Ibn Hibban he says: Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, while with us it is al-Fudayl; and Allah knows best what is correct. And Ibn Adi spoke about Abd Allah al-Khazzaz."
"1718","1848 - Abu Hamid Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hamid ibn Uqbah al-Harbi informed us there that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Fath informed us, Abu al-Fath Nasr ibn Ghalib al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to us, saying: Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Isa narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Charity extinguishes the anger of the Lord and wards off an evil death."
"1719","Another, 1849 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out, wanting the mosque, leaning upon Usamah ibn Zayd, wearing a Qitri garment wrapped around him, and led them in prayer."
"1720","1850 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them: Abu Ali Ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out leaning upon Usamah ibn Zayd, wrapped in a Qitri garment, and led them in prayer - or he said: covered with it, and led them in prayer. And Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad, from Hammad as well. And al-Tirmidhi transmitted it in al-Shama'il from Abd ibn Humayd, from Muhammad ibn al-Fadl, from Hammad ibn Salamah."
"1721","Another, 1851 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning Anas ibn Malik - who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with al-Hasan sitting upon his thigh, saying: I hope that this son of mine will be a leader, through whom Allah will reconcile two parties of the Muslims. Al-Nasa'i transmitted it in al-Yawm wa al-Laylah from Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from one of his companions - meaning Anas. And in al-Manaqib from Isma'il ibn Mas'ud, from Khalid, more complete than the first. And al-Ansari narrated it from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah. And al-Bukhari narrated it from the hadith of Isra'il, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah."
"1722","1852 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi informed us in Damascus that Abu al-Majd Ma'ali ibn Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Tha'labi informed them: Abu al-Faraj Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini informed us, saying: Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Munir al-Khallal informed us, saying: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh al-Naysaburi informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ali ibn Sinan ibn Bahr al-Nasa'i informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la informed us, Khalid narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning Anas - who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching with al-Hasan upon his thigh, saying: I hope that this son of mine will be a leader, and I hope that Allah will reconcile through him two parties of my community. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Awf and Dawud sent it as mursal."
"1723","Another, 1853 - The Sharif Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Sami' ibn Muhammad al-Hashimi informed us in Baghdad that Hibat Allah ibn Ahmad al-Hariri informed them: Ibrahim ibn Umar al-Barmaki informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Ja'far informed us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi informed us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us when we were all young men then, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is marriage; whoever cannot, fasting is upon him, for it is a suppressant for him. And Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated it from Thabit, from Anas. And it has already preceded in his biography."
"1724","1854 - Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja' ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid, known as Tiflaji, informed us in his book that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musa - he is Ibn Harun - narrated to us, Ishaq narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid informed us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us when we were all young men, and said: Upon you is marriage; whoever cannot, fasting is upon him, for it is a suppressant for him. He said: None narrated it from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from Anas except Baqiyyah. Al-Daraqutni said: Abu Shihab al-Hannat opposed him, narrating it from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from one of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and that is correct. And it has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud."
"1725","Another, 1855 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri' informed us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Maymun ibn Najih Abu al-Hasan al-Naji narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Anas, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I desire jihad but cannot undertake it? He said: Is anyone of your parents left? He said: My mother. He said: Then exert yourself for Allah in dutifulness to her; when you do that, you are a pilgrim, an umrah-performer, and a warrior. When your mother is pleased with you, fear Allah and honor her. Maymun ibn Najih: Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him, saying: Muslim ibn Ibrahim and Abu Asim narrate from him, and he did not mention any criticism of him."
"1726","1856 - Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Maymun ibn Najih narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I desire ... [truncated: I desire jihad but cannot undertake it]."
"1727","1857 - Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us in his book that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Hashim - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Maymun ibn Najih Abu al-Hasan narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I desire jihad but cannot undertake it? He said: Is anyone of your parents left? He said: My mother. He said: Then present your excuse to Allah in dutifulness to her; when you do that, you are a pilgrim, an umrah-performer, and a warrior. When your mother is pleased with you, fear Allah in dutifulness to her; the wording is one ... present your excuse in dutifulness to her, and at its end: and honor her."
"1728","Another, 1858 - The Imam, the Hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Silafi informed us by ijazah, and the Imam Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mahmudi informed us from him, that Abu Muti' Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Zakariyya al-Misri informed them - as recited to him - Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Amr ibn Mahdi al-Hafiz narrated to us, dictating: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ishaq the judge narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever aids his brother in his absence, Allah will aid him in this world and the Hereafter. Al-Daraqutni said: Yunus ibn Ubayd opposed him, narrating it from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn; and Allah knows best."
"1729","1859 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah and Abu Dharr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Salhaniyy both said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Hayyan informed us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever aids his brother in his absence, Allah, mighty and majestic, will aid him in this world and the Hereafter."
"1730","1860 - My mother Umm Ahmad Ruqayyah bint Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah, may Allah have mercy on her, informed us that Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Salman informed them in his book: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us, Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran and Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Allaf informed us, saying: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i informed us, Abu Yahya al-Naqid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever aids his brother in his absence, Allah will aid him in this world and the Hereafter."
"1731","Another, 1861 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari, who said: I heard al-Hasan saying: Anas ibn Malik informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to preach on Friday leaning his back against a wooden post. When the people grew numerous, he said: Build for me a pulpit. So they built for him a pulpit of only two steps. When he moved from the wood to the pulpit, the wood moaned. Anas said: I heard the wood - by Allah - moaning like the moaning of a bereaved she-camel, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended from the pulpit to it and embraced it, and it calmed. Al-Hasan said: O servants of Allah, the Muslims - the wood moans out of longing for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), missing his place with it; are not the men who hope to meet him more deserving of longing for him? Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ibrahim except Habban; Yahya ibn Muhammad is alone in it. I say: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated it from al-Hasan. And it has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Umar and Jabir ibn Abd Allah."
"1732","Another, 1862 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim al-Saydalani informed us, recited to him in Isfahan, that Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, saying: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani al-Basri narrated to us. 1863 - And Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us by ijazah that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, aids this religion with people who have no share (in the Hereafter). Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad except Hammad ibn Zayd; Hudbah is alone in it. I say: Humayd narrated it from Anas. Al-Daraqutni said: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated it from al-Hasan, from Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal. Hammad ibn Salamah said so; perhaps al-Hasan took it from both; and Allah knows best. I say: It has been narrated from Adam ibn Abi Iyas, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Humayd al-Tawil, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1733","Another, 1864 - Ahmad ibn Hamzah al-Sulami informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them by ijazah: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Hafiz al-Wasiti narrated to us, Nuh ibn Muhammad al-Ubulli narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Of my honor with my Lord, mighty and majestic, is that I was born circumcised, and no one saw my private parts. And al-Tabarani narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Faraj, from Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Fazari al-Massisi, from Hushaym, with its chain, except that Sufyan has been criticized."
"1734","The twentieth part of al-Ahadith al-Mukhtarah, being the fifth part of the hadith of Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him. In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful; there is no power nor strength except with Allah, the Most High, the Most Great. My Lord, make easy and aid. Remainder of the hadith of al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan from Anas. 1865 - Abu Ghalib Mahfuz ibn Ahmad Abi al-Faraj al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Dharr informed them: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Musa - meaning Ibn Isma'il - narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man works for a period of his life the deed which, had he died upon it, he would have entered Paradise; then before his death he changes and works the deed of the people of Hellfire, dies, and enters Hell. And a man works for a period of his life the deed which, had he died upon it, he would have entered Hell; then before his death he changes and works the deed of the people of Paradise, dies, and enters Paradise. Thus Musa ibn Isma'il narrated it from Hammad. And Yazid ibn Harun, Affan ibn Muslim, and Ibrahim al-Sami narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Humayd, from Anas, without mentioning al-Hasan. Likewise Wuhayb ibn Khalid ibn Ajlan al-Basri and Khalid ibn Abd Allah al-Tahhan al-Wasiti narrated it from Humayd, from Anas. And Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated it from Humayd, from Anas as mawquf, saying: Humayd once raised it, then refrained from it. And it has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Mas'ud and Sahl ibn Sa'd."
"1735","Another, 1866 - Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Haddad informed us in Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him, that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid informed us by his word, Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated to us, Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, al-Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Abd Allah al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: I saw al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, may Allah have mercy on him, perform ablution for Zuhr prayer, then go out, and some people of Khurasan met him and said: O Abu Sa'id, ablution is unclear to us and we would like you to guide us. He said: I have performed ablution for Zuhr, but I shall repeat my ablution. He dismounted from his animal and called a slave-girl of his called Malayhah, saying: O girl, bring that water-jar. She brought a mug and he poured into a brass basin. He washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water three times, washed his face three times, washed his forearms three times up to the elbows, then wiped his head once, wiped his ears, and ran his fingers through his beard. Then he said: Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me that this is the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Abu Arubah al-Harrani narrated it from Ishaq ibn Zayd and Sulayman ibn Sayf - both - from Muhammad ibn Sulayman, from Ayyub ibn Abd Allah al-Basri, saying: I witnessed al-Hasan, and a group from Khurasan came."
"1736","1867 - My maternal uncle, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad informed them: my cousin Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Bishran informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Daraqutni narrated to us, Abu Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim, the Sabori-merchant, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh, Muhammad ibn Ali al-Warraq, and Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Hunayn narrated to us - the wording is Ibn Zanjawayh's - saying: Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Abd Allah Abu Khalid al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: I saw al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan call for ablution water; a mug of water was brought and poured into a basin. He washed his hands three times, rinsed ... then he mentioned similarly, and in it: and he washed his feet up to the ankles."
"1737","Another, 1868 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad al-Isma'ili and Abu Nasr Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Musa both said: Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Harb informed us, Abu Hatim Makki ibn Abdan ibn Bakr ibn Muslim informed us, Muhammad ibn Umar - he is al-Darabjirdi - narrated to us, al-Nadr - he is Ibn Shumayl - informed us, al-Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions came calling out talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to exit ihram, and it was as if they were awed by that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Exit ihram - had I not had the sacrificial animal with me, I would have exited ihram. So they exited ihram until they exited regarding women."
"1738","1869 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us there that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions arrived in Makkah having called out talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah. After they circumambulated the House and ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to make it an Umrah, and it was as if the people were awed by that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I not driven the sacrificial animal, I would have exited ihram. So the people exited ihram and performed tamattu'. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Jabir ibn Abd Allah."
"1739","Another, 1870 - It was recited to Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi while we were listening in Damascus - Abu al-Majd Ma'ali ibn Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Tha'labi informed you, recited to him: Abu al-Faraj Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini informed us, Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Munir al-Khallal informed us, recited to him: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh al-Naysaburi informed us, recited to him, saying: Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ali ibn Sinan ibn Bahr al-Nasa'i informed us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad informed us, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam al-Basri, who said: I used to share a camel-litter with al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, and he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever invokes one blessing upon me, Allah invokes ten blessings upon him and removes ten sins from him. More than one narrated it from Yunus without mentioning al-Hasan in the chain. And it has already preceded in the narration of Burayd."
"1740","Another, 1871 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad informed us at Herat that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad al-Darimi informed them, recited to him: Abu Abd Allah ibn Abi Mas'ud Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Farisi informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Darrab informed us, Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Hamid ibn Ma'mar ibn Imran ibn Hayyan al-Sami narrated to us, Abu Umar Muhammad ibn Marwan ibn Umar ibn Marwan ibn Anbasah ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn al-As ibn Umayyah narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath and Imran ibn Hudayr, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying over funeral biers between the graves."
"1741","1872 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi in Herat informed us: Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Bahhathi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us: Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban ibn Ahmad al-Busti informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa Abdan informed us: Sahl ibn Uthman al-Askari and Abu Musa al-Zamin narrated: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated: from Ash'ath: from al-Hasan: from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying between graves. Abu Hatim narrated it thus in his book. Al-Daraqutni said: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated it from Ash'ath from al-Hasan as mursal, and the mursal is more correct."
"1742","Another 1873 - It was read to Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi in Damascus while we listened: the jurist Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fath al-Sulami informed you, read to him and he acknowledged it: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hasan ibn Jahdam al-Hamdani informed us, read to him in his house in Mecca, may Allah protect it: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Hatim al-Bazzaz informed us: Ibrahim ibn Sulayman al-Taymi narrated: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated: Abu al-Ashhab al-Utaridi narrated: from al-Hasan: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Praise be to Allah for Islam, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are indeed praising Allah for a great blessing. Abu al-Ashhab's name is Ja'far ibn Hayyan."
"1743","1874 - Abu al-Yaman Zayd ibn al-Hasan ibn Zayd al-Kindi the grammarian in Damascus informed us: Hibatullah ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Hariri informed them: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Fath known as Ibn al-Ushari informed us: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Isma'il known as Ibn Sam'un the preacher narrated: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad al-Sayrafi narrated: Ibrahim ibn Sulayman al-Taymi al-Nahami narrated: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated: Abu al-Ashhab informed us: from al-Hasan: from Anas, he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Praise be to Allah for Islam, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are indeed praising Allah, mighty and majestic, for a great blessing."
"1744","1875 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil ibn al-Husayn al-Khaffaf in Baghdad informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khayyat informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur informed us, he said: Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn Ali ibn Isa ibn al-Jarrah dictated: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Isma'il al-Ubulli narrated: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Harun narrated: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated: Abu al-Ashhab al-Utaridi narrated: from al-Hasan: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Praise be to Allah for Islam, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are indeed praising Allah for a great blessing."
"1745","Another 1876 - Abu Ali Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Khattab ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib al-Harbi there informed us: Abu Mansur Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muslimah informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya narrated: Sawwar ibn Abdullah al-Anbari the judge narrated: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh al-Anbari narrated: from al-Ash'ath, who is Ibn Abd al-Malik al-Humrani: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My Basin is from such-and-such to such-and-such; in it are vessels as many as the stars of the sky, sweeter than honey, colder than snow, and whiter than milk; whoever drinks from it will never thirst again, and whoever does not drink from it will never be quenched. In it are wordings not in al-Bukhari and Muslim, from his saying: sweeter than honey, to the end."
"1746","Another 1877 - Abu al-Qasim Zinki ibn Mahmud ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Khayyat in Marw informed us: al-Junayd ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Qayini informed them: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Umayri informed us, read to him: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Bashani informed us. And Abu Abdullah al-Usmi, who is Muhammad ibn al-Abbas ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad, narrated: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Arzunani, the trustworthy and reliable, narrated: Abdullah ibn Wuhayb narrated: Ibn Abi al-Sari narrated: al-Mu'tamir narrated: from his father: from al-Hasan: from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim quietly, and Abu Bakr and Umar did so."
"1747","1878 - Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh in Isfahan informed us of it: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated: from his father: from al-Hasan: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim quietly, and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them."
"1748","Another 1879 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us, read to him: Yahya ibn Ali al-Tarrah informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us, read to him: it was said to him: Abu Hamid Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to you, read to him: Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated: Hushaym narrated: from Awf: from al-Hasan: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us."
"1749","1880 - Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Isfahani informed us by ijazah: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nu'aym informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated: Ishaq ibn Shahin al-Wasiti narrated: Hushaym narrated: from Awf: from al-Hasan: from Anas ibn Malik: from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Attend to the Qur'an, for by the One in whose Hand is my soul, it escapes from the hearts of men more intensely than hobbled camels escape to their resting places. The wording is Ahmad ibn Zuhayr's. And al-Hadrami said: it escapes more intensely than hobbled camels to their homelands, and the rest is the same. Al-Tabarani said: none narrated this hadith from Awf except Hushaym; Ishaq ibn Shahin is alone in it. And al-Daraqutni said: Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated it from Hushaym from al-Hasan from Anas, while others narrate it from Hushaym from Awf from al-Hasan as mursal, and that is the preserved version. And this hadith has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Mas'ud and Ibn Umar."
"1750","Hafs ibn Ubaydullah ibn Anas from his grandfather 1881 - The hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud ibn al-Mubarak Ibn al-Akhdar in Baghdad informed us: Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Tarrah informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us: Abu al-Qasim Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated: Mus'ab ibn Abdullah ibn Mus'ab ibn Thabit ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam narrated: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to me: from Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi: from Hafs ibn Abdullah, and the correct is Ubaydullah, ibn Anas: from his grandfather Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a disheveled one in two worn garments, dusty, Usamah said: I do not know it except that he said: turned away from doors, if he were to swear by Allah the Exalted, He would fulfill it. And Thabit narrated something similar from Anas."
"1751","1882 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani in Isfahan informed us: Mahmud ibn Isma'il informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Ibn Kasib narrated: Ibn Abi Hazim narrated: from Usamah ibn Zayd: from Hafs ibn Ubaydullah ibn Anas: from his grandfather Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a disheveled dusty one in two worn garments, turned away from people's doors, he said: if he were to swear by Allah, He would fulfill his oath. And Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from Ja'far ibn Awn from Usamah. And Abd ibn Humayd and Abbas al-Duri narrated it from Ja'far ibn Awn."
"1752","Another 1883 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi, blind, may Allah have mercy on him, in Isfahan informed us: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Ibn Numayr narrated: Rawh narrated: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated: from Hafs ibn Ubaydullah: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pray at sunrise nor at sunset, for it rises between the two horns of Satan, and pray between that as much as you wish. And Muslim brought, through Usamah from Hafs, a hadith other than these two."
"1753","Hafs ibn Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah from Anas 1884 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Harawi there informed us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn al-Fudayl al-Fudayli informed them: Abu Mudar Muhallim ibn Isma'il al-Dabbi informed us: Abu Sa'id al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi informed us: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi al-Sarraj informed us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated: Khalaf, who is Ibn Khalifah, narrated: from Hafs, Anas's nephew: from Anas, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the circle, and a man was standing praying, meaning when he bowed and prostrated and made the tashahhud, he supplicated and said in his supplication: O Allah, I ask You, as all praise belongs to You, there is no god but You, the Most Compassionate, the Bestower, Originator of the heavens and the earth, O Possessor of majesty and honor, O Living, O Sustainer, I ask You. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Do you know with what he supplicated? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, he has supplicated with His greatest name, by which if He is called upon He answers, and if He is asked by it He gives."
"1754","1885 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi there informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated: my father narrated: Husayn ibn Muhammad and Affan narrated, they said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated: Hafs ibn Umar narrated: from Anas, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the circle, and a man was standing praying; when he bowed and prostrated, he sat and made the tashahhud, then supplicated and said: O Allah, I ask You, as all praise belongs to You, there is no god but You, the Bestower, O Originator of the heavens and the earth, O Possessor of majesty and honor, O Living, O Sustainer, I ask You. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know with what he supplicated? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, he has supplicated Allah with His greatest name, by which if He is called upon He answers, and if He is asked by it He gives. Abu Dawud brought it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubaydullah al-Halabi. And al-Nasa'i brought it from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id. And Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili narrated it in his Musnad from Dawud ibn Rushayd, all of them from Khalaf ibn Khalifah. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban al-Busti brought it in his book from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj."
"1755","Another 1886 - al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi in Baghdad informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated: my father narrated: Husayn, who is Ibn Muhammad, narrated: Khalaf narrated: from Hafs ibn Umar: from Anas, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the circle when a man came and greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the people. The man said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. When the man sat, he said: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed praise, as He loves to be praised and as befits Him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: How did you say it? He repeated to him as he had said. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, ten angels raced for it, each of them keen to record it, but they did not know how to write it until they raised it to the Possessor of might, and He said: Write it as My servant said it. And he also narrated it from Affan from Khalaf."
"1756","1887 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi in Herat informed us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il informed them: Muhallim ibn Isma'il al-Dabbi informed us: al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi informed us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated: Khalaf narrated: from Hafs, Anas's nephew: from Anas, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the circle when a man came to him and greeted the Prophet and the people, saying: Peace be upon you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied to him: And upon you peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. When the man sat, he said: I praise Allah with much, good, blessed praise, as our Lord loves and is pleased with. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: How did you say it? He repeated to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as he had said. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, ten angels raced with it, each of them keen to record it, but they did not know how to write it until they raised it to the Possessor of might, and He said: Write it as My servant said it. Al-Nasa'i brought it similarly from Qutaybah. And Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it in his book from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi similarly. And Muslim narrated in his Sahih from the narration of Qatadah and Thabit and Humayd from Anas that a man came and entered the row while out of breath, and said: Praise be to Allah, good, blessed praise, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Which of you spoke the words? The people fell silent. And what concerns us: I saw twelve angels racing for it, which of them would raise it. And this hadith is other than the one we wrote, similar to it."
"1757","Another 1888 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani in Isfahan informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us: Isma'il ibn Abdullah narrated: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated: from Hafs, Anas's nephew: from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (the hadith)."
"1758","1889 - al-Sharif Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Sami' ibn Muhammad al-Hashimi in Baghdad informed us: Hibatullah ibn Ahmad al-Hariri informed them: Ibrahim ibn Umar al-Barmaki informed us: Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn Ja'far al-Zabibi informed us: Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Mustafad informed us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated: from Anas's nephew, who is Hafs: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command marriage and forbid celibacy with a severe prohibition, saying: Marry the loving and fertile, for I will boast of your numbers before the nations. Their wording is one."
"1759","1890 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad in Herat informed us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Fudayli informed them: Muhallim ibn Isma'il informed us: al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj narrated: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated: Khalaf narrated: from Hafs: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command marriage and forbid celibacy with a severe prohibition, saying: Marry the loving and fertile, for I will boast before the Prophets on the Day of Resurrection. Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated it like this narration from Husayn ibn Muhammad and Affan ibn Muslim from Khalaf ibn Khalifah, and with him it is Hafs ibn Umar. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it in his book from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi. And Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Tawil narrated it from Khalaf ibn Khalifah."
"1760","Another 1891 - Abu Rawh ibn Muhammad al-Harawi there informed us: Muhammad al-Fudayli informed them: Muhallim al-Dabbi informed us: al-Khalil ibn Ahmad informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj informed us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated: Khalaf narrated: from Hafs, Anas's nephew: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with these supplications: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, a heart that does not humble itself, a supplication that is not heard, and a soul that is not satisfied. He said: then he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from these four."
"1761","1892 - Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali ibn al-Ma'tush al-Harimi in Baghdad informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated: Hafs ibn Umar narrated: from Anas, he said: among the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, a heart that does not humble itself, a soul that is not satisfied, and a supplication that is not heard; O Allah, I seek refuge in You from these four. Al-Nasa'i brought it from Qutaybah. And Qatadah narrated it from Anas, and it will come, Allah the Exalted willing, in Qatadah's narration. And this hadith has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Zayd ibn Arqam."
"1762","Another 1893 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi there informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated: Khalaf narrated: from Hafs: from Anas, he said: we set out to Syria to Abd al-Malik, we being forty men of the Ansar, so that he would assign stipends for us; when he returned, and we were at Fajj al-Naqah, he led us in Zuhr as two rak'ahs, then gave salam and entered his tent, and the people stood adding two more rak'ahs to his two. He said: May Allah disgrace those faces; by Allah, they neither hit the Sunnah nor accepted the concession. I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There are people who go deep in religion and pass through it as the arrow passes through the target."
"1763","1894 - Abu Rawh al-Harawi informed us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il informed them: Muhallim al-Dabbi informed us: al-Khalil al-Sijzi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj informed us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated: Khalaf narrated: from Hafs: from Anas, he said: I was taken with forty men of the Ansar until we were brought to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, and he assigned stipends for us; when he returned, we returned, until when we were at Fajj al-Naqah, he led us in Zuhr as two rak'ahs and gave salam, and entered his tent. The people stood adding two other rak'ahs to his two. He looked at them and said to his son Abu Bakr: What are these people doing? He said: they are adding two other rak'ahs to our two. He said: May Allah disgrace those faces; they neither accepted the concession nor hit the Sunnah. I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There are a people who go deep in religion and pass through religion as the arrow passes through the target."
"1764","Another 1895 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi there informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated: my father narrated: Husayn narrated: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated: from Hafs: from his uncle Anas ibn Malik, he said: there was a household of the Ansar who had a camel on which they drew water, but the camel became unruly and denied them its back. The Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We had a camel on which we drew water, but it became unruly and denied us its back, and the crops and palms have grown thirsty. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Arise. They arose, and he entered the garden with the camel in a corner. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked toward it. The Ansar said: O Prophet of Allah, it has become like a rabid dog, and we fear its attack for you. He said: There is no harm to me from it. When the camel looked at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it came toward him until it fell prostrate before him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it by its forelock in its most docile state ever, until he put it to work. His Companions said to him: O Prophet of Allah, this is a beast that does not reason, prostrating to you, while we reason, so we are more entitled to prostrate to you? He said: It is not right for a human to prostrate to a human; had it been right for a human to prostrate to a human, I would have commanded the wife to prostrate to her husband because of the greatness of his right over her. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, if from his foot to the crown of his head there were a wound bursting with pus and matter, then she faced it licking it, she would not have fulfilled his due."
"1765","Another 1896 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani in Isfahan informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Muqri al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Isfahani informed us: Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us: Isma'il ibn Abdullah Samuwayh narrated: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated: from Hafs, Anas's nephew: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Peace be upon you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten. Another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. He said: Twenty. Another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. He said: Thirty."
"1766","Another 1897 - It was read to Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani while I listened in Isfahan: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed you while you were present and listening, and he acknowledged it: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated: from Khalaf ibn Khalifah: from Hafs, Anas's nephew: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever in seven intestines. Al-Tabarani said: none narrated this hadith from Hafs except Khalaf."
"1767","1898 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani also informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Anbari in Baghdad informed us: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated: from Hafs ibn Ubaydullah: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained fasting one day; when evening came, he said: O Anas, bring the goat near me. He brought it near him. A Bedouin came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) milked and raised it to him, and he drank it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke the next morning fasting; when evening came, he said: O Anas, bring the goat near me. The Bedouin came and sat. I said: Woe to you, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained fasting yesterday and preferred you with the milk; if only you would stay away from him. He said: No, by Allah, I will not do so. He milked the sheep and handed it to him, and he drank it. On the third day he woke fasting; when evening came, he said: Bring me the goat. I brought it, and the Bedouin came. When it was brought, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held the vessel in his hand and said: Say: In the name of Allah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the name, and the Bedouin drank until quenched, and a remainder remained, which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, and said: Until today he drank in the intestine of a disbeliever and was never quenched, and today he drinks in the intestine of a believer and is quenched. It is narrated in the Sahih: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines, from the hadith of Ibn Umar, Abu Musa, Jabir ibn Abdullah, and Abu Hurayrah."
"1768","Humayd al-Tawil from Anas ibn Malik 1899 - Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Umari in Baghdad informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ghaylan informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i narrated: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sulayman narrated: Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated: from Khalid, meaning Ibn Abdullah: from Humayd: from Anas: that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a mount, and he said: We shall mount you on the offspring of a she-camel? He said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall I do with the offspring of a she-camel? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And do camels give birth to any but she-camels."
"1769","1900 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi in Isfahan informed us: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Wahb, who is Ibn Baqiyyah, narrated: Khalid narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Give me a mount. He said: We shall mount you on the offspring of a she-camel. He said: What shall I do with the offspring of a she-camel? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And do camels give birth to any but she-camels."
"1770","1901 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali in Baghdad informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him for a mount, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall mount you on the offspring of a she-camel. He said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall I do with the offspring of a she-camel? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And do camels give birth to any but she-camels. Abu Dawud brought it from Wahb ibn Baqiyyah. And al-Tirmidhi brought it from Qutaybah, both from Khalid ibn Abdullah, and he said: a sound, strange hadith."
"1771","Another 1902 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi in Isfahan informed us: Abu al-Faraj Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated: Yazid narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us: from Humayd: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Strive against the polytheists with your hands, your wealth, and your tongues."
"1772","1903 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Saydalani in Isfahan informed us: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abu Ali al-Sawwaf informed us: Bishr ibn Musa al-Asadi narrated: Affan narrated: Hammad narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fight the polytheists with your tongues and your hands."
"1773","1904 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi in Isfahan informed us: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Zuhayr narrated: Affan narrated: Hammad narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Strive against the polytheists with your hands and your tongues."
"1774","1905 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi there informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated: my father narrated to me: Yazid narrated: Hammad informed us: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (the hadith). 1906 - And Imam Ahmad said: Hasan, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (the hadith). 1907 - And he said: Affan narrated: Hammad narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Strive against the polytheists with your wealth, yourselves, and your tongues. The wording of the hadith of Yazid and Affan. And in Hasan ibn Musa's narration: with your tongues, yourselves, your wealth, and your hands. And al-Darimi narrated it from Amr ibn Asim: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: Humayd informed us from Anas. And Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan from Musa from Hammad. And al-Nasa'i brought it from Harun ibn Abdullah and Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Ibrahim from Yazid ibn Harun, and from Amr ibn Ali from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, all from Hammad from Humayd. And Thabit al-Bunani narrated it from Anas."
"1775","Another 1908 - Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi, who came to us in Damascus, informed us, read to him while we listened: it was said to him: Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn al-Haytham informed you while you were present: Ubaydullah ibn al-Mu'tazz ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Ali ibn Hujr narrated: Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas, he said: the people of Medina in the pre-Islamic period had two days each year in which they played; when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina, he said: You had two days in which you played, and Allah has replaced them for you with better than them: the day of Fitr and the day of Sacrifice. Yazid ibn Harun and Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi also narrated it from Humayd."
"1776","1909 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi in Isfahan informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Abu al-Qasim Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Abu Bakr, who is Ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated: al-Thaqafi, who is Abd al-Wahhab, narrated: from Humayd (the hadith). 1910 - Abu Ya'la said: and Zuhayr narrated to us: Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, narrated, he said: Humayd informed us: from Anas: that the Ansar had two days in the pre-Islamic period in which they played; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has replaced for you two days better than them: Fitr and Adha. The wording is al-Thaqafi's. And Yazid said in his hadith, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while they had two days in which they played, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have come to you while you have two days in which you play, and Allah, mighty and majestic, has replaced for you two days better than them: the day of Fitr and the day of Sacrifice. And Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated it from Humayd."
"1777","1911 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi there informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated: Ibn Abi Adi narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while they had two days in which they played in the pre-Islamic period, and he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, has replaced for you better than them: Fitr and the day of Adha. And Hammad narrated it from Humayd, mentioning his hearing from Anas."
"1778","1912 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi in Baghdad informed us: Hibatullah ibn al-Husayn informed them: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated: Hammad narrated: Humayd informed us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina while they had two days in which they played. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What are these two days? They said: We used to play in them in the pre-Islamic period. He said: Allah has replaced for you better than them: the day of Fitr and the day of Sacrifice. And Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari from Humayd. And likewise Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated it from al-Ansari. And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Adani narrated it from Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah from Humayd. And Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj narrated it from Sawwar ibn Abdullah from al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman from Humayd from Anas. And Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated it in his Sunan from Musa ibn Isma'il from Hammad from Humayd. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ali ibn Hujr."
"1779","Another 1913 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi there informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated: my father narrated to me: Ali ibn Ishaq and al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated, they said: Abdullah, who is Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us: Humayd al-Tawil informed us: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; when they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), face our qiblah, eat our slaughtered meat, and pray our prayer, their blood and wealth become forbidden to us except by its right; they have what belongs to the Muslims, and upon them is what is upon them."
"1780","1914 - Abu al-Mu'ammar Baqa ibn Umar ibn Jund in Baghdad informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hasnun al-Narsi informed us: Abu al-Qasim Musa ibn Isa ibn Abdullah al-Sarraj informed us: Abdullah, who is Ibn Abi Dawud, narrated: Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Amili narrated: Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay' narrated: Humayd al-Tawil narrated: from Anas ibn Malik: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was commanded..."
"1781","1915 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi in Isfahan informed us: Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us: Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Sinan al-Hiri informed us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us: Hisham ibn Ammar al-Dimashqi narrated: Muhammad ibn Isa narrated: Humayd al-Tawil narrated: from Anas: from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; when they testify to it, pray our prayer, face our qiblah, and eat our slaughtered meat, their blood and wealth become forbidden to us except by its right. The wording is Hisham's. And Harun said: I was commanded to fight the polytheists until they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; when they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger... and the rest is the same, except that he said: have become forbidden."
"1782","1916 - Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad informed us by ijazah, and my maternal uncle the Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi informed us from him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Bishran informed us: Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad al-Daraqutni the hafiz narrated: Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi narrated: Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la narrated: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight the polytheists until they say: there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah; when they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, pray our prayer, face our qiblah, and eat our slaughtered meat, their wealth and blood become forbidden to us except by its right; they have what belongs to the Muslim, and upon them is what is upon the Muslim."
"1783","1917 - Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us by ijazah: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nu'aym informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Bakr ibn Sahl narrated: Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated: Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated: from Humayd al-Tawil: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: there is no god but Allah; when they say it, they protect from me their blood and wealth except by its right. It was said: And what is its right? He said: adultery after chastity, disbelief after Islam, or killing a soul, for which he is killed. Al-Bukhari narrated it, saying: And Ibn Abi Maryam said from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Humayd: Anas narrated to us. He said: And Ali ibn Abdullah said to me: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated: Humayd narrated: Maymun ibn Siyah asked Anas: What makes a servant's blood and wealth forbidden? He said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah... as mawquf. And al-Bukhari narrated something like this through Maymun ibn Siyah, but the testimony is not in it, so this has an addition over that, and Allah knows best. And Abu Dawud and al-Tirmidhi narrated it in their books from Sa'id ibn Ya'qub al-Talqani from Ibn al-Mubarak. And Abu Dawud brought it from Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri from Ibn Wahb from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Humayd. And al-Tirmidhi said: a good, sound, strange hadith from this angle. And al-Nasa'i brought it in his Sunan from Muhammad ibn Hatim ibn Nu'aym from Hibban from Ibn al-Mubarak, and from Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal from Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay' from Humayd. And Abu Hatim al-Razi said: none narrates this hadith with isnad except three persons: Ibn al-Mubarak, Yahya ibn Ayyub, and Ibn Sumay'. I say: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar has narrated it from Humayd similarly."
"1784","Another 1918 - Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari in Baghdad informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ghaylan informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shafi'i narrated: Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated: Humayd, meaning al-Tawil, narrated: from Anas, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating cooked food and fresh dates. Rawh's narrators from Jarir: Hibban ibn Hilal, Abu Usamah, and Wahb ibn Jarir."
"1785","1919 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili narrated: Abu Khaythamah narrated: Hibban ibn Hilal narrated: from Jarir ibn Hazim: from Humayd: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combining cooked food and fresh dates."
"1786","1920 - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Abi Bakr Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Salim al-Khurasani al-Dallal in Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: Abu Shakir Muhammad ibn Abi Tahir ibn Abi Nasr al-Mustawfi informed them: Abu Muhammad Rizqullah ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Tamimi informed us: Abu Umar Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi informed us: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Makhlad al-Attar informed us: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated: Abu Usamah narrated: from Jarir ibn Hazim: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to eat fresh dates with khirbiz, meaning melon, combining them."
"1787","1921 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush in Baghdad informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated: my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Humayd al-Tawil narrating from Anas, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combining fresh dates and khirbiz. Al-Tirmidhi brought it in the Shama'il from Ibrahim ibn Ya'qub. And al-Nasa'i narrated it in al-Walimah from Ishaq ibn Mansur, both from Wahb ibn Jarir similarly. And Judge Ahmad ibn Abi Asim al-Nabil narrated it in the Book of Foods from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami and Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, both from Muslim ibn Ibrahim from Jarir. And it is reported from Muhanna, Ahmad ibn Hanbal's companion, from him that he said: It is not sound; it is not known from Humayd's hadith nor from other than Humayd's hadith; it is known only through Abdullah ibn Ja'far. I say, and Allah knows best: Ahmad's narration of it in the Musnad weakens this statement, or his retraction of it by narrating it and leaving it in his book. And Abdullah ibn Ja'far's hadith is in the two Sahihs, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating cucumber with fresh dates."
"1788","Another 1922 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Isfahani informed us: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Rayyan al-Misri informed us: Ishaq informed us, he said: we read to Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri: from Humayd al-Tawil: from Anas, he said: in prayer, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked the Muhajirun and Ansar to be next to him. A group narrated it from Humayd, among them al-Thawri, and this is his narration, Yazid ibn Harun, Abdullah ibn Bakr, Khalid, al-Mu'tamir, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi, al-Abyad ibn al-Agharr al-Minqari, and Ibn Abi Adi."
"1789","1923 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi in Isfahan informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Yazid narrated: Humayd informed us (the hadith). 1924 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim al-Khabbaz informed us: Abu Bakr Ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: al-Thaqafi narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked the Muhajirun and Ansar to be next to him, so that they would learn from him. The wording is Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi's. And Yazid ibn Harun said in his hadith: that they be next to him in prayer, the Muhajirun and Ansar, so that they would learn from him."
"1790","1925 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi in Baghdad informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated: Mu'tamir narrated (the hadith). 1926 - And Imam Ahmad said: Yazid narrated: Humayd informed us: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked the Muhajirun and Ansar to be next to him in prayer. The wording is Mu'tamir's. And Yazid added: so that they would learn from him."
"1791","1927 - My maternal uncle the learned Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Salman informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Shadhan informed us, he said: it was read to Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i: Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Matar al-Warraq informed us, he said: Wahb, meaning Ibn Baqiyyah, informed us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us: from Humayd (the hadith). 1928 - Al-Shafi'i also said: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Abduwayh al-Khazzaz narrated: Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated: Humayd al-Tawil narrated: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked the Muhajirun and Ansar to be next to him so that they would memorize from him. The wording is al-Sahmi's. And Khalid said: and the Ansar in prayer so that they would learn from him. And Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abdullah ibn Bakr: Humayd narrated like al-Khazzaz's narration."
"1792","1929 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Sarraj in Egypt informed us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated: al-Abyad ibn al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah al-Minqari narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked the Muhajirun and Ansar to be next to him, so that they would learn from him and memorize from him. Al-Nasa'i brought it in al-Manaqib from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Khalid. And Ibn Majah brought it in prayer from Nasr ibn Ali from al-Thaqafi. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it in his book from Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Awn from Bakr ibn Khalaf from Ibn Abi Adi, all from Humayd from Anas. Muslim narrated in his Sahih from the hadith of Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let those of you with understanding and reason be next to me."
"1793","Another 1930 - Zahir ibn Ahmad in Isfahan informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated: Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Muhajirun came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we never saw any people more generous with much, nor better in sharing little, than the Ansar; we came to Medina and they shared with us the pleasant life; we fear they will take all the reward? He said: No, as long as you praise them and supplicate for them. Yazid ibn Harun, Abbad ibn al-Awwam, Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, Harun ibn Musa, and Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated it like Khalid's narration from Humayd."
"1794","1931 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn al-Fakhir in Isfahan informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Mu'allim informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated, he said: Humayd informed us: from Anas, he said: when the Muhajirun came to Medina, they stayed with the Ansar in their houses and said: O Messenger of Allah, we never saw any people we stayed with better in sharing little, nor more generous with much, than them; they shared with us the pleasant life and sufficed us the burden, and we feared they would take all the reward? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, as long as you supplicate to Allah for them and praise Him for them."
"1795","1932 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi in al-Harbiyyah informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yazid ibn Harun narrated: Humayd informed us: from Anas, he said: the Muhajirun said: O Messenger of Allah, we never saw any people we came to better in sharing little, nor better in generosity with much; they sufficed us the burden and shared with us the pleasant life, until we feared they would take all the reward? He said: No, as long as you praise them and supplicate to Allah for them."
"1796","1933 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas, he said: the Muhajirun said: O Messenger of Allah, we never saw any people we came to more generous with much, nor better in sharing little; they sufficed us the burden and shared with us the pleasant life; we feared they would take all the reward? He said: No, as long as you praise them and supplicate to Allah for them."
"1797","1934 - Hibatullah ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Muzaffar ibn al-Sibt in Baghdad informed us: his father informed them, he said: my father al-Muzaffar ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sibt informed us: Abu al-Qasim Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Saqati informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us: Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated: Arim narrated: Harun ibn Musa al-A'war narrated, he said: I came to Humayd al-Tawil and asked him about this hadith, and he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: when the Muhajirun came to Medina, they said: O Messenger of Allah, we never saw any people we stayed with better in sharing; they shared with us the pleasant life and sufficed us the burden, and we feared they would take all the reward. He said: No, as long as you supplicate for them and praise them. And Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari. And Hanbal ibn Ishaq narrated it from Hasan ibn al-Rabi' from Yazid ibn Zuray' both from Humayd. And al-Tirmidhi brought it from Husayn ibn al-Hasan from Ibn Abi Adi from Humayd, and said: a good, sound, strange hadith. And Thabit narrated it from Anas. Harun ibn Musa al-Nahwi the reciter: Abu Abdullah al-Basri; Yahya ibn Ma'in and Abu Zur'ah deemed him trustworthy, and Shu'bah said: he is among the best of Muslims."
"1798","Another 1935 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi, read to him, in al-Harbiyyah informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated: my father narrated to me: Ibn Abi Adi narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him. They said: And how does He employ him? He said: He grants him success to do a righteous deed before his death. Yazid ibn Harun, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi, and Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated it from Humayd like Ibn Abi Adi's narration."
"1799","1936 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Saydalani informed us: Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and how does He employ him? He said: He grants him success to do a righteous deed before his death."
"1800","1937 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Yazid narrated, he said: Humayd informed us: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and how does He employ him? He said: He grants him success to do a righteous deed, then takes his soul upon it."
